// Auto-generated for the Unit Board (Zone 2: Hot Words for the SAT)
window.HOT_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Brevity and Silence","themeZh":"簡潔與沉默","cards":[{"w":"concise","p":"adj.","d":"Giving much information clearly in few words.","c":"簡潔的；簡明的","s":"Because the journal limits abstracts to 150 words, the epidemiologist spent days revising her summary until it was concise enough to convey the study's design, sample size, and central finding without sacrificing any of the statistical detail that reviewers would need to evaluate it.","t":"由於該期刊將摘要限制在一百五十字以內，這位流行病學家花了好幾天修改她的摘要，直到它夠簡潔，能在不犧牲審查者評估時所需的任何統計細節之下，傳達研究設計、樣本數與核心發現。","as":"Unlike the verbose memos of his predecessors, the new director's concise reports were praised as judicious and incisive, allowing even skeptical board members to grasp the company's precarious finances within minutes of opening them.","at":"與前任主管冗長的備忘錄不同，新任主管簡潔的報告被讚譽為明智而一針見血，讓即使抱持懷疑態度的董事，也能在打開報告幾分鐘內就掌握公司岌岌可危的財務狀況。"},{"w":"reticent","p":"adj.","d":"Reluctant to reveal one's thoughts or feelings.","c":"沉默寡言的；有所保留的","s":"Although the retired diplomat had witnessed several of the most consequential negotiations of the Cold War, he remained reticent about them in interviews, politely declining to discuss specific conversations and insisting that confidentiality was a promise that did not expire when one left office.","t":"雖然這位退休外交官親眼見證了冷戰時期幾場最具影響力的談判，他在受訪時對這些事卻始終有所保留，客氣地拒絕談論具體的對話內容，並堅稱保密是一項承諾，不會因卸任而失效。","as":"The normally reticent physicist became surprisingly voluble when asked about her research, but she grew wary again once reporters began asking about the scandal surrounding her laboratory, offering only deliberately ambiguous replies.","at":"這位平時沉默寡言的物理學家被問到自己的研究時，變得出乎意料地健談；但當記者開始詢問她實驗室捲入的醜聞時，她又變得謹慎起來，只給出刻意模稜兩可的回答。"},{"w":"succinct","p":"adj.","d":"Expressed clearly and precisely in very few words.","c":"簡明扼要的；簡潔的","s":"The Supreme Court justice was admired for her succinct opinions; where colleagues filled forty pages with historical digressions, she could state the constitutional question, apply the relevant precedent, and announce the holding in fewer than ten carefully reasoned paragraphs.","t":"這位最高法院大法官以簡明扼要的判決意見書著稱；同僚動輒用四十頁篇幅穿插歷史題外話，她卻能在不到十段縝密推理的文字中，陳述憲法爭點、援引相關判例並宣布判決結果。","as":"Asked to explain the debacle, the chief engineer gave a succinct account that debunked several spurious rumors, pointing instead to a single overlooked discrepancy in the collapsed bridge's original load calculations.","at":"被要求解釋這場慘敗時，總工程師給出了一段簡明扼要的說明，揭穿了好幾則不實的謠言，並指出問題其實出在倒塌橋梁原始載重計算中一個被忽略的誤差。"},{"w":"laconic","p":"adj.","d":"Using very few words; expressing much briefly.","c":"言簡意賅的；惜字如金的","s":"When journalists pressed the famously laconic Vermont farmer to describe the devastating flood that had destroyed his barn and half his herd, he replied only, 'Bad year,' and returned to repairing the fence, leaving reporters to supply the drama themselves.","t":"當記者追問這位以惜字如金聞名的佛蒙特州農夫，請他描述那場摧毀他的穀倉和半數牲口的洪水時，他只回了一句「年頭不好」，便又回頭修補籬笆，讓記者們自行去渲染戲劇性的情節。","as":"The novelist's laconic dialogue, in which characters exchange only a few clipped phrases, conveys tension more effectively than the grandiloquent speeches of her contemporaries, whose verbose, ostentatious prose often obscures the emotions it intends to reveal.","at":"這位小說家筆下簡短扼要的對白，讓角色之間只交換寥寥數語，卻比她同時代作家那些浮誇的長篇演說更能有效傳達緊張感；那些作家冗長而賣弄的文筆，往往反而遮蔽了它想揭示的情感。"},{"w":"terse","p":"adj.","d":"Brief and abrupt, sometimes to the point of rudeness.","c":"簡短生硬的；扼要的","s":"After months of polite correspondence, the publisher's terse two-line email ('We will not be renewing your contract. Please return the advance.') signaled to the novelist that the relationship had soured beyond repair and that further negotiation would be pointless.","t":"在幾個月客氣的書信往來之後，出版商那封簡短生硬的兩行電子郵件（「我們不會與您續約，請退還預付金。」）讓這位小說家明白，雙方關係已惡化到無可挽回，再談下去也毫無意義。","as":"Irritated by the reporter's insolent questions, the normally affable senator gave a terse reply, then strode out of the crowded briefing room, leaving his aides to mollify the indignant press corps.","at":"被記者無禮的提問激怒後，這位平時和藹可親的參議員簡短生硬地回了一句，便大步走出擠滿人的簡報室，留下幕僚去安撫憤憤不平的記者團。"},{"w":"brevity","p":"n.","d":"The quality of being brief in speech or writing.","c":"簡潔；簡短","s":"Lincoln's Gettysburg Address, at roughly 270 words, owes much of its enduring power to its brevity; Edward Everett, who had spoken for two hours before him, later wrote that he wished he had come as close to the heart of the occasion in two hours as the president had in two minutes.","t":"林肯的蓋茲堡演說僅約兩百七十字，其歷久不衰的感染力很大程度上來自它的簡潔；在他之前演講了兩個小時的愛德華．艾佛瑞特後來寫道，他真希望自己花兩個小時所觸及的典禮核心，能像總統在兩分鐘內做到的那樣深刻。","as":"Critics praised the brevity of the eulogy, noting that its restrained, unpretentious language moved mourners far more deeply than the hackneyed platitudes and grandiloquent tributes that usually dominate such solemn occasions.","at":"評論者稱讚這篇悼詞的簡潔，指出其節制而樸實的語言，遠比這類莊嚴場合中常見的陳腐套話與浮誇頌詞更能深深打動弔唁者。"},{"w":"pithy","p":"adj.","d":"Brief but full of meaning and force.","c":"精闢的；言簡意賅的","s":"Benjamin Franklin's Poor Richard's Almanack popularized dozens of pithy sayings, such as 'Well done is better than well said,' whose compact phrasing made practical moral advice easy for colonial readers to remember, repeat, and pass on to their children.","t":"班傑明．富蘭克林的《窮理查年鑑》讓數十句精闢的格言廣為流傳，例如「做得好勝過說得好」；這些格言措辭精簡，使殖民地讀者容易記住、複誦，並傳給自己的孩子。","as":"Rather than offering banal platitudes, the economist summed up the heated debate over inflation with one pithy observation that was both erudite and accessible, and even her most cynical critics conceded its force.","at":"這位經濟學家沒有搬出平庸的陳腔濫調，而是用一句精闢的評論總結了這場關於通膨的激烈辯論；這句話既博學又淺顯易懂，連她最憤世嫉俗的批評者也承認其說服力。"},{"w":"quiescent","p":"adj.","d":"In a state of inactivity or dormancy.","c":"靜止的；不活動的","s":"Although the varicella-zoster virus can remain quiescent in nerve cells for decades after a childhood case of chickenpox, a weakened immune system in later life may allow it to reactivate, producing the painful rash known as shingles.","t":"雖然水痘帶狀疱疹病毒在童年感染水痘後，可能在神經細胞中靜止潛伏數十年，但晚年免疫系統衰弱時，它可能重新活化，引發疼痛的皮疹，也就是俗稱「皮蛇」的帶狀疱疹。","as":"Geologists warn that the volcano's quiescent state may be an illusion: beneath its tranquil surface, magma is slowly accumulating, and the transient tremors recorded last spring could be an ominous sign of an imminent eruption.","at":"地質學家警告，這座火山的靜止狀態可能只是假象：在平靜的表面下，岩漿正緩慢累積，而去年春天記錄到的短暫震動，可能是火山即將噴發的不祥徵兆。"},{"w":"taciturn","p":"adj.","d":"Habitually silent and reserved in speech.","c":"沉默寡言的","s":"Calvin Coolidge was so taciturn that Washington hostesses competed to coax more than a few words from him; according to a popular anecdote, when a dinner guest bet she could get more than two words out of him, he replied, 'You lose.'","t":"卡爾文．柯立芝沉默寡言到華府的女主人們競相設法讓他多說幾句話；根據一則流傳甚廣的軼事，曾有一位晚宴賓客跟他打賭，說她能讓他說出超過兩個字，他只回答：「妳輸了。」","as":"The taciturn Danish sculptor rarely discussed her work in interviews, yet critics found her aloof demeanor oddly compelling, and her eclectic installations, assembled from obsolete factory machinery, received widespread critical acclaim.","at":"這位沉默寡言的丹麥雕塑家很少在受訪時談論自己的作品，但評論家覺得她冷漠疏離的態度別具魅力，而她以廢棄工廠機械組裝而成、風格多元的裝置藝術，也廣受評論界讚譽。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Wordiness and Talkativeness","themeZh":"冗長與多話","cards":[{"w":"circumlocution","p":"n.","d":"The use of many words to avoid saying something directly.","c":"迂迴的說法；拐彎抹角","s":"Rather than admitting that the drug trial had failed, the pharmaceutical company's press release relied on elaborate circumlocution, describing the disappointing results as 'not yet aligned with initial expectations' and the abandoned study as 'a strategic recalibration of the clinical timeline.'","t":"這家製藥公司的新聞稿沒有承認藥物試驗失敗，而是用盡拐彎抹角的說法，把令人失望的結果形容為「尚未符合初步預期」，並把已放棄的研究稱為「臨床時程的策略性調整」。","as":"Annoyed by the minister's circumlocution, the incisive journalist demanded a succinct answer, observing that candor, not evasion, was what voters expected from an official accused of squandering public funds.","at":"被部長拐彎抹角的說法惹惱後，這位一針見血的記者要求他給出簡明扼要的回答，並指出選民期待一位被控揮霍公帑的官員坦誠以對，而不是閃爍其詞。"},{"w":"colloquial","p":"adj.","d":"Characteristic of informal, everyday conversation.","c":"口語的；通俗的","s":"Mark Twain's decision to narrate Adventures of Huckleberry Finn in the colloquial speech of an uneducated Missouri boy, complete with regional grammar and slang, shocked some nineteenth-century critics who believed that serious literature required formal, polished English.","t":"馬克．吐溫決定以一個未受教育的密蘇里男孩的口語來敘述《頑童歷險記》，連同地方性的文法和俚語都保留下來，這讓一些認為嚴肅文學必須使用正式、精練英文的十九世紀評論家大為震驚。","as":"The poet's colloquial diction, drawn from the chatter of city streets, struck pretentious critics as banal, yet younger readers found her eclectic blend of slang and classical allusion refreshingly novel.","at":"這位詩人取材自城市街頭閒談的口語化用詞，在自命不凡的評論家看來平庸乏味，但年輕讀者卻覺得她融合俚語與古典典故的多元風格新穎得令人耳目一新。"},{"w":"digress","p":"v.","d":"To stray temporarily from the main subject.","c":"離題；偏離主題","s":"The biology professor's tendency to digress from his lecture on cellular respiration into long stories about his fieldwork in the Amazon delighted some students, but others complained that the exam covered material he had never actually finished explaining in class.","t":"這位生物學教授在講授細胞呼吸作用時，常常離題去講他在亞馬遜雨林做田野調查的長篇故事，讓一些學生聽得津津有味，但也有學生抱怨考試考到了他在課堂上根本沒講完的內容。","as":"Whenever the historian began digressing into trivial anecdotes, her meticulous co-author would gently steer the discussion back to the debacle at Gallipoli and the strategic errors that caused it.","at":"每當這位歷史學家開始離題講些瑣碎的軼事，她那位一絲不苟的共同作者就會溫和地把討論拉回加里波利戰役的慘敗，以及導致這場慘敗的戰略失誤。"},{"w":"diffuse","p":"adj.","d":"Wordy and lacking focus or clear organization.","c":"冗長散漫的；不集中的","s":"Reviewers rejected the dissertation's first draft as diffuse, noting that its central argument about Ottoman trade networks was buried beneath hundreds of pages of loosely connected observations, repetitive summaries, and tangents that never returned to the thesis.","t":"審查委員認為這篇博士論文的初稿冗長散漫而予以退回，指出它關於鄂圖曼貿易網絡的核心論點，被埋沒在數百頁鬆散相連的觀察、重複的摘要，以及始終沒有回到論旨的枝節之中。","as":"The committee found the report so diffuse that its key recommendation was nearly invisible, so an astute editor abridged it into a concise summary that even the most phlegmatic legislators read with interest.","at":"委員會認為這份報告冗長散漫到幾乎看不出它的關鍵建議，於是一位精明的編輯將它刪節成一份簡潔的摘要，連最冷淡的立法委員都讀得津津有味。"},{"w":"eloquence","p":"n.","d":"Fluent, persuasive, and moving skill in speaking or writing.","c":"口才；雄辯","s":"Frederick Douglass's eloquence so astonished nineteenth-century audiences that some skeptics refused to believe he had ever been enslaved, assuming that no one denied a formal education could speak with such moving clarity, logical force, and command of classical rhetoric.","t":"弗雷德里克．道格拉斯的雄辯口才令十九世紀的聽眾大為驚嘆，以致一些懷疑者拒絕相信他曾經是奴隸，認定沒有受過正規教育的人不可能說話如此清晰動人、邏輯有力，又能駕馭古典修辭。","as":"Her eloquence won the debate not through flashy flourishes but through lucid, judicious arguments that left even her most belligerent opponents unable to impugn her reasoning.","at":"她憑藉雄辯贏得了這場辯論，靠的不是華麗的修辭，而是清晰而明智的論證，讓即使是最好鬥的對手也無從質疑她的推理。"},{"w":"grandiloquent","p":"adj.","d":"Using pompous, lofty language to impress others.","c":"浮誇的；誇大其詞的","s":"The dictator's grandiloquent speeches, filled with references to 'the eternal destiny of the motherland' and 'the immortal glory of our ancestors,' contrasted sharply with the grim reality of food shortages and power outages that ordinary citizens endured every day.","t":"這位獨裁者浮誇的演說充斥著「祖國永恆的命運」和「先祖不朽的榮光」之類的字眼，與一般民眾每天忍受的糧食短缺和停電等嚴峻現實形成強烈對比。","as":"The candidate's grandiloquent promises about restoring the nation's glory struck many voters as pretentious, and his ostentatious campaign rallies only reinforced the impression that he was a braggart rather than a serious leader.","at":"這位候選人關於恢復國家榮光的浮誇承諾，讓許多選民覺得自命不凡，而他鋪張炫耀的造勢晚會，更加深了他只是個愛吹牛的人、而非認真領袖的印象。"},{"w":"loquacious","p":"adj.","d":"Very talkative; fond of talking.","c":"話多的；健談的","s":"The loquacious tour guide filled every silence on the six-hour bus ride with stories about local legends, family gossip, and regional politics, so that by the time the group reached the ancient monastery, several exhausted passengers were pretending to sleep just to escape the commentary.","t":"這位話多的導遊在六小時的巴士車程中，用地方傳說、家族八卦和區域政治的故事填滿每一段沉默，以致於團員抵達那座古老修道院時，好幾位疲憊的乘客正假裝睡覺，只為了躲開他的解說。","as":"The loquacious host of the talk show, normally ebullient and jocular, became oddly reticent when guests asked about the lawsuit that had tarnished his reputation.","at":"這位脫口秀主持人平時話多、熱情洋溢又愛說笑，但當來賓問起那件損害他名譽的訴訟時，他卻變得異常沉默。"},{"w":"verbose","p":"adj.","d":"Using more words than are needed.","c":"冗長的；囉嗦的","s":"Software engineers often criticize older technical documentation as verbose, since a manual that devotes twelve pages to a single installation step forces users to wade through redundant definitions and repeated warnings before finding the one command they actually need.","t":"軟體工程師常批評舊的技術文件冗長囉嗦，因為一本花十二頁說明單一安裝步驟的手冊，迫使使用者在找到真正需要的那一行指令之前，必須費力讀過一堆重複的定義和警告。","as":"The legislation was so verbose that few lawmakers read it completely, allowing a clandestine provision buried on page nine hundred to give a mercenary contractor lucrative and unprecedented control over the state's prisons.","at":"這項法案冗長到很少有議員把它讀完，使得一條藏在第九百頁的祕密條款，讓一家唯利是圖的承包商取得了對該州監獄有利可圖、前所未有的控制權。"},{"w":"garrulous","p":"adj.","d":"Excessively talkative, especially about trivial matters.","c":"喋喋不休的；嘮叨的","s":"In Chaucer's Canterbury Tales, the garrulous Wife of Bath delivers a prologue longer than many of the tales themselves, rambling cheerfully through her five marriages, her opinions on scripture, and countless personal anecdotes before finally beginning the story she has promised the other pilgrims.","t":"在喬叟的《坎特伯里故事集》中，喋喋不休的巴斯婦人所講的開場白比許多故事本身還長，她興致勃勃地東拉西扯，談她的五段婚姻、她對經文的看法以及數不清的個人軼事，最後才開始講她答應其他朝聖者的故事。","as":"The garrulous neighbor's endless gossip seemed harmless, but detectives later realized that her trivial chatter contained a crucial clue about the furtive stranger who had been seen lingering near the house.","at":"那位喋喋不休的鄰居沒完沒了的閒話看似無害，但警探後來發現，她瑣碎的閒聊中藏著一條關鍵線索，指向那名曾被人看見在房子附近徘徊、鬼鬼祟祟的陌生人。"},{"w":"prattle","p":"v.","d":"To talk at length in a foolish or trivial way.","c":"喋喋不休地閒扯；胡扯","s":"During the hearing, the witness continued to prattle about his vacation plans, his favorite restaurants, and a dispute with his landlord, until the exasperated judge reminded him that the court needed only a simple answer about where he had been on the night of the robbery.","t":"聽證會上，這名證人一直喋喋不休地閒扯他的度假計畫、他最喜歡的餐廳，以及他和房東的糾紛，直到惱怒的法官提醒他，法庭只需要他簡單回答搶案當晚他人在哪裡。","as":"While the guests prattled about trivial matters like the weather and the menu, the astute diplomat quietly gathered intelligence from the nonchalant ambassador seated beside her.","at":"當賓客們閒扯著天氣和菜單之類的瑣事時，這位精明的外交官悄悄從坐在她身旁、漫不經心的大使那裡蒐集情報。"},{"w":"rant","p":"v.","d":"To speak loudly, angrily, and at length.","c":"大聲咆哮；激動地痛罵","s":"Instead of responding calmly to the scientific criticism of his methods, the embattled researcher ranted for twenty minutes during the conference session, shouting accusations at his critics and pounding the lectern, a performance that damaged his credibility far more than the original critique.","t":"這位飽受抨擊的研究人員沒有冷靜回應學界對他研究方法的批評，反而在研討會上咆哮了二十分鐘，對批評者大聲指控、猛拍講台；這番表現對他信譽的傷害，遠比原本的批評還要大。","as":"Rather than ranting at the referee, the coach adopted a stoical silence, knowing that a vociferous tirade would only earn a penalty and intimidate his already sluggish players.","at":"這位教練沒有對裁判大聲咆哮，而是選擇隱忍地保持沉默，因為他知道一番大吵大鬧的怒罵只會招來判罰，還會嚇到他那些原本就動作遲緩的球員。"},{"w":"rhetorical","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to language used to persuade or impress.","c":"修辭的；為修辭效果的","s":"Historians note that Martin Luther King Jr.'s 'I Have a Dream' speech derives much of its rhetorical power from anaphora, the deliberate repetition of a phrase at the start of successive sentences, a technique that builds emotional momentum and makes the speech memorable.","t":"歷史學家指出，馬丁．路德．金恩的〈我有一個夢〉演說，其修辭力量很大程度上來自首語重複法，也就是在連續句子的開頭刻意重複同一個片語；這種技巧能累積情感動能，使演說令人難忘。","as":"The senator's rhetorical skill could not disguise the spurious statistics in her speech, and an incisive fact-checker soon debunked her most ostentatious claims.","at":"這位參議員的修辭技巧掩蓋不了她演講中那些虛假的統計數據，一位眼光犀利的事實查核者很快就揭穿了她最誇張的說法。"},{"w":"voluble","p":"adj.","d":"Speaking fluently, readily, and at length.","c":"健談的；口若懸河的","s":"Normally shy in seminars, the graduate student became remarkably voluble whenever conversation turned to medieval astronomy, speaking rapidly and fluently for long stretches about astrolabes, star charts, and the Islamic scholars who had preserved and refined Ptolemy's calculations.","t":"這名研究生平時在研討課上很害羞，但只要話題轉到中世紀天文學，他就變得口若懸河，滔滔不絕地談論星盤、星圖，以及保存並改良托勒密計算的伊斯蘭學者。","as":"The voluble salesman's charm concealed a devious scheme: his glib assurances persuaded gullible investors to squander their savings on a fraudulent company run by a notorious charlatan.","at":"這位能言善道的推銷員的魅力背後藏著一個狡詐的詭計：他油嘴滑舌的保證說服了容易受騙的投資人，把積蓄揮霍在一家由惡名昭彰的騙子經營的詐騙公司上。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Arrogance and Pride","themeZh":"傲慢與自大","cards":[{"w":"arrogant","p":"adj.","d":"Having an exaggerated sense of one's own importance.","c":"傲慢的；自大的","s":"The young surgeon's arrogant refusal to consult the nurses, whom he considered beneath him, proved costly when he dismissed their warning about a patient's allergy, an error that a more humble physician would almost certainly have avoided.","t":"這位年輕外科醫師傲慢地拒絕徵詢護理師的意見，認為她們不如自己；當他對護理師關於病患過敏的警告置之不理時，這種態度付出了慘痛代價，而一位較謙虛的醫師幾乎肯定能避免這個錯誤。","as":"The arrogant general dismissed his scouts' cautious reports as frivolous, and his refusal to heed their warnings led to a debacle in which his army was trapped in a labyrinth of narrow mountain passes.","at":"這位傲慢的將軍把偵察兵謹慎的報告斥為無聊小事，而他拒絕聽從警告，導致了一場慘敗：他的軍隊被困在迷宮般的狹窄山路之中。"},{"w":"contemptuous","p":"adj.","d":"Showing that one considers someone or something worthless.","c":"輕蔑的；鄙視的","s":"Many established painters were openly contemptuous of the first Impressionist exhibition in 1874; one critic sneered that the loose brushwork looked like wallpaper in its earliest stage, and several refused to treat the movement as serious art at all.","t":"許多成名畫家對一八七四年的首次印象派畫展公開表示輕蔑；一位評論家譏諷那些鬆散的筆觸看起來像是剛起稿的壁紙，還有好幾位畫家根本拒絕把這個畫派當成嚴肅的藝術。","as":"The aristocrat's contemptuous dismissal of the artisans who built his palace revealed an odious snobbery, and his ostentatious spending soon became a frequent target of vociferous public criticism.","at":"這位貴族輕蔑地看待為他建造宮殿的工匠，暴露出令人憎惡的勢利心態，而他鋪張炫耀的揮霍也很快成為民眾大聲批評的常見目標。"},{"w":"complacent","p":"adj.","d":"Smugly satisfied and unaware of possible dangers.","c":"自滿的；自鳴得意的","s":"After decades as the world's dominant camera maker, the company grew complacent, assuming customers would always prefer film; executives ignored the early digital sensors developed in their own laboratories, and rivals who embraced the new technology soon captured the market.","t":"在稱霸全球相機市場數十年後，這家公司變得自滿，以為顧客永遠會偏好底片；高層忽視了自家實驗室早期研發的數位感光元件，而擁抱新技術的對手很快就奪走了市場。","as":"Public health officials warned that a complacent attitude toward the virus, even after infections became negligible, could prove detrimental, since a single virulent new strain might rapidly spread through a population whose vigilance had faded.","at":"公共衛生官員警告，即使感染人數已微不足道，對病毒抱持自滿的態度仍可能造成危害，因為只要出現一種毒性強的新變種，就可能在警覺心已鬆懈的人群中迅速蔓延。"},{"w":"disdainful","p":"adj.","d":"Showing scorn for something considered unworthy.","c":"輕蔑的；不屑的","s":"Classically trained musicians in the 1920s were often disdainful of jazz, dismissing its improvised solos as undisciplined noise, yet within a generation many conservatories had added jazz programs and recognized musicians like Louis Armstrong as genuine innovators.","t":"一九二〇年代受古典訓練的音樂家常對爵士樂不屑一顧，把它的即興獨奏斥為毫無章法的噪音；然而不到一個世代，許多音樂學院就已增設爵士課程，並認可路易．阿姆斯壯等音樂家為真正的創新者。","as":"The disdainful critic dismissed the debut novel as hackneyed and derivative, yet his pretentious review was soon forgotten while the book became a classic.","at":"這位不屑的評論家把那部處女作斥為陳腐又缺乏原創，但他那篇自命不凡的書評很快就被遺忘，而那本書卻成了經典。"},{"w":"insolent","p":"adj.","d":"Boldly rude and disrespectful toward authority.","c":"傲慢無禮的；目無尊長的","s":"When the young officer answered the admiral's order with an insolent shrug and a sarcastic remark in front of the entire crew, he was immediately relieved of duty, since naval discipline treated such open disrespect toward a superior as a serious offense.","t":"當這名年輕軍官在全體船員面前以傲慢無禮的聳肩和一句挖苦話回應上將的命令時，他立刻被解除職務，因為海軍紀律把這種公然冒犯上級的行為視為嚴重違紀。","as":"The insolent apprentice mocked his master's antiquated methods, but his impudent remarks only revealed how little he understood the craft he was so eager to scorn.","at":"這個傲慢無禮的學徒嘲笑師傅過時的手法，但他那番無禮的言論只暴露出他對自己急於鄙視的這門手藝有多麼無知。"},{"w":"presumptuous","p":"adj.","d":"Overstepping proper limits; taking too much for granted.","c":"冒昧的；放肆的","s":"Junior researchers sometimes worry that it would be presumptuous to correct a senior professor's calculation in public, yet philosophers of science argue that progress depends on precisely such willingness to challenge authority whenever the evidence demands it.","t":"資淺的研究人員有時擔心，當眾糾正資深教授的計算會顯得冒昧，但科學哲學家主張，科學的進步正仰賴這種只要證據需要，就願意挑戰權威的態度。","as":"Critics considered it presumptuous for the novice director, whose debut film was banal and lackluster, to extol his own work as an unprecedented achievement in cinema.","at":"評論家認為，這位新手導演的處女作平庸又乏味，他卻把自己的作品吹捧為電影史上前所未有的成就，實在是太過放肆。"},{"w":"pretentious","p":"adj.","d":"Trying to appear more important or cultured than one is.","c":"自命不凡的；做作的","s":"The art critic mocked the gallery's pretentious wall labels, which described a simple red square as 'a transcendent interrogation of chromatic hegemony,' arguing that inflated academic jargon often disguised the absence of any genuine idea about the work itself.","t":"這位藝評家嘲諷畫廊自命不凡的展品說明牌，它把一個簡單的紅色方塊形容為「對色彩霸權的超驗詰問」；他認為，浮誇的學術術語往往只是在掩飾作品本身毫無真正的想法。","as":"The restaurant's pretentious menu, full of grandiloquent descriptions of ordinary dishes, could not disguise the insipid food, and diners soon abandoned it for more unpretentious, palatable fare elsewhere.","at":"這家餐廳自命不凡的菜單，用浮誇的詞藻描述普通的菜色，卻掩蓋不了食物的平淡無味，顧客很快就轉往別處，去吃更樸實、更可口的餐點。"},{"w":"supercilious","p":"adj.","d":"Behaving as though one is superior to others.","c":"目中無人的；高傲的","s":"The museum's supercilious curator, who raised an eyebrow whenever visitors asked basic questions, was eventually replaced by a director who believed that public institutions had a duty to welcome newcomers rather than make them feel ignorant and unwelcome.","t":"這座博物館那位目中無人的策展人，每當參觀者問些基本問題就挑起眉毛；後來他終於被一位新館長取代，這位館長認為公共機構有責任歡迎初來乍到的人，而不是讓他們覺得自己無知又不受歡迎。","as":"The supercilious sommelier treated the diners with obvious disdain, and his condescending remarks about their unsophisticated taste struck everyone as petty, impudent, and needlessly belligerent.","at":"這位目中無人的侍酒師明顯對用餐的客人不屑一顧，他對客人品味粗俗的那番居高臨下的評論，讓所有人都覺得小家子氣、無禮，而且毫無必要地咄咄逼人。"},{"w":"ostentatious","p":"adj.","d":"Showy in a way meant to impress or attract notice.","c":"炫耀的；鋪張的","s":"During the Gilded Age, wealthy industrialists built ostentatious mansions in Newport, Rhode Island, complete with marble ballrooms and gold-leaf ceilings, less to provide comfortable homes than to display their newly acquired fortunes to rival families.","t":"在鍍金時代，富有的實業家在羅德島州的新港興建奢華炫耀的豪宅，配備大理石舞廳和金箔天花板；與其說是為了提供舒適的住所，不如說是要向敵對家族炫耀他們新得的財富。","as":"The billionaire's ostentatious yacht, adorned with a lavish gold staircase, struck observers as a vulgar contrast to the austere lives of the indigent fishermen who worked in the harbor where it was docked.","at":"這位億萬富翁鋪張炫耀的遊艇，飾有奢華的黃金階梯，在旁觀者眼中，與停泊港口裡那些貧困漁民的簡樸生活形成了庸俗的對比。"},{"w":"braggart","p":"n.","d":"A person who boasts loudly about achievements.","c":"吹牛者；自誇的人","s":"The Roman playwright Plautus created the comic character of the boastful soldier, a cowardly braggart who brags endlessly of imaginary victories and the enemies he claims to have slain, only to flee at the first sign of genuine danger.","t":"羅馬劇作家普勞圖斯創造了「吹牛軍人」這個喜劇角色：一個膽小的吹牛者，不停誇耀他那些想像中的勝利和他聲稱殺過的敵人，卻在真正的危險一出現時就落荒而逃。","as":"The braggart's egotistical boasts about his fortune proved spurious when investigators discovered that he was virtually indigent, having squandered his inheritance on gambling years earlier.","at":"這個吹牛者自我中心地誇耀自己的財富，結果被證明是假話；調查人員發現他幾乎一貧如洗，多年前就已把遺產揮霍在賭博上。"},{"w":"egotistical","p":"adj.","d":"Excessively absorbed in oneself; conceited.","c":"自我中心的；自負的","s":"The orchestra's musicians complained that their egotistical new conductor rearranged every program to feature his own compositions, demanded that his name appear in larger type than the composers', and spoke in rehearsals almost exclusively about his past triumphs.","t":"樂團成員抱怨，他們那位自我中心的新指揮把每場節目都改成以他自己的作品為主，要求他的名字要印得比作曲家還大，而且排練時幾乎只談他過去的輝煌成就。","as":"The egotistical chef was so contemptuous of criticism that he rebuffed every suggestion from his staff, and his intractable arrogance and rancorous outbursts eventually drove away his most talented cooks.","at":"這位自我中心的主廚對批評極為輕蔑，拒絕了員工的每一項建議，而他那難以駕馭的傲慢與充滿怨恨的暴怒，最終趕走了他最有才華的廚師。"},{"w":"haughty","p":"adj.","d":"Arrogantly proud and scornful of others.","c":"高傲的；傲慢的","s":"In Pride and Prejudice, Mr. Darcy's haughty refusal to dance with Elizabeth Bennet at the Meryton ball, together with his remark, made within her hearing, that she is merely 'tolerable' and not handsome enough to tempt him, establishes the poor first impression that much of the novel's plot is devoted to overturning.","t":"在《傲慢與偏見》中，達西先生在梅里頓舞會上高傲地拒絕與伊莉莎白．班奈特共舞，還在她聽得到的地方說她只是「還過得去」，不夠漂亮、引不起他的興趣；這奠定了糟糕的第一印象，而小說的大部分情節正是在扭轉這個印象。","as":"The haughty duchess treated her servants with disdain, yet when her fortune collapsed and she became indigent, she was forced to depend on the benevolent charity of the very servants she had scorned, whose magnanimous forgiveness astonished her.","at":"這位高傲的公爵夫人以輕蔑的態度對待僕人，然而當她家道中落、陷入貧困時，卻不得不仰賴那些曾被她鄙視的僕人好心的接濟，而他們寬宏大量的原諒令她大為震驚。"},{"w":"narcissist","p":"n.","d":"A person excessively absorbed in self-admiration.","c":"自戀者","s":"Psychologists distinguish healthy self-esteem from the behavior of a true narcissist, who constantly seeks admiration, exploits others without guilt, and reacts with rage to even mild criticism because his inflated self-image is, paradoxically, extremely fragile.","t":"心理學家把健康的自尊和真正自戀者的行為區分開來；自戀者不斷尋求讚美，毫無愧疚地利用他人，甚至對溫和的批評也勃然大怒，因為他膨脹的自我形象其實極為脆弱。","as":"The narcissist's obsession with his own reflection on social media left him oblivious to his friends' needs, and his egotistical demands for constant adulation eventually alienated even his most obsequious and servile admirers.","at":"這個自戀者沉迷於自己在社群媒體上的形象，對朋友的需要渾然不覺，而他自我中心地要求不斷被奉承，最終連他最阿諛諂媚、卑躬屈膝的崇拜者也疏遠了他。"},{"w":"swagger","p":"v.","d":"To walk or behave in a boastful, arrogant way.","c":"大搖大擺地走；神氣十足","s":"Contemporary accounts describe how the victorious pirate captain swaggered through the captured port, a jeweled sword at his hip and stolen silks draped over his shoulders, deliberately displaying his triumph to the frightened merchants who watched from shuttered windows.","t":"當時的記載描述，那位獲勝的海盜船長如何大搖大擺地穿過被攻占的港口，腰間掛著鑲滿寶石的佩劍，肩上披著搶來的絲綢，刻意向躲在緊閉窗戶後觀望、驚恐萬分的商人炫耀他的勝利。","as":"The champion swaggered onto the stage with exuberant confidence, but the audience found his vociferous boasts about defeating every adversary rather hackneyed.","at":"這位冠軍帶著洋溢的自信大搖大擺地走上舞台，但觀眾覺得他大聲誇口打敗所有對手的說法相當陳腐。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Dull and Unoriginal","themeZh":"乏味與陳腐","cards":[{"w":"derivative","p":"adj.","d":"Imitating the work of others; lacking originality.","c":"模仿的；缺乏原創性的","s":"Although the young architect's first skyscraper attracted attention, critics dismissed it as derivative, pointing out that its bronze-tinted glass curtain walls, exterior bronze I-beams, and open entrance plaza closely reproduced features of the Seagram Building, which Mies van der Rohe had designed half a century earlier.","t":"雖然這位年輕建築師的第一棟摩天大樓引起了關注，評論家卻認為它缺乏原創性，指出它的古銅色玻璃帷幕牆、外牆的青銅工字樑和開放式入口廣場，幾乎照搬了密斯．凡德羅半個世紀前所設計的西格拉姆大廈的特色。","as":"Critics who had praised the band's debut dismissed its second album as derivative, complaining that its songs merely recycled the melodies of obscure 1970s groups and that the musicians had grown complacent, even pretentious, after their early acclaim.","at":"曾稱讚這支樂團首張專輯的評論家，認為他們的第二張專輯缺乏原創，抱怨那些歌曲只是在重複一九七〇年代冷門樂團的旋律，而且團員在早期獲得讚譽後，變得自滿，甚至自命不凡。"},{"w":"insipid","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking flavor, interest, or vigor.","c":"枯燥乏味的；淡而無味的","s":"Food scientists discovered that tomatoes bred for uniform color and long shelf life tended to be insipid, because the genetic mutation responsible for even ripening also suppressed the production of the sugars and aromatic compounds that give homegrown varieties their rich flavor.","t":"食品科學家發現，為了顏色均勻和保存期長而培育的番茄往往淡而無味，因為造成均勻成熟的基因突變，同時也抑制了糖分和芳香化合物的生成，而正是這些物質賦予自家種植品種濃郁的風味。","as":"Diners found the celebrated chef's newest dish surprisingly insipid; his epicurean reputation could not disguise the fact that the stew was neither savory nor palatable.","at":"用餐者覺得這位知名主廚的最新菜色出奇地淡而無味；他講究美食的名聲也掩蓋不了這道燉菜既不鮮美也不可口的事實。"},{"w":"lackluster","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking brilliance, energy, or excitement; dull.","c":"黯淡無光的；平淡乏味的","s":"Economists attributed the region's lackluster growth during the 1990s to declining investment in education and infrastructure; while neighboring states attracted technology firms and expanded rapidly, its output rose by barely one percent a year for nearly a decade.","t":"經濟學家把這個地區在一九九〇年代黯淡的成長歸因於教育和基礎建設投資的減少；當鄰近各州吸引科技公司進駐並迅速擴張時，該地區的產出近十年來每年僅勉強成長約百分之一。","as":"After a lackluster first half, the sluggish team seemed listless and apathetic, but the coach's impassioned halftime speech transformed them into a vibrant, determined squad.","at":"在表現平平的上半場之後，這支動作遲緩的球隊顯得無精打采、漠不關心，但教練在中場休息時慷慨激昂的演說，讓他們脫胎換骨，成為一支充滿活力、意志堅定的隊伍。"},{"w":"mundane","p":"adj.","d":"Ordinary and everyday; lacking excitement.","c":"平凡的；世俗的","s":"Social historians increasingly study mundane records such as grocery receipts, laundry lists, and household account books, arguing that these seemingly unremarkable documents reveal more about how ordinary people actually lived than the speeches of kings or the decrees of governments.","t":"社會史學家越來越常研究平凡的紀錄，例如雜貨收據、洗衣清單和家庭帳簿，他們認為，這些看似不起眼的文件，比國王的演說或政府的法令更能揭示一般人實際上如何生活。","as":"The novelist transforms mundane events, such as a trivial argument over breakfast, into moments of profound insight, and her incisive, meticulous prose makes even the most prosaic details seem extraordinary.","at":"這位小說家能把平凡的事件，例如一場早餐時的瑣碎爭吵，轉化為深刻洞察的時刻；她犀利而一絲不苟的文筆，讓即使最平淡的細節也顯得非比尋常。"},{"w":"banal","p":"adj.","d":"So lacking in originality as to be boring.","c":"平庸的；陳腐的","s":"The philosopher Hannah Arendt famously described the evil of the Nazi bureaucrat Adolf Eichmann as banal, observing that he was not a monstrous fanatic but an ordinary, thoughtless official who spoke in clichés and carried out atrocities as routine administrative tasks.","t":"哲學家漢娜．鄂蘭有一句名言，形容納粹官僚阿道夫．艾希曼的邪惡是平庸的；她觀察到，他並不是一個殘暴的狂熱分子，而是一個平凡、不經思考的官員，滿口陳腔濫調，把暴行當作例行行政工作來執行。","as":"The commencement speaker's banal advice to 'follow your passion' disappointed the discerning graduates, who had hoped for an erudite, incisive address rather than a series of empty slogans.","at":"畢業典禮演講者那句「追隨你的熱情」的平庸建議，讓眼光敏銳的畢業生大失所望；他們原本期待一場博學而犀利的演說，而不是一連串空洞的口號。"},{"w":"platitude","p":"n.","d":"A remark used so often it has become meaningless.","c":"陳腔濫調；老生常談","s":"After the factory closure eliminated three thousand jobs, residents grew angry when the company's spokesperson offered only the platitude that 'change brings new opportunities,' a statement that provided no concrete information about retraining programs, severance pay, or future employment.","t":"工廠關閉造成三千人失業後，公司發言人只說了一句「改變帶來新機會」的陳腔濫調，讓居民十分憤怒，因為這句話完全沒有提供任何有關職業再訓練計畫、資遣費或未來就業的具體資訊。","as":"The politician's speech was a tedious string of platitudes about unity, and its vapid optimism did nothing to mollify voters who were indignant about the precarious economy.","at":"這位政治人物的演講是一連串關於團結的冗長陳腔濫調，那種空洞的樂觀完全無法安撫因經濟岌岌可危而憤慨的選民。"},{"w":"vapid","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking liveliness, interest, or intellectual substance.","c":"乏味的；空洞的","s":"Media scholars argue that algorithm-driven entertainment tends to become vapid, because programs engineered to appeal to the widest possible audience avoid challenging ideas, complex characters, or unfamiliar themes, leaving viewers with pleasant but intellectually empty content.","t":"媒體學者認為，演算法驅動的娛樂節目往往變得空洞乏味，因為那些為了吸引最廣大觀眾而設計的節目，會避開具挑戰性的想法、複雜的角色或陌生的主題，只留給觀眾愉快卻缺乏思想內涵的內容。","as":"The talk show's vapid conversations about celebrity fashion seemed frivolous to serious viewers, who longed for the incisive, thought-provoking debates the program had featured in its early, more contentious years.","at":"這個脫口秀關於名人時尚的空洞對話，在認真的觀眾眼中顯得輕浮無聊；他們懷念節目早期那些犀利、發人深省，而且更具爭議的辯論。"},{"w":"cliche","p":"n.","d":"An overused expression or idea that lacks originality.","c":"陳腔濫調；老套","s":"Film critics have noted that the 'mad scientist' who builds a dangerous machine in a remote castle has become such a cliche that contemporary screenwriters either avoid the figure entirely or present it ironically, knowing audiences will immediately recognize its familiar conventions.","t":"影評人指出，「在偏遠城堡裡打造危險機器的瘋狂科學家」已成為一種老套，因此當代編劇不是完全避開這個角色，就是以反諷的方式呈現，因為他們知道觀眾會立刻認出其中熟悉的套路。","as":"The novelist cleverly subverts the cliche of the brooding hero, giving her protagonist a jocular wit and an affable charm that render the usual gloomy stereotype obsolete.","at":"這位小說家巧妙地顛覆了陰鬱英雄的老套形象，賦予她的主角愛說笑的機智與和藹可親的魅力，讓常見的陰沉刻板印象顯得過時。"},{"w":"hackneyed","p":"adj.","d":"Made dull and meaningless through overuse.","c":"陳腐的；老掉牙的","s":"Literary agents report receiving hundreds of fantasy manuscripts built on the same hackneyed premise, in which an orphaned farm boy discovers he is the chosen one destined to defeat a dark lord, a plot so familiar that many agents stop reading after the first page.","t":"文學經紀人表示，他們收到數百份奇幻小說稿件，都建立在同一個老掉牙的前提上：一個成為孤兒的農場男孩發現自己是天選之人，注定要打敗黑暗魔王；這個情節熟悉到許多經紀人讀完第一頁就停下來了。","as":"The advertising agency rejected the hackneyed slogan as derivative and insipid, demanding instead an ingenious, novel campaign that would distinguish the brand from its competitors and win acclaim from jaded consumers.","at":"這家廣告公司以缺乏原創又平淡無味為由，否決了那句老掉牙的標語，要求改出一個巧妙新穎的宣傳活動，讓品牌與競爭對手有所區別，並贏得已感厭倦的消費者讚賞。"},{"w":"prosaic","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking imagination or poetic beauty; dull.","c":"平淡無奇的；乏味的","s":"Although legends claimed the ancient tunnels had been built to hide royal treasure, archaeologists found a far more prosaic explanation: the passages were simply drainage channels that carried rainwater away from the city's crowded markets and prevented seasonal flooding.","t":"雖然傳說宣稱這些古老隧道是為了藏匿王室寶藏而建，考古學家卻發現了一個平淡得多的解釋：這些通道只是排水渠道，用來把雨水從城市擁擠的市集排走，防止季節性淹水。","as":"Readers expecting a thrilling tale of espionage found the memoir disappointingly prosaic, since the former spy devoted most chapters to mundane paperwork rather than the audacious, clandestine missions and covert operations promised on the cover.","at":"期待一本刺激間諜故事的讀者，發現這本回憶錄平淡得令人失望，因為這位前間諜把大部分章節都花在平凡的文書作業上，而不是封面上承諾的大膽祕密任務和隱密行動。"},{"w":"trite","p":"adj.","d":"Overused and consequently of little importance; stale.","c":"陳腐的；老套的","s":"Speechwriters for the new prime minister deliberately avoided trite phrases such as 'a bright future for our children,' believing that voters had grown so weary of empty campaign language that only concrete, specific promises would persuade them to take the speech seriously.","t":"新任總理的講稿撰寫人刻意避開「為我們的孩子創造光明未來」這類老套的說法，因為他們認為選民早已厭倦空洞的競選語言，只有具體明確的承諾才能讓選民認真看待這篇演說。","as":"The teacher praised the student's essay for avoiding trite conclusions, noting that its incisive analysis, astute observations, and judicious use of evidence made it far more compelling than the banal summaries most classmates submitted.","at":"老師稱讚這名學生的文章避開了老套的結論，指出它犀利的分析、精闢的觀察和對證據明智的運用，使它遠比大多數同學交出的平庸摘要更具說服力。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Calming and Soothing","themeZh":"安撫與緩和","cards":[{"w":"alleviate","p":"v.","d":"To make pain, suffering, or a problem less severe.","c":"減輕；緩和","s":"To alleviate the chronic water shortages that had forced farmers to abandon their fields, engineers in the Negev Desert developed drip irrigation, a technique that delivers small amounts of water directly to plant roots and dramatically reduces the losses caused by evaporation.","t":"為了減輕長期缺水迫使農民放棄田地的問題，內蓋夫沙漠的工程師研發出滴灌技術，這種技術能將少量的水直接送到植物根部，大幅減少因蒸發造成的水分流失。","as":"Relief workers struggled to alleviate the suffering of the emaciated refugees, whose precarious camp lacked ample food, and the benevolent donations of foreign charities arrived only after weeks of delay.","at":"救援人員努力減輕骨瘦如柴的難民所受的苦難，他們棲身的營地岌岌可危，缺乏充足的食物，而外國慈善機構好心的捐贈，在延誤了好幾週之後才送達。"},{"w":"ameliorate","p":"v.","d":"To make a bad situation better or more tolerable.","c":"改善；改良","s":"Nineteenth-century reformers such as Edwin Chadwick sought to ameliorate the appalling living conditions in London's industrial slums by building sewers, supplying clean water, and enforcing sanitation laws, measures that sharply reduced deaths from cholera and typhoid within a generation.","t":"十九世紀的改革者，例如艾德溫．查德威克，試圖透過興建下水道、供應乾淨的水以及執行衛生法規，來改善倫敦工業貧民窟惡劣的生活條件；這些措施在一個世代內大幅降低了霍亂和傷寒的死亡人數。","as":"The new governor promised to ameliorate the plight of indigent families, but skeptics noted that her predecessor's similar pledges had proved spurious and that the state's finances remained precarious.","at":"新任州長承諾要改善貧困家庭的困境，但懷疑者指出，她前任類似的承諾已被證明是空話，而州政府的財政依然岌岌可危。"},{"w":"appease","p":"v.","d":"To calm someone by giving in to their demands.","c":"安撫；姑息","s":"In 1938, British Prime Minister Neville Chamberlain hoped to appease Adolf Hitler by allowing Germany to annex part of Czechoslovakia, but the concession only encouraged further aggression, and within a year Europe was at war.","t":"一九三八年，英國首相張伯倫希望透過允許德國併吞捷克斯洛伐克的部分領土來安撫希特勒，但這項讓步只助長了更多侵略行為，不到一年歐洲便陷入戰爭。","as":"The cantankerous critic was impossible to appease; he berated the orchestra for its lackluster tempo and dismissed the soloist's virtuoso performance as ostentatious display.","at":"這位脾氣暴躁的評論家根本無法安撫；他痛斥樂團的速度平淡無力，還把獨奏家精湛的演出貶為賣弄炫技。"},{"w":"assuage","p":"v.","d":"To make an unpleasant feeling less intense.","c":"緩和；平息（情緒）","s":"To assuage public fears after the nuclear accident, the government released hourly radiation readings from dozens of monitoring stations, hoping that transparent data would calm residents more effectively than official reassurances, which many citizens no longer trusted.","t":"為了緩和核災後民眾的恐懼，政府每小時公布數十個監測站的輻射讀數，希望透明的數據能比官方的保證更有效地安撫居民，因為許多民眾已不再信任官方說法。","as":"The candid apology from the company's chief executive did little to assuage the anger of investors, who remained indignant that their savings had been squandered through such imprudent decisions.","at":"公司執行長坦率的道歉，幾乎無法平息投資人的怒氣；他們仍對自己的積蓄因如此輕率的決策而被揮霍殆盡感到憤慨。"},{"w":"conciliate","p":"v.","d":"To win over or reconcile through friendly acts.","c":"安撫；調和；爭取（好感）","s":"After the bitter civil war, the new president sought to conciliate the defeated rebels by appointing several of their leaders to cabinet posts and granting amnesty to former soldiers, gestures intended to persuade former enemies that they had a future in the united nation.","t":"在慘烈的內戰之後，新總統試圖撫慰戰敗的叛軍，任命其中幾位領袖擔任內閣職位，並赦免前士兵；這些舉動旨在說服昔日的敵人，讓他們相信自己在統一的國家中仍有未來。","as":"Hoping to conciliate her belligerent rivals within the party, the prime minister offered them prominent cabinet posts, a magnanimous gesture that gradually eased years of rancorous division.","at":"為了爭取黨內那些好鬥的對手，首相提供他們重要的內閣職位；這個寬宏大量的舉動逐漸化解了多年來充滿怨恨的分裂。"},{"w":"mitigate","p":"v.","d":"To make something harmful less severe or serious.","c":"減輕；緩和","s":"Coastal cities in the Netherlands have built floating homes, storm-surge barriers, and parks designed to absorb excess water, all intended to mitigate the damage that rising sea levels and increasingly powerful storms are expected to cause over the coming century.","t":"荷蘭的沿海城市興建了漂浮屋、防暴潮屏障和可吸收多餘水量的公園，全都是為了減輕未來一個世紀海平面上升和日益強烈的暴風雨預計將造成的損害。","as":"Engineers designed the levees to mitigate the effects of flooding, but the unprecedented turbulence of the storm and the detrimental erosion of the riverbanks overwhelmed even these meticulous preparations.","at":"工程師設計這些堤防是為了減輕洪水的影響，但暴風雨前所未有的劇烈擾動，加上河岸遭受的有害侵蝕，連這些一絲不苟的準備也抵擋不住。"},{"w":"mollify","p":"v.","d":"To soothe the anger or anxiety of someone.","c":"撫慰；平息（怒氣）","s":"To mollify the furious passengers whose flight had been delayed overnight, the airline offered hotel vouchers, meal credits, and a full refund, though several travelers insisted that no compensation could make up for missing a family wedding the following morning.","t":"為了平息航班延誤一整夜的乘客的怒氣，航空公司提供了飯店住宿券、餐點抵用金和全額退款，但仍有幾位旅客堅稱，無論什麼補償都彌補不了他們錯過隔天早上家族婚禮的遺憾。","as":"Nothing the manager said could mollify the irate customer, whose vociferous complaints about the restaurant's insipid food and the waiter's supercilious attitude echoed through the dining room.","at":"經理說什麼都無法平息那位暴怒顧客的怒氣，他大聲抱怨餐廳的食物淡而無味、服務生目中無人，聲音響徹整個用餐區。"},{"w":"pacify","p":"v.","d":"To bring peace or calm to someone or something.","c":"使平靜；平定","s":"Developmental psychologists have found that rhythmic rocking and low, steady sounds such as a heartbeat can pacifyedistressed infants more quickly than feeding, possibly because these sensations resemble the conditions babies experienced in the womb.","t":"發展心理學家發現，有節奏的搖晃和低沉穩定的聲音，例如心跳聲，比餵奶更能快速讓不安的嬰兒平靜下來，可能是因為這些感覺與嬰兒在子宮中所經歷的環境相似。","as":"The colonial governor attempted to pacify the rebellious province with a combination of lavish bribes and threats designed to intimidate local leaders, but these devious tactics only intensified the turmoil.","at":"殖民地總督企圖以豐厚的賄賂與用來恐嚇地方領袖的威脅雙管齊下，來平定這個叛亂的省分，但這些狡詐的手段只讓動盪更加劇烈。"},{"w":"allay","p":"v.","d":"To reduce or put to rest fear, worry, or suspicion.","c":"減輕；消除（疑慮）","s":"To allay parents' concerns about the new vaccine, pediatricians held community meetings at which they explained the results of large clinical trials, described possible side effects honestly, and answered questions until even the most hesitant families felt reassured.","t":"為了消除家長對新疫苗的疑慮，小兒科醫師舉辦社區說明會，解釋大型臨床試驗的結果，坦白說明可能的副作用，並一一回答問題，直到連最猶豫的家庭也感到安心。","as":"The central bank's candid statement helped allay investors' fears of an imminent debacle, and the volatile market, after weeks of turbulence, finally began to stabilize.","at":"央行坦率的聲明幫助消除了投資人對即將發生大崩盤的恐懼，而動盪不安的市場在經歷數週的劇烈波動後，終於開始趨於穩定。"},{"w":"quell","p":"v.","d":"To put an end to something, typically by force.","c":"鎮壓；平息","s":"Roman emperors frequently relied on the legions to quell provincial uprisings, and historians estimate that the campaign to crush the Jewish revolt of 66 CE involved more than sixty thousand soldiers and ended with the destruction of Jerusalem's Temple.","t":"羅馬皇帝經常仰賴軍團鎮壓行省的叛亂；歷史學家估計，西元六十六年鎮壓猶太人起義的戰役動用了超過六萬名士兵，最後以耶路撒冷聖殿被摧毀告終。","as":"The authorities quelled the riot within hours, but the underlying animosity between the two communities, fueled by years of rancorous disputes, remained an ominous threat to the city's fragile tranquility.","at":"當局在數小時內平息了暴動，但兩個社群之間因多年充滿怨恨的爭端而助長的潛在敵意，仍是對這座城市脆弱安寧的不祥威脅。"},{"w":"mediate","p":"v.","d":"To act as a go-between to settle a dispute.","c":"調解；斡旋","s":"In 1978, President Jimmy Carter invited Egypt's Anwar Sadat and Israel's Menachem Begin to Camp David and spent thirteen days shuttling between their cabins to mediate the negotiations, eventually helping the two former enemies reach a historic peace agreement.","t":"一九七八年，美國總統卡特邀請埃及總統沙達特和以色列總理比金前往大衛營，花了十三天在兩人的小屋之間來回奔走，居中調解談判，最終協助這兩個昔日敵人達成歷史性的和平協議。","as":"The retired judge agreed to mediate the contentious dispute between the union and management, and her impartial, judicious approach gradually eased the animosity that had stalled negotiations for months.","at":"這位退休法官同意居中調解工會與資方之間爭議不斷的糾紛，她公正而明智的做法逐漸化解了讓談判停滯數月的敵意。"},{"w":"placate","p":"v.","d":"To make someone less angry or hostile.","c":"安撫；使息怒","s":"Facing mounting protests over rising bread prices, the eighteenth-century French government placated the crowds in Paris by temporarily lowering grain taxes, but the measure did nothing to address the deeper economic inequalities that would erupt into revolution only a few years later.","t":"面對因麵包價格上漲而日益升高的抗議，十八世紀的法國政府暫時降低穀物稅來安撫巴黎的群眾，但這項措施完全沒有處理更深層的經濟不平等，而這些不平等僅僅幾年後就爆發成大革命。","as":"Attempting to placate the indignant villagers, the mining company offered a lavish compensation package, but residents remained wary, suspecting the offer was a devious ploy to silence their complaints about polluted water.","at":"為了安撫憤慨的村民，這家礦業公司提出一份優渥的賠償方案，但居民仍保持警惕，懷疑這項提議是一個狡猾的計謀，目的是讓他們對水源污染的抱怨噤聲。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Friendly and Sociable","themeZh":"友善與合群","cards":[{"w":"affable","p":"adj.","d":"Friendly, easy to talk to, and approachable.","c":"和藹可親的；平易近人的","s":"Although the Nobel laureate was famous for her uncompromising rigor in the laboratory, graduate students who visited her office were surprised to find her affable and unpretentious, happy to chat about their half-finished experiments and quick to put even the most nervous newcomer at ease.","t":"雖然這位諾貝爾獎得主以在實驗室中毫不妥協的嚴謹著稱，但拜訪她辦公室的研究生卻驚訝地發現她和藹可親、毫不做作，樂於討論他們尚未完成的實驗，也總能很快讓最緊張的新人放鬆下來。","as":"Unlike his haughty and supercilious predecessor, the new ambassador was affable with local officials, and his willingness to mediate small disputes over coffee did more to placate the restless provinces than any grandiloquent speech.","at":"與他那傲慢自大、目中無人的前任不同，新任大使對地方官員和藹可親；他願意在喝咖啡時調解小糾紛，這比任何浮誇的演講都更能安撫那些躁動不安的省份。"},{"w":"congenial","p":"adj.","d":"Pleasant and agreeable, especially because suited to one's tastes.","c":"意氣相投的；宜人的","s":"After years of isolation at a provincial university, the young philosopher found the Vienna Circle wonderfully congenial: its members shared her enthusiasm for logic and science, welcomed her blunt criticisms, and met each week in a café where ideas were debated with good humor rather than hostility.","t":"在一所地方大學孤立多年之後，這位年輕哲學家發現維也納學圈與她非常意氣相投：成員們和她一樣熱愛邏輯與科學，歡迎她直率的批評，而且每週在咖啡館聚會，以幽默而非敵意的態度辯論各種想法。","as":"The congenial atmosphere of the writers' retreat encouraged even the most reticent poets to share their drafts, and the director's pithy, constructive feedback helped them prune verbose passages without any sense of humiliation.","at":"作家駐村營融洽宜人的氛圍，讓即使是最沉默寡言的詩人也願意分享草稿，而主任精闢且具建設性的回饋，幫助他們刪減冗長的段落，卻絲毫不讓人感到難堪。"},{"w":"convivial","p":"adj.","d":"Friendly and lively, especially when eating and drinking together.","c":"歡樂的；好交際的","s":"Historians of the Enlightenment argue that London's coffeehouses were not merely places of refreshment but convivial spaces in which merchants, scientists, and pamphleteers shared tables, swapped gossip over steaming cups, and, amid the laughter and noise, formed the alliances that shaped commercial and intellectual life.","t":"研究啟蒙運動的歷史學家認為，倫敦的咖啡館不僅是提供飲料的場所，更是歡樂熱鬧的交際空間：商人、科學家和小冊子作者在此同桌而坐，一邊喝著熱騰騰的咖啡一邊交換八卦，並在笑聲與喧鬧中結成了塑造商業與知識生活的同盟。","as":"Far from the stiff, taciturn banquets of the old court, the new king's feasts were convivial affairs, though critics complained that their ostentatious displays of wealth and the garrulous toasts that lasted past midnight bordered on vulgarity.","at":"新國王的宴會與舊宮廷那種拘謹沉悶的宴席截然不同，總是歡樂熱鬧；但批評者抱怨，宴會上炫耀財富的浮華排場，以及持續到午夜之後、喋喋不休的祝酒詞，簡直近乎粗俗。"},{"w":"amicable","p":"adj.","d":"Characterized by friendliness and goodwill, without serious disagreement.","c":"友好的；和睦的","s":"Although the two research universities had spent a decade quarreling over patent rights to the gene-editing technique, their lawyers eventually negotiated an amicable settlement that divided licensing revenues evenly and allowed scientists from both institutions to resume their once-productive collaboration.","t":"儘管這兩所研究型大學為了基因編輯技術的專利權爭吵了十年，雙方律師最終仍協商出一份友好的和解協議，平分授權收入，並讓兩校的科學家得以恢復曾經成果豐碩的合作。","as":"The amicable separation of the two nations, achieved through patient mediation rather than war, helped allay regional fears of violence and showed that even deeply rooted hostility could be ameliorated by skillful diplomacy.","at":"這兩個國家透過耐心的調停而非戰爭達成友好分離，有助於平息區域內對暴力衝突的恐懼，也證明了即使是根深蒂固的敵意，也能藉由高明的外交手腕加以緩和。"},{"w":"amiable","p":"adj.","d":"Having a pleasant, friendly, and good-natured disposition.","c":"友善的；和藹的","s":"Jane Austen's narrator gently mocks Mr. Bingley as almost too amiable: so eager to please everyone and so incapable of suspecting ill intentions in others that his good nature makes him easily manipulated by friends and relatives who hope to steer his romantic choices.","t":"珍·奧斯汀筆下的敘述者溫和地嘲諷賓利先生近乎過於和善：他太急於討好每個人，又完全不會懷疑別人居心不良，以致他的好脾氣讓他很容易被那些想左右他婚戀選擇的朋友和親戚操縱。","as":"The amiable host tried to pacify his quarreling guests with a few jokes, but his attempt to mollify them failed when one arrogant critic launched into a long rant about the hackneyed plot of the play they had just seen.","at":"這位和藹的主人試圖用幾個笑話安撫爭吵不休的賓客，但當一位傲慢的評論家開始滔滔不絕地抨擊他們剛看完那齣戲的陳腐情節時，他平息眾人情緒的努力便宣告失敗。"},{"w":"cordial","p":"adj.","d":"Warm, sincere, and politely friendly.","c":"熱誠的；友好的","s":"Despite decades of Cold War rivalry, the 1975 docking of an American Apollo capsule with a Soviet Soyuz spacecraft featured a remarkably cordial exchange: the two commanders shook hands through the open hatch, traded gifts, and shared a meal broadcast to millions of viewers on both sides of the Iron Curtain.","t":"儘管美蘇之間有數十年的冷戰對抗，1975年美國阿波羅太空艙與蘇聯聯盟號太空船對接時，雙方的互動卻格外熱誠友好：兩位指揮官透過敞開的艙門握手、互贈禮物，並共進一餐，畫面向鐵幕兩側數百萬觀眾播出。","as":"Although the meeting between the two rival chief executives was cordial, observers noted that their terse replies and reticent body language suggested that the merger talks had not truly assuaged years of bitter competition.","at":"雖然兩家對手公司執行長的會面氣氛客氣友好，但觀察人士注意到，他們簡短生硬的回答和拘謹保留的肢體語言顯示，合併談判並未真正化解多年來的激烈競爭。"},{"w":"gregarious","p":"adj.","d":"Fond of company; sociable and outgoing.","c":"愛交際的；合群的","s":"Psychologists have found that gregarious people, who seek out crowded parties and strike up conversations with strangers on trains, tend to report higher daily happiness, yet even naturally introverted participants felt happier when instructed to behave more sociably for a week.","t":"心理學家發現，喜歡參加熱鬧派對、會在火車上主動與陌生人攀談的愛交際者，往往表示日常幸福感較高；然而，即使是天生內向的受試者，在被要求連續一週表現得更外向合群之後，也感到更快樂。","as":"The gregarious senator could charm almost anyone at a fundraiser, but his loquacious speeches and colloquial jokes struck some voters as pretentious attempts to seem like an ordinary citizen rather than sincere expressions of his character.","at":"這位愛交際的參議員在募款餐會上幾乎能迷住任何人，但他滔滔不絕的演講和口語化的笑話，在部分選民眼中只是刻意裝成普通市民的做作之舉，而非真誠展現其性格。"},{"w":"levity","p":"n.","d":"Humor or lightheartedness, especially at a serious moment.","c":"輕鬆幽默；輕浮","s":"Abraham Lincoln was often criticized for telling jokes during the darkest months of the Civil War, but he defended his levity as a necessity, explaining to grieving colleagues that without occasional laughter the strain of so much bloodshed would have broken him entirely.","t":"亞伯拉罕·林肯常因在南北戰爭最黑暗的幾個月裡講笑話而受到批評，但他辯稱這種輕鬆幽默是必要的，並向悲痛的同僚解釋，若沒有偶爾的笑聲，如此多流血犧牲帶來的壓力早已將他徹底擊垮。","as":"A moment of levity during the tense negotiations helped mitigate the hostility in the room: when the weary mediator made a self-deprecating joke, even the most taciturn delegates laughed, and that brief laughter appeased tempers enough for the talks to resume.","at":"緊張談判中的片刻輕鬆幽默，有助於緩和會場裡的敵意：當疲憊的調解人說了個自嘲的笑話時，連最沉默寡言的代表也笑了出來，而這短暫的笑聲平息了眾人的怒氣，讓談判得以繼續進行。"},{"w":"jocular","p":"adj.","d":"Fond of joking; humorous or playful in manner.","c":"詼諧的；愛開玩笑的","s":"Darwin's private letters to his botanist friend Joseph Hooker are surprisingly jocular, full of good-natured teasing, mock complaints about the barnacles he spent eight years dissecting, and playful exaggerations—a lighthearted tone that contrasts sharply with the cautious, carefully hedged prose of On the Origin of Species.","t":"達爾文寫給植物學家友人約瑟夫·胡克的私人信件出奇地詼諧，充滿善意的調侃、對他花了八年解剖的藤壺所發的假意抱怨，以及俏皮的誇飾——這種輕鬆的語氣與《物種起源》中謹慎、措辭保留的文字形成強烈對比。","as":"The professor's jocular asides kept his lectures lively, but students noticed that his humor never caused him to digress: each joke was succinct, pointed, and designed to make an otherwise prosaic concept in thermodynamics memorable.","at":"這位教授詼諧的插話讓他的課生動活潑，但學生注意到他的幽默從不使他離題：每個笑話都簡潔扼要、一針見血，目的是讓熱力學中原本平淡無奇的概念令人印象深刻。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Hostile and Argumentative","themeZh":"敵意與好鬥","cards":[{"w":"antagonism","p":"n.","d":"Active hostility or opposition between people or groups.","c":"敵對；對抗","s":"The long-standing antagonism between Thomas Edison and George Westinghouse during the so-called War of the Currents led Edison's allies to stage public demonstrations in which animals were electrocuted with alternating current, a grim publicity campaign intended to convince Americans that his rival's system was lethally dangerous.","t":"在所謂的「電流之戰」期間，湯瑪斯·愛迪生與喬治·威斯汀豪斯之間長期的敵對，導致愛迪生的盟友公開示範以交流電電死動物，這場殘酷的宣傳活動意在讓美國人相信對手的系統具有致命危險。","as":"The antagonism between the two schools of economists was so entrenched that every conference became a contest of grandiloquent rhetoric, and only an affable moderator with a gift for amicable compromise could keep the debates civil.","at":"這兩派經濟學家之間的對立根深蒂固，每次研討會都淪為浮誇言辭的較勁，只有一位和藹可親、善於促成友好妥協的主持人，才能讓辯論保持文明。"},{"w":"contentious","p":"adj.","d":"Causing or likely to cause heated argument.","c":"引起爭議的；好爭論的","s":"The ownership of the Parthenon sculptures, removed by Lord Elgin in the early 1800s, remains one of the most contentious issues in cultural heritage law, pitting Greek officials who demand their return against British Museum trustees who insist the marbles were legally acquired.","t":"埃爾金勳爵於十九世紀初移走的帕德嫩神廟雕塑，其所有權至今仍是文化遺產法中最具爭議的問題之一，一邊是要求歸還的希臘官員，另一邊則是堅稱這些大理石雕像乃合法取得的大英博物館董事。","as":"In a contentious town hall meeting, residents who opposed the new highway delivered a voluble stream of objections, while the mayor tried in vain to placate them with banal assurances that the project would benefit everyone.","at":"在一場爭論激烈的市民大會上，反對新公路的居民滔滔不絕地提出一連串異議，而市長則試圖用陳腔濫調的保證來安撫他們，聲稱這項工程將造福所有人，卻徒勞無功。"},{"w":"disputatious","p":"adj.","d":"Fond of arguing; inclined to dispute.","c":"好辯的；愛爭論的","s":"Samuel Johnson's companions often noted that he was so disputatious in conversation that he would happily defend a position he did not actually believe, simply for the pleasure of contradicting whoever was speaking and overpowering his opponents with sheer force of wit and erudition.","t":"山繆·約翰生的友人常提到，他在交談中極為好辯，甚至樂於為自己其實並不相信的立場辯護，只為了享受反駁眼前說話者的樂趣，並以純粹的機智與淵博學識壓倒對手。","as":"The disputatious philosopher would seize on any platitude a student uttered and dismantle it with pithy counterarguments, yet his disdainful tone made even his most cogent objections seem arrogant rather than enlightening.","at":"這位好辯的哲學家會抓住學生說出的任何陳腔濫調，用精闢的反駁將其逐一拆解；然而他輕蔑的語氣，卻使他最有說服力的反對意見也顯得傲慢自大，而非發人深省。"},{"w":"predator","p":"n.","d":"An animal or person that preys on or exploits others.","c":"掠食者；掠奪者","s":"Regulators warned that payday lenders operating near military bases had become financial predators, deliberately targeting young enlisted soldiers with loans whose annual interest rates exceeded 300 percent and trapping many borrowers in cycles of debt they could not escape.","t":"監管機關警告，在軍事基地附近營業的發薪日貸款業者已成為金融掠奪者，刻意鎖定年輕的入伍士兵，提供年利率超過百分之三百的貸款，使許多借款人陷入無法脫身的債務循環。","as":"Documentaries often portray the shark as a ruthless predator, but marine biologists argue that such hackneyed images are derivative of Hollywood thrillers and that this banal stereotype hampers conservation efforts for species that are now critically endangered.","at":"紀錄片常把鯊魚描繪成冷酷無情的掠食者，但海洋生物學家認為，這類老套的形象只是仿效好萊塢驚悚片，而這種陳腐的刻板印象阻礙了對如今已極度瀕危物種的保育工作。"},{"w":"animosity","p":"n.","d":"Strong dislike or hostility toward someone.","c":"敵意；仇恨","s":"The bitter animosity between Isaac Newton and Gottfried Leibniz over who had invented calculus lasted until Leibniz's death in 1716, and Newton, then president of the Royal Society, secretly wrote much of the supposedly impartial committee report that accused his rival of plagiarism.","t":"艾薩克·牛頓與哥特佛萊德·萊布尼茲之間為了誰發明微積分而產生的強烈敵意，一直持續到萊布尼茲於1716年去世為止；當時身為皇家學會會長的牛頓，還暗中撰寫了那份號稱公正、指控對手剽竊的委員會報告的大部分內容。","as":"Years of animosity between the rival architects had poisoned their professional relationship, so when one publicly called the other's design hackneyed and insipid, no amount of cordial diplomacy could pacify him.","at":"兩位互相較勁的建築師多年來的敵意早已毒害了彼此的專業關係，因此當其中一人公開批評對方的設計陳腐乏味時，無論多麼客氣友好的斡旋都無法平息對方的怒氣。"},{"w":"captious","p":"adj.","d":"Inclined to find fault or raise petty objections.","c":"吹毛求疵的；挑剔的","s":"The peer reviewer's report was so captious that the authors struggled to take it seriously: rather than addressing the study's central methodology, it devoted three pages to complaints about comma placement, the font used in one figure, and the order in which references were listed.","t":"那位同儕審查者的報告極為吹毛求疵，作者們實在很難認真看待：報告沒有討論這項研究的核心方法，反而花了三頁篇幅抱怨逗號位置、其中一張圖使用的字型，以及參考文獻的排列順序。","as":"The captious critic dismissed the novel's eloquence as mere ornament and complained that its dialogue was too colloquial, yet readers found his own reviews far more trite than anything he claimed to despise.","at":"這位吹毛求疵的評論家把這部小說的優美文筆貶為純粹的裝飾，還抱怨其對白太過口語化，然而讀者卻覺得他自己的書評遠比他聲稱厭惡的任何東西都更加陳腐。"},{"w":"belligerent","p":"adj.","d":"Hostile, aggressive, and eager to fight.","c":"好戰的；挑釁的","s":"Diplomatic historians note that Kaiser Wilhelm II's belligerent speeches, including his notorious urging that German troops sent to China behave like the Huns of Attila, alarmed British leaders and helped convince them that Germany's expanding navy was intended for aggression rather than defense.","t":"外交史學家指出，德皇威廉二世好戰的演說——包括他惡名昭彰地鼓吹派往中國的德軍要像阿提拉的匈人一樣行事——令英國領導人深感不安，並使他們相信德國不斷擴張的海軍是為了侵略而非防禦。","as":"Rather than conciliate his critics, the belligerent commander issued a contemptuous statement mocking their concerns, a haughty response that only intensified public outrage and made a negotiated peace seem even more remote.","at":"這位好戰的指揮官非但沒有安撫批評者，反而發表了一份輕蔑的聲明嘲弄他們的憂慮；這種傲慢的回應只讓民眾的憤怒更加高漲，也讓透過談判實現和平的希望顯得更加渺茫。"},{"w":"pugnacious","p":"adj.","d":"Eager or quick to argue, quarrel, or fight.","c":"好鬥的；愛挑釁的","s":"Known for his pugnacious temperament, the nineteenth-century anatomist Thomas Henry Huxley relished public confrontations so much that he earned the nickname 'Darwin's Bulldog,' famously clashing with Bishop Samuel Wilberforce at the 1860 Oxford debate over evolution.","t":"十九世紀解剖學家湯瑪斯·亨利·赫胥黎以好鬥的性格聞名，他非常熱衷於公開交鋒，因而贏得「達爾文的鬥牛犬」這個綽號；他在1860年牛津的演化論辯論中與山繆·威爾伯福斯主教激烈交鋒，此事廣為人知。","as":"The pugnacious talk-show host loved to swagger across the stage and rant at his guests, but his insolent interruptions and constant personal attacks eventually alienated even loyal viewers who had once admired his bluntness.","at":"這位好鬥的脫口秀主持人喜歡在臺上大搖大擺地走來走去，對著來賓高聲咆哮，但他無禮的插話與不斷的人身攻擊，最終連那些曾經欣賞他直率作風的忠實觀眾也疏遠了。"},{"w":"bellicose","p":"adj.","d":"Eager to fight or go to war; aggressive.","c":"好戰的；尚武的","s":"Historians argue that the bellicose rhetoric of newspapers owned by William Randolph Hearst, which published lurid and often exaggerated stories about Spanish atrocities in Cuba, helped push a hesitant American public toward war with Spain in 1898.","t":"歷史學家認為，威廉·藍道夫·赫斯特旗下報紙那些好戰的言論——大量刊登聳人聽聞、往往誇大其詞的西班牙在古巴暴行報導——促使原本猶豫不決的美國民眾在1898年走向對西班牙的戰爭。","as":"The general's bellicose speeches were long on grandiloquent threats but short on strategy, and diplomats hoped that quiet mediation could allay the fears of neighboring states before his pretentious bluster provoked an actual war.","at":"這位將軍好戰的演說充滿浮誇的威脅，卻缺乏實際戰略；外交官們希望在他那做作的虛張聲勢真正引發戰爭之前，能透過低調的調停來消除鄰國的疑懼。"},{"w":"cantankerous","p":"adj.","d":"Bad-tempered, argumentative, and difficult to deal with.","c":"脾氣暴躁的；難相處的","s":"By the end of his career, the once-celebrated astronomer had grown so cantankerous that younger colleagues avoided the observatory dining hall, knowing that any casual remark about the weather, the telescope schedule, or university politics might provoke an irritable twenty-minute lecture on everyone else's incompetence.","t":"到了職業生涯末期，這位曾經備受讚譽的天文學家變得脾氣極為暴躁，年輕同事們都避開天文台的餐廳，因為他們知道，任何關於天氣、望遠鏡排程或大學政治的隨口一提，都可能引來他一場長達二十分鐘、怒氣沖沖地數落別人無能的訓話。","as":"The cantankerous old editor was notoriously taciturn with strangers, but when a young writer submitted a verbose, hackneyed manuscript, he responded with a terse note that simply read, 'Cut everything you love.'","at":"這位脾氣暴躁的老編輯以對陌生人沉默寡言出了名，但當一位年輕作家交來一份冗長又陳腐的稿件時，他回了一張簡短生硬的紙條，上面只寫著：「把你所有心愛的段落全刪了。」"},{"w":"polemical","p":"adj.","d":"Strongly critical or argumentative in writing or speech.","c":"論戰的；爭論性的","s":"Thomas Paine's Common Sense was openly polemical, attacking the very idea of hereditary monarchy as absurd and ridiculing King George III as a 'royal brute,' and its fierce, combative style helped convert thousands of hesitant colonists to the cause of independence in 1776.","t":"湯瑪斯·潘恩的《常識》具有鮮明的論戰色彩，抨擊世襲君主制本身荒謬可笑，並嘲諷英王喬治三世為「皇家野獸」；其猛烈好鬥的文風，在1776年促使數以千計猶豫不決的殖民地居民轉而支持獨立大業。","as":"Her polemical essay attacked the complacent assumptions of mainstream economists, but critics argued that its sweeping claims were too diffuse to persuade anyone not already inclined to agree, and that its rhetorical flourishes obscured her evidence.","at":"她那篇論戰性的文章抨擊主流經濟學家自滿的假設，但批評者認為，文中籠統的主張太過散漫，無法說服原本就不傾向認同的人，而且修辭上的華麗詞藻也掩蓋了她的論證依據。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Generosity and Extravagance","themeZh":"慷慨與揮霍","cards":[{"w":"prodigal","p":"adj.","d":"Spending money or resources wastefully and recklessly.","c":"揮霍的；浪費的","s":"The Spanish crown's prodigal use of the silver shipped from Potosí during the sixteenth century, spent on endless wars and extravagant court ceremonies rather than on domestic industry, helps explain why Spain repeatedly declared bankruptcy despite controlling one of the richest mines in history.","t":"十六世紀時，西班牙王室揮霍從波托西運回的白銀，將其花在連綿不斷的戰爭和奢華的宮廷儀式上，而非發展本國產業，這有助於解釋為何西班牙雖然掌控著史上最富饒的銀礦之一，卻仍一再宣告破產。","as":"The prodigal heir mocked his father's careful habits, yet after years of ostentatious parties and pretentious art purchases, he was forced to appease his creditors by selling the family estate.","at":"這位揮霍無度的繼承人嘲笑父親謹慎持家的習慣，然而在多年舉辦浮華派對、購買附庸風雅的藝術品之後，他不得不變賣家族莊園來安撫債主。"},{"w":"altruistic","p":"adj.","d":"Showing selfless concern for the well-being of others.","c":"利他的；無私的","s":"Biologists long puzzled over the altruistic behavior of vampire bats, which regurgitate blood meals to feed hungry roostmates that would otherwise starve, until field studies revealed that individuals who share food are more likely to receive help themselves when they fail to find prey.","t":"生物學家長久以來對吸血蝙蝠的利他行為感到不解：牠們會反芻吸食到的血液，餵養原本會餓死的飢餓同伴；直到野外研究揭示，願意分享食物的個體在自己覓食失敗時，也更有可能得到幫助。","as":"Although the billionaire described her donation as purely altruistic, skeptics pointed to the ostentatious press conference, the egotistical speech that accompanied it, and the pretentious gold plaque bearing her name as evidence that vanity, not generosity, was her true motive.","at":"雖然這位億萬富翁形容她的捐款完全出於無私，但懷疑者指出那場浮華的記者會、伴隨而來的自我吹捧演說，以及刻有她名字的俗麗金色牌匾，認為這些都證明她真正的動機是虛榮而非慷慨。"},{"w":"magnanimous","p":"adj.","d":"Generous and forgiving, especially toward a rival or enemy.","c":"寬宏大量的；寬大的","s":"Rather than humiliating the defeated Confederate soldiers at Appomattox in 1865, Ulysses S. Grant was remarkably magnanimous, allowing them to keep their horses for spring planting and ordering his own troops to share rations with their starving former enemies.","t":"1865年在阿波馬托克斯，尤利西斯·格蘭特並未羞辱戰敗的南方邦聯士兵，反而展現了非凡的寬宏大量：他允許他們保留馬匹以便春耕，並下令自己的部隊與這些飢腸轆轆的昔日敵人分享口糧。","as":"The magnanimous debate champion refused to swagger after her victory; instead she offered her defeated rival a cordial embrace and praised her opponent's eloquence in a speech so gracious that it seemed to mollify even the most partisan fans.","at":"這位寬宏大量的辯論冠軍在勝利後並未趾高氣揚，而是給了落敗的對手一個熱情的擁抱，並在演說中讚揚對方的雄辯口才；她的言辭如此得體，似乎連最偏激的支持者都被安撫下來。"},{"w":"munificent","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely generous in giving money or gifts.","c":"慷慨的；大方的","s":"Andrew Carnegie's munificent funding of public libraries—more than 2,500 buildings constructed across the English-speaking world between 1883 and 1929—transformed access to books in small towns that had never before been able to afford a collection open to ordinary readers.","t":"安德魯·卡內基慷慨捐助公共圖書館——1883年至1929年間在英語世界興建了兩千五百多座——徹底改變了小城鎮取得書籍的管道，這些城鎮過去從未負擔得起一座向一般讀者開放的藏書館。","as":"The munificent endowment from the anonymous donor did much to alleviate the university's budget crisis, though some faculty were wary of the reticent benefactor's motives and worried that the gift might quell open debate about how research is funded.","at":"這筆來自匿名捐贈者的豐厚捐款大大緩解了大學的預算危機，不過部分教職員對這位低調寡言的捐助者動機有所提防，並擔心這份贈禮可能會壓制有關研究經費來源的公開討論。"},{"w":"benevolent","p":"adj.","d":"Kind and well-meaning; eager to help others.","c":"仁慈的；慈善的","s":"The nineteenth-century mill owner Robert Owen considered himself a benevolent employer: at his textile factory in New Lanark he refused to hire young children, opened one of Britain's first infant schools, and provided his workers with affordable housing, medical care, and evening classes.","t":"十九世紀的紡織廠主羅伯特·歐文自認是一位仁慈的雇主：他在新拉納克的紡織廠拒絕雇用年幼的孩童，開辦了英國最早的幼兒學校之一，並為工人提供平價住宅、醫療照護和夜間課程。","as":"The benevolent queen tried to ameliorate the suffering of her poorest subjects, but her haughty ministers dismissed such reforms with disdainful remarks, and their supercilious attitude eventually provoked a popular uprising.","at":"這位仁慈的女王試圖改善最貧困子民的苦難，但她那些傲慢的大臣卻以輕蔑的言論駁斥這些改革，而他們目中無人的態度最終激起了民眾起義。"},{"w":"largess","p":"n.","d":"Generous giving of money or gifts to others.","c":"慷慨贈與；慷慨","s":"Roman emperors cultivated popularity through public largess, distributing free grain to hundreds of thousands of citizens and funding spectacular gladiatorial games—a strategy the satirist Juvenal mocked as 'bread and circuses,' arguing that it kept the populace content while stripping it of political power.","t":"羅馬皇帝透過公開的慷慨施予來博取民心，向數十萬公民發放免費穀物，並資助壯觀的角鬥士競技——諷刺作家尤維納利斯譏之為「麵包與馬戲」，認為這種手段讓民眾心滿意足，卻剝奪了他們的政治權力。","as":"The tycoon's largess was legendary, but his ostentatious charity galas and grandiloquent speeches about civic duty struck many observers as a calculated way to placate critics of his company's labor practices.","at":"這位大亨的慷慨贈與堪稱傳奇，但他浮華的慈善晚宴和關於公民責任的浮誇演說，在許多觀察者看來，只是為了安撫那些批評其公司勞工政策的人而精心盤算的手段。"},{"w":"lavish","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely generous or extravagant in giving or spending.","c":"慷慨的；奢華的","s":"Critics of the 2014 Winter Olympics in Sochi pointed to the lavish spending on the games—an estimated fifty billion dollars, much of it devoted to roads, stadiums, and luxury hotels that now sit largely empty—as evidence that the event served political prestige more than athletics.","t":"2014年索契冬季奧運的批評者指出，這屆奧運的花費極其奢華——估計高達五百億美元，大部分用於興建如今大多閒置的道路、體育場和豪華飯店——證明這場盛會服務政治聲望的成分多過服務體育。","as":"The director praised her cast with lavish compliments, but critics found the film itself lackluster, its dialogue full of trite sentiments and its plot so derivative that it seemed assembled from scraps of older movies.","at":"導演對演員們讚不絕口，但影評人卻認為這部電影本身平淡乏味，對白充滿陳腐的情感，情節更是毫無新意，彷彿是用舊電影的片段拼湊而成的。"},{"w":"philanthropic","p":"adj.","d":"Seeking to promote others' welfare through generous donations.","c":"慈善的；博愛的","s":"John D. Rockefeller's philanthropic campaign against hookworm in the American South, launched in 1909, funded free testing, treatment, and sanitation programs for hundreds of thousands of people and is now regarded as a model for modern public-health initiatives.","t":"約翰·洛克斐勒於1909年在美國南方發起的慈善防治鉤蟲運動，資助數十萬人接受免費檢驗、治療與衛生改善計畫，如今被視為現代公共衛生倡議的典範。","as":"The philanthropic foundation tried to mitigate the effects of the drought, but its well-meaning director was criticized for issuing verbose reports and banal press releases instead of delivering food quickly to the villages most affected.","at":"這個慈善基金會試圖減輕乾旱帶來的衝擊，但其立意良善的負責人卻因只發表冗長的報告和陳腔濫調的新聞稿，而非迅速將糧食送往受災最嚴重的村莊，而遭到批評。"},{"w":"squander","p":"v.","d":"To waste money, time, or opportunities carelessly.","c":"揮霍；浪費","s":"Economists who study resource-rich nations describe a 'resource curse' in which governments squander windfall oil revenues on prestige projects and political patronage rather than investing in education and infrastructure, leaving their economies dangerously dependent on a single commodity whose price can collapse overnight.","t":"研究資源豐富國家的經濟學家描述了一種「資源詛咒」：政府把意外得來的石油收入揮霍在面子工程和政治酬庸上，而非投資於教育與基礎建設，導致經濟危險地依賴單一商品，而該商品的價格可能一夜之間崩跌。","as":"The team squandered a twenty-point lead, and the coach's terse postgame comments did little to assuage angry fans, who found his platitudes about 'learning from adversity' as insipid as the team's second-half performance.","at":"球隊揮霍掉二十分的領先優勢，而教練賽後簡短生硬的評論也幾乎無法平息球迷的怒氣；球迷覺得他那些「從逆境中學習」的陳腔濫調，就跟球隊下半場的表現一樣乏味。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Stinginess and Thrift","themeZh":"吝嗇與節儉","cards":[{"w":"frugal","p":"adj.","d":"Careful and sparing in spending money or using resources.","c":"節儉的；儉樸的","s":"Benjamin Franklin's Poor Richard's Almanack urged colonial readers to be frugal, filling its pages with maxims such as 'A penny saved is two pence clear,' and Franklin himself claimed that careful economy in his youth had allowed him to retire from printing at forty-two.","t":"班傑明·富蘭克林的《窮理查年鑑》勸誡殖民地讀者要節儉，書中充滿「省下一便士，等於淨賺兩便士」之類的格言；富蘭克林本人也聲稱，年輕時的精打細算讓他在四十二歲就得以從印刷業退休。","as":"Although the family was famously frugal, the parents were lavish with praise and affable with every visitor, and their magnanimous spirit helped their children resist the ostentatious habits of wealthier classmates.","at":"雖然這家人以節儉出名，但父母從不吝於讚美，對每位訪客也都和藹可親；他們寬厚的胸襟幫助孩子們抵擋了家境較富裕同學那種炫富的習氣。"},{"w":"parsimonious","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely unwilling to spend money; excessively stingy.","c":"吝嗇的；極度節儉的","s":"Historians of the Irish Famine criticize the British Treasury's parsimonious approach to relief: officials under Charles Trevelyan, determined to keep public spending to a minimum, closed food depots and insisted that the starving work on public projects for meager wages.","t":"研究愛爾蘭大饑荒的歷史學家批評英國財政部在救濟上極度吝嗇：查爾斯·屈維廉手下的官員為了將公共支出壓到最低，關閉了糧食供應站，並堅持要飢民從事公共工程以換取微薄工資。","as":"The parsimonious landlord refused to repair the leaking roof, and his laconic, contemptuous replies to tenants' complaints only intensified their animosity until they organized a citywide rent strike that drew national attention.","at":"這位吝嗇的房東拒絕修理漏水的屋頂，而他對房客抱怨所作的簡短又輕蔑的回應，只讓房客的敵意愈來愈深，最後他們組織了一場引起全國關注的全市性拒繳房租行動。"},{"w":"avarice","p":"n.","d":"Extreme greed for money or material wealth.","c":"貪婪；貪財","s":"In Dante's Inferno, souls guilty of avarice are condemned to the fourth circle, where they push enormous weights in endless collisions with the spendthrifts—a punishment suggesting that hoarding wealth and wasting it recklessly are two sides of the same sin.","t":"在但丁的《地獄篇》中，犯下貪婪之罪的靈魂被打入第四層地獄，在那裡推著巨大的重物，與揮霍者無止境地相互碰撞——這種懲罰暗示，囤積財富與肆意揮霍其實是同一種罪的兩面。","as":"The documentary portrayed the CEO's avarice as the root of the scandal, showing how his arrogant disregard for regulations and his ostentatious lifestyle were funded by schemes that defrauded thousands of complacent investors.","at":"這部紀錄片將執行長的貪婪描繪為醜聞的根源，呈現出他對法規傲慢的漠視與奢華炫富的生活方式，如何靠著詐騙數千名掉以輕心的投資人的計謀來支撐。"},{"w":"austere","p":"adj.","d":"Severely simple and plain, without comfort or luxury.","c":"簡樸的；樸素的；嚴峻的","s":"The Shakers, a religious community that flourished in nineteenth-century America, built furniture of deliberately austeredesign—chairs and cabinets without carving, inlay, or ornament—believing that plain, useful objects reflected spiritual purity, and collectors now prize these simple pieces for their elegant restraint.","t":"震顫派是十九世紀在美國興盛的宗教團體，他們刻意以簡樸的設計製作家具——椅子和櫥櫃上沒有雕刻、鑲嵌或任何裝飾——相信樸實實用的器物能反映心靈的純淨；如今收藏家珍視這些簡單作品所展現的優雅節制。","as":"The monastery's austere routine of silence, fasting, and prayer appealed to the taciturn novelist, who had grown weary of the city's garrulous literary parties, its pretentious critics, and the endless pressure to promote his books.","at":"修道院裡靜默、禁食與祈禱的簡樸作息，深深吸引了這位沉默寡言的小說家，因為他早已厭倦了城市裡喋喋不休的文學派對、裝腔作勢的評論家，以及無止境的新書宣傳壓力。"},{"w":"mercenary","p":"adj.","d":"Motivated chiefly by a desire for money or gain.","c":"唯利是圖的；圖利的","s":"Critics accused the pharmaceutical company of purely mercenary motives when it raised the price of a decades-old antiparasitic drug from about thirteen dollars to $750 per pill overnight, arguing that its executives cared only about profits and not at all about the vulnerable patients who depended on the medicine.","t":"當這家製藥公司一夜之間將一種已有數十年歷史的抗寄生蟲藥物，從每顆約十三美元調漲到七百五十美元時，批評者指責該公司純粹出於唯利是圖的動機，認為其高層只在乎利潤，完全不顧依賴這種藥物的弱勢病患。","as":"Some historians portray the explorer as a mercenary adventurer, but others argue that his altruistic work among the sick and his magnanimous treatment of captured enemies complicate such a hackneyed caricature.","at":"有些歷史學家把這位探險家描繪成唯利是圖的冒險者，但也有人認為，他照顧病患的無私工作以及寬待被俘敵人的寬大胸襟，使這種老套的醜化形象難以成立。"},{"w":"miserly","p":"adj.","d":"Unwilling to spend money, like a miser.","c":"吝嗇的；小氣的","s":"Hetty Green, once considered the richest woman in America, was so miserly that she reportedly wore the same black dress until it fell apart, ate cold oatmeal to avoid heating costs, and delayed treatment for her son's injured leg while searching for a free clinic.","t":"海蒂·格林曾被視為美國最富有的女性，據說她吝嗇到同一件黑色洋裝一直穿到破爛為止、為了省下加熱的費用而吃冷燕麥粥，還為了尋找免費診所而延誤兒子腿傷的治療。","as":"The museum's miserly acquisitions budget forced the curators to rely on donors' largess, and their obsequious letters to wealthy patrons, full of grandiloquent flattery, struck younger staff as a humiliating way to appease the board.","at":"博物館吝嗇的典藏預算迫使策展人仰賴捐贈者的慷慨解囊，而他們寫給富有贊助人那些充滿浮誇奉承之詞的諂媚信件，在年輕員工看來，只是一種為了討好董事會而自取其辱的做法。"},{"w":"penurious","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely stingy and unwilling to spend money.","c":"吝嗇的；一毛不拔的","s":"Though he had amassed a fortune as a shipping magnate, the old man remained so penurious that he paid his household staff below the legal wage, refused to replace the cracked windows of his mansion, and kept detailed ledgers recording every candle his servants burned.","t":"雖然這位老人身為航運大亨累積了巨額財富，他卻依然吝嗇到極點：付給家中僕役的工資低於法定標準，拒絕更換豪宅裡破裂的窗戶，還記了詳細的帳簿，記錄僕人們點過的每一根蠟燭。","as":"The penurious publisher paid his translators so little that only the most desperate would accept his contracts, and his terse, disdainful refusals to renegotiate earned him a reputation as an insolent bully throughout the industry.","at":"這位吝嗇的出版商付給譯者的稿酬少得可憐，只有走投無路的人才會接受他的合約；而他每次都以簡短又輕蔑的態度拒絕重新談判，使他在整個業界落得蠻橫無禮的惡霸名聲。"},{"w":"thrifty","p":"adj.","d":"Using money and resources carefully and without waste.","c":"節儉的；精打細算的","s":"Researchers studying household finances in postwar Japan found that thrifty families, who saved nearly a fifth of their income by buying secondhand goods, cooking at home, and avoiding consumer debt, supplied much of the capital that banks lent to the rapidly expanding manufacturing sector.","t":"研究戰後日本家庭財務的學者發現，那些節儉的家庭透過購買二手物品、在家烹飪以及避免消費性借貸，存下將近五分之一的收入，為銀行貸給迅速擴張的製造業的資金提供了大部分來源。","as":"The thrifty couple avoided the ostentatious weddings fashionable among their friends, preferring a convivial dinner for a few relatives, and they politely ignored the haughty remarks of guests who considered such simplicity a sign of poverty.","at":"這對節儉的夫妻避開了朋友間流行的鋪張婚禮，寧可為幾位親戚辦一場歡樂溫馨的晚宴；對於那些把這種簡樸視為窮酸象徵的賓客所發表的傲慢言論，他們也禮貌地置之不理。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Trouble and Confusion","themeZh":"困境與混亂","cards":[{"w":"adversity","p":"n.","d":"Serious difficulty or misfortune.","c":"逆境；困境","s":"Studies of children who grew up during the Great Depression found that many developed remarkable resilience: having endured hunger, unemployment in the family, and frequent moves in search of work, they later reported that early adversity had taught them resourcefulness and a deep appreciation for financial security.","t":"針對在經濟大蕭條期間成長的孩童所做的研究發現，許多人培養出非凡的韌性：他們經歷過飢餓、家人失業，以及為了找工作而頻繁搬家，後來表示，早年的逆境教會了他們隨機應變，也讓他們深深珍惜經濟上的安穩。","as":"In the face of adversity, the frugal immigrant family refused to squander their meager savings, and their quiet, stoical perseverance eventually allowed them to open a bakery whose convivial atmosphere made it a neighborhood landmark.","at":"面對逆境，這個節儉的移民家庭拒絕揮霍他們微薄的積蓄，而他們默默堅忍的毅力，最終讓他們開了一家麵包店，店裡歡樂溫馨的氣氛使它成為社區的地標。"},{"w":"conflagration","p":"n.","d":"A large and destructive fire.","c":"大火；大火災","s":"The Great Chicago Fire of 1871 began in a small barn on the city's southwest side, but strong winds, a long drought, and densely packed wooden buildings turned it into a conflagration that burned for two days, destroyed more than 17,000 structures, and left roughly 100,000 residents homeless.","t":"1871年的芝加哥大火起初只是城市西南側一座小穀倉裡的火苗，但強風、長期乾旱以及密集的木造建築，使它演變成一場延燒兩天的大火，燒毀了一萬七千多棟建築物，約十萬名居民因而無家可歸。","as":"After the conflagration destroyed the old quarter, the mayor's grandiloquent promises to rebuild did little to mollify residents, and his ostentatious ribbon-cutting ceremonies only deepened their animosity toward city hall.","at":"大火燒毀舊城區後，市長浮誇的重建承諾幾乎無法安撫居民，而他那些鋪張的剪綵典禮，更加深了民眾對市政府的敵意。"},{"w":"confounding","p":"adj.","d":"Causing surprise and confusion; baffling.","c":"令人困惑的；費解的","s":"For decades, astronomers found the rotation of spiral galaxies deeply confounding: stars at the outer edges were orbiting just as fast as those near the center, a pattern that contradicted Newtonian predictions and eventually led researchers to propose the existence of invisible dark matter.","t":"數十年來，天文學家一直對螺旋星系的自轉現象深感困惑：位於外緣的恆星繞行速度竟與靠近中心的恆星一樣快，這種模式與牛頓力學的預測相矛盾，最終促使研究人員提出看不見的暗物質存在的假說。","as":"The novel's confounding final chapter, in which the narrator constantly digresses into unexplained symbols, frustrated reviewers who had praised the succinct style of the author's earlier books, though a few defended the ending as a deliberate rejection of prosaic, hackneyed storytelling.","at":"這部小說令人費解的最後一章中，敘事者不斷離題，轉向一些未加解釋的象徵，令曾經讚揚作者早期作品簡潔文風的評論家大感失望；不過也有少數人為這個結局辯護，認為它是有意拒絕平淡陳腐的敘事方式。"},{"w":"debacle","p":"n.","d":"A sudden and complete failure; a fiasco.","c":"慘敗；大失敗","s":"The 1961 Bay of Pigs invasion, in which some 1,400 CIA-trained Cuban exiles were overwhelmed by Castro's forces within three days, proved such a debacle for the Kennedy administration that the president publicly accepted responsibility and quietly forced the CIA's director to resign.","t":"1961年的豬玀灣入侵事件中，約一千四百名受中央情報局訓練的古巴流亡者在三天內就被卡斯楚的部隊擊潰，這對甘迺迪政府而言是一場慘敗，總統不得不公開承擔責任，並悄悄迫使中情局局長辭職。","as":"The product launch was a debacle: the company's ostentatious marketing campaign had promised a revolution, but reviewers found the device insipid and its software so derivative that executives could not placate furious investors.","at":"這次產品發表是一場大失敗：公司浮誇的行銷活動號稱將掀起一場革命，但評論者卻認為這款裝置平淡乏味，軟體也毫無新意，主管們根本無法安撫憤怒的投資人。"},{"w":"cryptic","p":"adj.","d":"Mysterious or obscure in meaning; puzzling.","c":"隱晦的；神秘難解的","s":"Emily Dickinson's poems puzzled her first editors, who found many lines so cryptic—full of unconventional dashes, compressed metaphors, and abrupt shifts in thought—that they altered her punctuation and wording before publication in 1890, changes that later scholars painstakingly reversed.","t":"艾蜜莉·狄金生的詩作讓她最初的編輯們大感困惑，他們發現許多詩句十分隱晦——充滿非傳統的破折號、高度濃縮的隱喻和突如其來的思緒轉折——因此在1890年出版前更動了她的標點和用字，而這些修改後來被學者們費盡心力地還原。","as":"The spy's cryptic message was deliberately terse, but the analysts, wary of reading too much into a single phrase, refused to digress into speculation and instead compared it with dozens of earlier, equally laconic transmissions.","at":"這名間諜的隱晦訊息刻意寫得極為簡短，但分析人員擔心對單一詞句過度解讀，因此拒絕偏離主題去臆測，而是拿它與數十則先前同樣言簡意賅的傳訊相互比對。"},{"w":"enigma","p":"n.","d":"A person or thing that is mysterious or hard to understand.","c":"謎；難以理解的人或事","s":"Despite centuries of speculation, the purpose of Stonehenge remains an enigma: archaeologists have variously interpreted the massive stone circle as a solar calendar, a burial site, a place of healing, and a monument uniting distant communities, yet no single theory accounts for all the evidence.","t":"儘管人們推測了好幾個世紀，巨石陣的用途至今仍是個謎：考古學家曾分別將這座巨大的石圈解讀為太陽曆、墓葬地、療癒之所，以及聯合遠方社群的紀念建築，但沒有任何單一理論能解釋所有證據。","as":"To his biographers the reclusive composer remains an enigma: he was taciturn in public and disdainful of interviews, yet his private letters reveal a voluble, jocular man who delighted in gossip about his rivals.","at":"對傳記作家而言，這位離群索居的作曲家至今仍是個謎：他在公開場合沉默寡言，對訪談不屑一顧，然而他的私人信件卻顯示他是個健談、詼諧，又熱衷於談論對手八卦的人。"},{"w":"labyrinth","p":"n.","d":"A complicated network of winding passages; a maze.","c":"迷宮；錯綜複雜的事物","s":"The medina of Fez, one of the largest car-free urban areas in the world, is a labyrinth of more than nine thousand narrow, winding alleys, many of them dead ends, and even lifelong residents sometimes rely on landmarks such as fountains and mosques to find their way.","t":"非斯舊城是世界上最大的無車都市區之一，由九千多條狹窄蜿蜒的巷弄構成，宛如一座迷宮，其中許多巷子是死路，就連土生土長的居民有時也得靠噴泉、清真寺等地標來辨認方向。","as":"The tax code has become a labyrinth of exceptions and loopholes, and critics argue that its verbose regulations, written in grandiloquent legal jargon rather than concise language, benefit only wealthy taxpayers who can afford expert guides.","at":"稅法已成為一座充滿例外條款與漏洞的迷宮，批評者認為，那些以浮誇的法律術語而非簡潔語言寫成的冗長法規，只對負擔得起專業顧問的富裕納稅人有利。"},{"w":"quandary","p":"n.","d":"A state of uncertainty about what to do; a dilemma.","c":"困惑；進退兩難","s":"Doctors treating the elderly patient faced an ethical quandary: an aggressive surgery might extend her life by several years but carried a high risk of complications, while a gentler course of medication would preserve her comfort but almost certainly allow the cancer to spread.","t":"為這位年長病患治療的醫生們陷入了倫理上的兩難：積極的手術或許能延長她數年壽命，但併發症風險很高；而較溫和的藥物療法雖能保持她的舒適，卻幾乎必然會讓癌症擴散。","as":"The regulators were in a quandary: if they tried to placate the angry public with strict new rules, they might squander the fragile goodwill of the industry, yet a complacent response would only intensify public animosity.","at":"監管機關陷入兩難：如果他們試圖以嚴格的新規定安撫憤怒的民眾，可能會揮霍掉業界脆弱的善意；然而若是回應得自滿怠慢，只會加深民眾的敵意。"},{"w":"precarious","p":"adj.","d":"Dangerously unstable or uncertain; likely to collapse.","c":"不穩定的；岌岌可危的","s":"Many gig-economy workers describe their livelihoods as deeply precarious: without guaranteed hours, health insurance, or protection against sudden termination, a single slow month or minor illness can leave them unable to pay rent, and few have savings to cushion such shocks.","t":"許多零工經濟的勞工形容自己的生計極不穩定：由於沒有保障的工時、健康保險，也不受突然解雇的保護，只要一個月生意清淡或生一場小病，就可能讓他們付不出房租，而且很少人有積蓄可以緩衝這類衝擊。","as":"The ceasefire remained precarious, and diplomats worked to conciliate the bellicose factions on both sides, knowing that a single insolent remark from either commander could reignite the fighting along the disputed border.","at":"停火協議依然岌岌可危，外交官們努力安撫雙方好戰的派系，因為他們知道，只要任何一方指揮官說出一句無禮的話，就可能讓爭議邊界沿線的戰火再度燃起。"},{"w":"turbulence","p":"n.","d":"A state of violent disorder, unrest, or instability.","c":"動盪；騷亂","s":"The year 1848 brought such political turbulence to Europe—barricades in Paris, uprisings in Vienna and Berlin, and nationalist revolts in Hungary and Italy—that conservative governments, once restored to power, responded with censorship, secret police, and the suppression of liberal newspapers.","t":"1848年為歐洲帶來了極大的政治動盪——巴黎街頭築起街壘，維也納和柏林爆發起義，匈牙利和義大利也掀起民族主義叛亂——以致保守派政府在恢復權力後，以審查制度、秘密警察和查禁自由派報紙作為回應。","as":"During the financial turbulence of 2008, the central bank tried to allay public fears with a succinct statement, but commentators found its tone complacent, and a few even accused officials of a haughty disregard for ordinary savers.","at":"在2008年的金融動盪期間，央行試圖以一份簡明扼要的聲明來平息大眾的恐慌，但評論員認為其語氣自滿，有些人甚至指責官員們對一般存款戶抱持傲慢漠視的態度。"},{"w":"turmoil","p":"n.","d":"A state of great confusion, disturbance, or uncertainty.","c":"混亂；騷動","s":"In the years after the 1929 stock market crash, the American banking system was thrown into turmoil as panicked depositors rushed to withdraw their savings, thousands of banks collapsed, and the absence of federal deposit insurance meant that many families lost everything they had saved.","t":"1929年股市崩盤後的幾年裡，美國銀行體系陷入一片混亂：驚慌的存戶爭相提領存款，數以千計的銀行倒閉，而由於缺乏聯邦存款保險，許多家庭因此失去了所有積蓄。","as":"Amid the turmoil of the election, the candidate tried to pacify voters with mundane promises about road repairs, but his rivals' pugnacious attacks and the voluble protests in the streets drowned out his message.","at":"在選舉的一片混亂中，這位候選人試圖用修路之類平凡無奇的承諾來安撫選民，但對手好鬥的攻擊以及街頭喧嚷不休的抗議聲，完全淹沒了他的訴求。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Harmful and Wicked","themeZh":"有害與邪惡","cards":[{"w":"detrimental","p":"adj.","d":"Tending to cause harm or damage.","c":"有害的；不利的","s":"Ecologists monitoring the coastal estuary found that runoff from upstream fertilizer use was detrimental to the native oyster beds: the excess nitrogen triggered algal blooms that depleted dissolved oxygen, and within five years the harvest had fallen by more than half.","t":"監測沿海河口的生態學家發現，上游施用肥料所產生的逕流對當地原生的牡蠣床有害：過量的氮引發藻華，耗盡水中的溶氧，五年內牡蠣產量便減少了一半以上。","as":"Economists warned that the government's prodigal spending, though intended to alleviate the immediate turmoil of the recession, could prove detrimental in the long run by leaving the nation in a precarious fiscal position.","at":"經濟學家警告，政府揮霍無度的支出雖然意在緩解經濟衰退帶來的眼前動盪，長遠來看卻可能造成損害，使國家陷入岌岌可危的財政處境。"},{"w":"devious","p":"adj.","d":"Using dishonest or underhanded tricks to get what one wants.","c":"狡詐的；不正當的","s":"Investigative reporters eventually exposed the lobbyist's devious strategy: rather than openly opposing the clean-air bill, he quietly funded a network of seemingly independent citizen groups that flooded legislators with letters claiming the regulations would destroy local jobs.","t":"調查記者最終揭露了這名說客的狡詐策略：他並未公開反對這項清淨空氣法案，而是暗中資助一個看似獨立的公民團體網絡，讓這些團體寄出大量信件給議員，聲稱這些法規將摧毀地方的就業機會。","as":"In the chronicle, the devious courtier learns to placate the haughty king with lavish flattery while covertly spreading rumors that deepen the animosity between rival noble families, ensuring that no one notices his own steady rise to power.","at":"在這部編年史中，那位狡詐的朝臣學會用大量的奉承安撫傲慢的國王，同時暗中散播謠言，加深敵對貴族家族之間的仇恨，確保沒有人察覺他自己正穩步掌權。"},{"w":"iniquitous","p":"adj.","d":"Grossly unfair and morally wrong.","c":"極不公正的；邪惡的","s":"Nineteenth-century reformers denounced the iniquitous system of debtors' prisons, in which impoverished families could be jailed indefinitely for small debts, often unable to earn the very money they needed to secure their release.","t":"十九世紀的改革者譴責極不公正的債務人監獄制度：在這種制度下，貧困家庭可能因小額債務而遭無限期監禁，往往無法賺得換取自由所需的那筆錢。","as":"Charles Dickens, whose father was imprisoned for debt, wrote with impassioned eloquence about the iniquitous treatment of the poor, contrasting the ostentatious wealth of factory owners with the penurious lives of the children who labored for them.","at":"父親曾因負債入獄的狄更斯，以慷慨激昂的雄辯描寫窮人所受的不公待遇，將工廠老闆炫耀的財富與替他們做工的童工貧困的生活形成對比。"},{"w":"pernicious","p":"adj.","d":"Causing great harm, often gradually and unnoticed.","c":"有害的；潛移默化地危害的","s":"Public health officials consider lead contamination especially pernicious because its effects are invisible at first: children exposed to old paint or corroded pipes may show no symptoms for years, even as the metal steadily impairs their cognitive development and attention span.","t":"公共衛生官員認為鉛污染特別有害，因為它的影響起初難以察覺：接觸老舊油漆或鏽蝕水管的兒童可能多年毫無症狀，而這種金屬卻持續損害他們的認知發展與專注力。","as":"The historian argued that the most pernicious legacy of the war was not the conflagration that leveled the capital but the lingering animosity between neighboring communities, a turmoil of suspicion that no treaty could quell.","at":"這位歷史學家認為，這場戰爭最有害的遺緒並非夷平首都的那場大火，而是鄰近社群之間揮之不去的仇恨——一種任何條約都無法平息的猜疑與動盪。"},{"w":"ominous","p":"adj.","d":"Suggesting that something bad is about to happen.","c":"不祥的；預示凶兆的","s":"Seismologists grew alarmed when the volcano's usual tremors gave way to an ominous silence, accompanied by a rapid swelling of its northern flank, signs that magma was accumulating beneath the surface faster than it could escape.","t":"火山平常的震動轉變為一片不祥的寂靜，同時北側山坡迅速隆起，地震學家因此深感警覺，因為這些跡象顯示岩漿在地表下累積的速度超過了它能釋出的速度。","as":"The ominous headlines about a banking debacle prompted even the most complacent investors to sell their shares, and the resulting turbulence in the markets bewildered economists who had predicted a long period of quiescent markets and steady growth.","at":"關於銀行業崩盤的不祥頭條，促使連最自滿的投資人也拋售持股，隨之而來的市場動盪讓原本預測市場將長期平靜、經濟穩定成長的經濟學家大感困惑。"},{"w":"nefarious","p":"adj.","d":"Wicked, criminal, or villainous in nature.","c":"邪惡的；不法的","s":"Interpol agents spent three years tracing the smuggling ring's nefarious activities, which included forging export permits, bribing customs officials, and trafficking looted antiquities from war zones to private collectors in Europe and Asia.","t":"國際刑警組織的探員花了三年追查這個走私集團的不法勾當，包括偽造出口許可證、賄賂海關官員，以及將戰區遭掠奪的古物販運給歐洲與亞洲的私人收藏家。","as":"The documentary portrays the nefarious hackers not as cryptic geniuses but as mercenary opportunists, motivated purely by avarice and indifferent to the hospitals whose computer systems they crippled during the worst months of the pandemic.","at":"這部紀錄片並未把那些邪惡的駭客描繪成神祕難解的天才，而是唯利是圖的投機分子，他們純粹受貪婪驅使，對於在疫情最嚴峻的幾個月裡遭他們癱瘓電腦系統的醫院漠不關心。"},{"w":"virulent","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely harmful or infectious; bitterly hostile.","c":"劇毒的；惡毒的","s":"Epidemiologists were alarmed that the new strain proved far more virulent than its predecessors, spreading through an entire hospital ward within days and causing severe pneumonia even in young patients with no underlying medical conditions.","t":"流行病學家深感憂慮，因為這株新病毒的毒性遠比先前的病株強，數天之內就傳遍整個病房，甚至讓沒有任何潛在疾病的年輕病患罹患嚴重的肺炎。","as":"The critic's virulent review, a rant that mocked the young composer's symphony as derivative and banal, provoked a contentious debate about whether reviewers should temper their judgments when assessing a debut.","at":"這位評論家惡毒的樂評簡直是一篇謾罵，嘲諷這位年輕作曲家的交響曲抄襲模仿又陳腐平庸，引發了一場激烈的爭論：評論者在評價新人的首部作品時，是否應該緩和自己的批判。"},{"w":"deleterious","p":"adj.","d":"Causing harm or damage, especially to health.","c":"有害的；有損健康的","s":"Although the herbicide was initially praised for boosting crop yields, later studies revealed its deleterious effects on pollinators: even trace amounts impaired the navigation abilities of honeybees, preventing many from finding their way back to the hive.","t":"這種除草劑起初因能提高作物產量而備受讚揚，但後來的研究揭露了它對授粉昆蟲的有害影響：即使只是微量，也會損害蜜蜂的導航能力，使許多蜜蜂找不到回巢的路。","as":"Nutritionists caution that the deleterious effects of a diet heavy in sugar are often obscured by lavish advertising, which presents sweetened cereals as wholesome and dismisses scientific warnings as the alarmist prattle of overly austere critics.","at":"營養學家提醒，高糖飲食的有害影響往往被鋪天蓋地的廣告所掩蓋，這些廣告把含糖穀片包裝成健康食品，並把科學警告貶為過度嚴苛的批評者危言聳聽的胡言亂語。"},{"w":"baneful","p":"adj.","d":"Causing great harm, ruin, or destruction.","c":"有害的；毀滅性的","s":"Historians of the Irish famine emphasize the baneful consequences of relying on a single crop: when blight destroyed the potato harvests of the 1840s, roughly a million people died and another million emigrated, permanently reshaping the island's population.","t":"研究愛爾蘭大饑荒的歷史學家強調，仰賴單一作物會帶來毀滅性的後果：當枯萎病摧毀了1840年代的馬鈴薯收成，約有一百萬人死亡，另有一百萬人移居海外，永久改變了這座島嶼的人口結構。","as":"Critics of the regime described its censorship as baneful, arguing that by punishing every outspoken journalist and rewarding only hackneyed propaganda, the government had made public debate so insipid that citizens grew complacent about their own lack of freedom.","at":"該政權的批評者形容其新聞審查危害深遠，認為政府懲罰每一位敢言的記者、只獎勵陳腔濫調的宣傳，使公共討論變得索然無味，以致公民對自身缺乏自由一事變得安於現狀。"},{"w":"malicious","p":"adj.","d":"Intending to harm, upset, or damage others.","c":"惡意的；存心不良的","s":"Cybersecurity analysts traced the outage to a malicious program disguised as a routine software update; once installed, it encrypted the utility's billing records and displayed a message demanding payment in cryptocurrency before the files would be restored.","t":"資安分析師追查出這次系統中斷的源頭是一個偽裝成例行軟體更新的惡意程式；安裝後，它便將這家公用事業公司的帳單紀錄加密，並顯示訊息要求以加密貨幣付款，否則不會恢復檔案。","as":"Though the columnist claimed her remarks were merely jocular, the malicious gossip she spread about her rival's private life was so contemptuous and insolent that even her loyal readers began to question her integrity.","at":"雖然那位專欄作家聲稱她的言論只是開玩笑，但她散播關於對手私生活的惡意八卦是如此輕蔑又無禮，連她的忠實讀者也開始質疑她的人品。"},{"w":"odious","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely unpleasant and deserving hatred or disgust.","c":"可憎的；令人厭惡的","s":"Many Northern readers who had once tolerated slavery as an unfortunate economic necessity came to see it as truly odious after reading Frederick Douglass's firsthand accounts of families sold apart at auction and of laborers whipped for the smallest infractions.","t":"許多原本把奴隸制當成不幸但必要的經濟制度而予以容忍的北方讀者，在讀了道格拉斯親身記述家人在拍賣會上被拆散出售、勞工因最輕微的過失而遭鞭打的經歷後，開始認為奴隸制真正令人憎惡。","as":"The ambassador found the dictator's swagger odious, yet he chose to conciliate rather than confront him, reasoning that a cordial tone might mitigate the regime's belligerent posture toward its neighbors.","at":"這位大使覺得那名獨裁者趾高氣揚的模樣令人厭惡，但他選擇安撫而非對抗，理由是友好的語氣或許能緩和該政權對鄰國的好戰姿態。"},{"w":"rancorous","p":"adj.","d":"Marked by deep, long-lasting bitterness and resentment.","c":"積怨很深的；充滿怨恨的","s":"The partnership between the two founders, once celebrated as a model of collaboration, became so rancorous after a dispute over patent royalties that they spent the next decade suing each other and refused to appear together even at the company's anniversary celebration.","t":"這兩位創辦人的合夥關係曾被譽為合作典範，卻在一場專利權利金糾紛後變得積怨甚深，兩人在接下來的十年裡互相提告，甚至拒絕一同出席公司的週年慶祝活動。","as":"Once the budget talks collapsed over the contentious issue of taxation, the rancorous debate between the two parties degenerated into a polemical shouting match, and the negotiator, normally affable and patient, finally abandoned his efforts to appease either side.","at":"預算協商因具爭議性的稅收問題破裂後，兩黨之間積怨已深的辯論淪為一場充滿論戰火藥味的叫罵，而那位平時和藹又有耐心的協調者，最終也放棄了安撫任何一方的努力。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Criticizing and Scolding","themeZh":"批評與責備","cards":[{"w":"deprecate","p":"v.","d":"To express disapproval of; to play down as unimportant.","c":"反對；不贊成；貶低","s":"Early critics of Impressionism deprecated the movement's loose brushwork and unfinished-looking canvases, dismissing Monet's paintings as mere sketches, yet within a generation the same techniques were being taught in academies and celebrated as a revolution in the depiction of light.","t":"印象派早期的評論者對這個畫派鬆散的筆觸和看似未完成的畫作頗不以為然，把莫內的畫貶為僅是草圖；然而不到一個世代，同樣的技法便在美術學院裡傳授，並被譽為描繪光線的一場革命。","as":"The modest physicist tended to deprecate her own role in the discovery, describing it as fortuitous, yet her colleagues insisted that her meticulous methods, rather than luck, had resolved the enigma that had confounded the field for decades.","at":"這位謙虛的物理學家總是貶低自己在這項發現中的角色，稱之為幸運的巧合，但她的同事堅稱，是她一絲不苟的研究方法而非運氣，解開了困擾這個領域數十年的謎團。"},{"w":"impugn","p":"v.","d":"To challenge something as false or call it into question.","c":"質疑；抨擊","s":"During cross-examination, the defense attorney sought to impugn the expert witness's credibility by revealing that her laboratory had received substantial funding from the plaintiff's company, suggesting that her conclusions about the product's safety might not be entirely impartial.","t":"在交互詰問時，辯護律師試圖質疑專家證人的可信度，揭露她的實驗室曾獲得原告公司的大筆資助，暗示她對該產品安全性所下的結論可能並非完全公正。","as":"Rather than engage with the substance of the report, the senator chose to impugn the motives of its authors, delivering a grandiloquent and contemptuous speech that dismissed their careful findings as the work of mercenary activists.","at":"這位參議員並未針對報告的實質內容回應，而是選擇質疑撰寫者的動機，發表了一篇浮誇又輕蔑的演說，把他們嚴謹的研究結果貶為唯利是圖的運動人士之作。"},{"w":"rebuke","p":"v.","d":"To express sharp disapproval of someone's behavior.","c":"斥責；指責","s":"The United Nations Security Council formally rebuked the government for launching missile tests in defiance of international agreements, warning that further provocations would result in expanded sanctions on the country's energy exports.","t":"聯合國安理會正式譴責該國政府違反國際協議發射飛彈試射，並警告若再有挑釁行為，將擴大對該國能源出口的制裁。","as":"The editor did not hesitate to rebuke the young reporter, whose verbose and pretentious article was full of trite phrases and digressions that obscured the story's few important facts.","at":"編輯毫不猶豫地斥責這位年輕記者，因為他那篇冗長又矯揉造作的報導充滿陳腔濫調和離題的段落，掩蓋了報導中少數幾項重要事實。"},{"w":"rebuff","p":"v.","d":"To reject an offer, request, or person bluntly.","c":"斷然拒絕；冷落","s":"When the multinational corporation offered to buy the family-owned vineyard for triple its appraised value, the owners politely but firmly rebuffed the proposal, explaining that preserving their grandparents' winemaking traditions mattered more to them than any sum of money.","t":"當這家跨國企業提出以估價三倍的價格收購這座家族經營的葡萄園時，園主禮貌但堅定地回絕了這項提議，表示對他們而言，保存祖父母的釀酒傳統比任何金錢都重要。","as":"The reticent novelist would routinely rebuff journalists seeking interviews, and her terse replies were often mistaken for haughty disdain, though friends insisted that she was simply shy and found the publicity surrounding her work mundane.","at":"這位沉默寡言的小說家經常斷然拒絕前來邀訪的記者，她簡短的回覆常被誤解為高傲的輕蔑，但朋友們堅稱她只是害羞，而且覺得圍繞她作品的宣傳活動枯燥乏味。"},{"w":"reprove","p":"v.","d":"To criticize or correct someone, usually gently.","c":"責備；告誡","s":"In her letters to her son at boarding school, Abigail Adams gently reproved him for neglecting his studies of Latin and Greek, reminding him that a nation struggling to establish itself would need citizens educated well enough to govern wisely.","t":"愛碧蓋兒‧亞當斯在寫給就讀寄宿學校的兒子的信中，溫和地責備他荒廢了拉丁文與希臘文的學業，並提醒他，一個正努力立足的國家將需要受過良好教育、能明智治國的公民。","as":"The mentor would reprove her apprentices kindly rather than harshly, believing that an affable correction could ameliorate their technique more effectively than the cantankerous outbursts favored by her own former teacher.","at":"這位導師總是和善而非嚴厲地告誡學徒，她相信溫和親切的指正比起她從前老師慣用的暴躁斥責，更能有效改進他們的技藝。"},{"w":"castigate","p":"v.","d":"To criticize or punish someone severely.","c":"嚴厲批評；懲戒","s":"In a scathing editorial, the medical journal castigated the pharmaceutical firm for concealing data from its clinical trials, arguing that withholding evidence of serious side effects had placed thousands of patients at unnecessary risk.","t":"這份醫學期刊在一篇措辭尖銳的社論中嚴厲批評這家製藥公司隱瞞臨床試驗數據，指出隱匿嚴重副作用的證據使數千名病患承受了不必要的風險。","as":"Environmental groups castigated the mining company for its pernicious disregard of local ecosystems, accusing its executives of avarice and of using lavish public-relations campaigns to mollify critics while rivers turned toxic.","at":"環保團體嚴厲譴責這家礦業公司對當地生態系統的有害漠視，指責其高層貪婪無度，並在河川變得有毒之際，利用鋪張的公關活動來安撫批評者。"},{"w":"berate","p":"v.","d":"To scold someone angrily and at length.","c":"嚴厲斥責；痛罵","s":"Witnesses described how the frustrated conductor berated the orchestra for nearly twenty minutes during the rehearsal, shouting at individual players for every missed entrance until several musicians walked off the stage in protest.","t":"目擊者描述，那位氣急敗壞的指揮在排練時痛罵整個樂團將近二十分鐘，對每一個沒跟上進場拍子的樂手個別大吼，直到好幾位樂手憤而離開舞臺以示抗議。","as":"The arrogant manager would berate his staff in long, garrulous tirades, yet his outbursts did nothing to alleviate the turmoil in the department and only deepened the employees' antagonism toward him.","at":"那位傲慢的經理總是用冗長又嘮叨的長篇大論痛罵員工，但他的發作絲毫無助於緩解部門的混亂，只加深了員工對他的敵意。"},{"w":"censure","p":"v.","d":"To express formal, official disapproval of someone.","c":"（正式）譴責；責難","s":"In 1954 the United States Senate voted to censure Joseph McCarthy for conduct that brought the chamber into dishonor, a formal reprimand that effectively ended the influence of the senator whose reckless accusations of communist infiltration had ruined many careers.","t":"1954年，美國參議院表決譴責約瑟夫‧麥卡錫有損議院聲譽的行為；這項正式的懲戒實際上終結了這位參議員的影響力，他草率地指控共產黨滲透，曾毀了許多人的職業生涯。","as":"The medical board censured the physician for his presumptuous habit of prescribing experimental drugs without consent, finding that his conduct, though perhaps benevolent in intent, had placed vulnerable patients in a precarious position.","at":"醫師公會正式譴責這名醫師擅自在未經同意下開立實驗性藥物的做法，認定他的行為或許出於善意，卻使弱勢病患陷入岌岌可危的處境。"},{"w":"chastise","p":"v.","d":"To criticize or punish someone severely for wrongdoing.","c":"懲罰；嚴厲責備","s":"Puritan magistrates in colonial New England would publicly chastise residents who skipped Sunday services, sometimes confining them in wooden stocks in the town square so that their neighbors could witness the consequences of neglecting religious duty.","t":"殖民時期新英格蘭的清教徒地方官會公開懲罰缺席主日禮拜的居民，有時把他們鎖在城鎮廣場的木製足枷中，讓鄰居目睹怠忽宗教義務的下場。","as":"In his memoir the former chancellor chastised himself for having been so complacent, admitting that his austere budget, intended to mitigate the debt crisis, had instead deepened the adversity of the poorest citizens.","at":"這位前財政大臣在回憶錄中自責當年太過自滿，承認他那份原本要緩解債務危機的緊縮預算，反而加深了最貧困公民的困境。"},{"w":"upbraid","p":"v.","d":"To scold or criticize someone sharply and bitterly.","c":"嚴厲責罵；申斥","s":"In the final act of the play, the aging king upbraids his eldest daughter for her ingratitude, condemning her in a furious speech for repaying years of generosity with cruelty and contempt.","t":"在劇本的最後一幕，年邁的國王嚴厲責罵長女忘恩負義，以一段憤怒的獨白痛斥她以殘酷與輕蔑回報他多年來的慷慨。","as":"Rather than placate the protesters, the governor chose to upbraid them as insolent troublemakers, a bellicose response that only intensified their animosity and turned a peaceful demonstration into prolonged turmoil.","at":"州長沒有安撫抗議群眾，反而嚴厲斥責他們是無禮的滋事分子；這種好鬥的回應只加深了他們的敵意，使一場和平的示威演變成長期的動盪。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Indifferent and Unemotional","themeZh":"冷漠與不動聲色","cards":[{"w":"detached","p":"adj.","d":"Not emotionally involved; aloof or objective.","c":"超然的；冷漠的；不帶感情的","s":"Anthropologists are trained to remain detached while conducting fieldwork, recording rituals and customs without judging them by the standards of their own culture, although many admit that years of living within a community make such objectivity difficult to sustain.","t":"人類學家受過訓練，在進行田野調查時要保持超然客觀，記錄各種儀式與習俗而不以自身文化的標準加以評判；不過許多人也承認，在一個社群中生活多年後，很難一直維持這種客觀。","as":"The narrator's detached voice, terse and almost clinical, describes the family's adversity without sentiment, a technique that critics once dismissed as vapid but now praise for making the novel's quiet tragedies all the more poignant.","at":"敘事者超然冷靜的口吻簡潔得近乎臨床記錄，毫不煽情地描述這個家庭的苦難；評論家曾把這種手法斥為乏味，如今卻稱讚它讓小說中無聲的悲劇更加令人心酸。"},{"w":"impassive","p":"adj.","d":"Showing no emotion on the face or in manner.","c":"面無表情的；不動聲色的","s":"Throughout the three-hour sentencing hearing, the defendant sat impassive at the table, his face revealing neither remorse nor defiance as the victims' families read aloud statements describing how the fraud had destroyed their savings.","t":"在長達三小時的量刑聽證會中，被告始終面無表情地坐在桌前；當受害者家屬朗讀陳述、描述這場詐騙如何毀掉他們的積蓄時，他的臉上既沒有悔意，也沒有反抗。","as":"The diplomat remained impassive while the belligerent minister delivered his rant, and her calm restraint did more to mollify the tense delegates than any eloquence could have achieved.","at":"當那位好戰的部長發表激烈的謾罵時，這位外交官始終不動聲色，她冷靜的克制比任何雄辯都更能安撫緊張的與會代表。"},{"w":"indifferent","p":"adj.","d":"Having no interest in or concern about something.","c":"漠不關心的；不在乎的","s":"Economists were puzzled that consumers seemed largely indifferent to the rising price of streaming subscriptions, continuing to pay for multiple services even after successive increases, a pattern suggesting that convenience mattered more to them than cost.","t":"經濟學家感到不解的是，消費者似乎對串流訂閱價格的上漲大多不以為意，即使價格接連調漲，仍繼續付費訂閱多個服務；這種模式顯示，對他們而言，便利比成本更重要。","as":"The candidate's ostentatious campaign events could not disguise how indifferent he was to the penurious farmers of the region, whose quandary over falling crop prices he dismissed with a few hackneyed promises.","at":"這位候選人鋪張浮誇的競選活動，掩蓋不了他對該地區貧困農民的漠不關心；面對農民因作物價格下跌而陷入的困境，他只用幾句陳腔濫調的承諾就打發了。"},{"w":"remote","p":"adj.","d":"Distant in manner; not friendly or involved.","c":"冷淡的；疏遠的；遙遠的","s":"Biographers describe the composer as a remote figure even to his own children, who recalled that he spent most evenings alone in his study and spoke to them chiefly through brief notes left on the dining-room table.","t":"傳記作家形容這位作曲家即使對自己的孩子也很疏遠；孩子們回憶說，他大多數晚上都獨自待在書房，主要是透過留在餐桌上的簡短字條跟他們說話。","as":"The emperor grew increasingly remote from his subjects, surrounding himself with obsequious advisers and lavish palaces while the provinces descended into turmoil and adversity that he scarcely acknowledged.","at":"這位皇帝與子民日漸疏遠，身邊圍繞著阿諛奉承的顧問與奢華的宮殿，而各省則陷入動盪與困苦，他卻幾乎不聞不問。"},{"w":"nonchalant","p":"adj.","d":"Calm and casual, showing no anxiety or strong interest.","c":"若無其事的；漫不經心的","s":"Although the veteran pilot later admitted that his heart had been pounding, his voice on the recorded radio transmission sounded almost nonchalant as he informed air-traffic controllers that both engines had failed and that he intended to land on the river.","t":"雖然這位資深機師事後承認當時心跳得很厲害，但在無線電通訊錄音中，他告知塔臺兩具引擎都已失效、打算降落在河面上時，聲音聽起來幾乎若無其事。","as":"The insolent heir adopted a nonchalant attitude toward the family fortune, squandering millions on ostentatious parties as though the prodigal habits of his youth could never lead to financial ruin.","at":"這位傲慢無禮的繼承人對家族財富抱持滿不在乎的態度，在鋪張炫耀的派對上揮霍數百萬，彷彿他年少時揮金如土的習慣永遠不會招致財務崩潰。"},{"w":"apathetic","p":"adj.","d":"Showing no interest, enthusiasm, or concern.","c":"冷漠的；無動於衷的","s":"Political scientists studying the region found that voters were not apathetic by nature; rather, decades of rigged elections had convinced many citizens that participation was pointless, so turnout rose sharply once independent observers began monitoring the polls.","t":"研究該地區的政治學者發現，選民並非天生冷漠；而是數十年來操縱選舉的情況讓許多公民相信參與毫無意義，因此一旦有獨立觀察員開始監督投票，投票率便大幅上升。","as":"Teachers worry that a curriculum dominated by banal worksheets and mundane drills makes students apathetic, and they argue that even a little levity in the classroom can rekindle the curiosity such insipid lessons have extinguished.","at":"教師們擔心，以陳腐的練習卷和枯燥的反覆操練為主的課程會讓學生變得冷漠，他們主張，課堂上即使多一點輕鬆幽默，也能重新點燃被這些乏味課程澆熄的好奇心。"},{"w":"phlegmatic","p":"adj.","d":"Calm and unemotional; not easily excited or upset.","c":"冷靜的；沉著的；遲鈍的","s":"Ancient physicians, following the theory of the four humors, believed that an excess of phlegm produced a phlegmatic temperament, describing such people as calm, slow to anger, and unlikely to be stirred by either joy or fear.","t":"古代醫生依循四體液說，認為黏液過多會造就冷靜沉著的氣質，並形容這樣的人平和、不易動怒，也不容易被喜悅或恐懼所觸動。","as":"The phlegmatic engineer listened patiently to the cantankerous client's verbose complaints about delays, and his steady composure allayed the man's anger far more effectively than any argument could have done.","at":"這位沉著冷靜的工程師耐心聽完那位脾氣暴躁的客戶對進度延誤的冗長抱怨，他穩重的態度比任何辯解都更有效地平息了對方的怒氣。"},{"w":"aloof","p":"adj.","d":"Cool and distant; not friendly or forthcoming.","c":"冷淡的；疏遠的","s":"Classmates remembered the future physicist as aloofeduring his university years, seldom joining study groups or social gatherings, though later accounts suggested that his apparent coldness concealed an intense shyness rather than any sense of superiority.","t":"同學們記得這位日後的物理學家在大學時代相當冷淡疏離，很少參加讀書會或社交聚會；不過後來的記述顯示，他表面上的冷漠其實掩藏著極度的害羞，而非任何優越感。","as":"The new ambassador, whose aloof manner was often mistaken for disdain, surprised the gregarious local officials by proving remarkably cordial once they gathered at the convivial banquet held in her honor.","at":"這位新任大使冷淡疏離的態度常被誤認為輕蔑，但在為她舉辦的歡樂宴會上，她卻表現得格外熱情親切，讓那些善於交際的地方官員大感意外。"},{"w":"listless","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking energy or enthusiasm, often from illness or sadness.","c":"無精打采的；倦怠的","s":"Veterinarians warn that a normally playful puppy that becomes listless, refusing food and sleeping far more than usual, may be suffering from a serious infection and should be examined promptly rather than simply allowed to rest.","t":"獸醫提醒，一隻平常活潑好動的幼犬若變得無精打采、拒絕進食且睡得比平常多很多，可能是罹患了嚴重的感染，應盡快就醫檢查，而不是只讓牠休息。","as":"After months of adversity, the refugees appeared listless and gaunt, and aid workers knew that even a munificent shipment of supplies could only partially alleviate the hardships they had endured.","at":"歷經數月的苦難後，難民們看起來無精打采又形容枯槁；救援人員知道，即使送來大批慷慨捐贈的物資，也只能部分減輕他們所承受的苦難。"},{"w":"stoical","p":"adj.","d":"Enduring pain or hardship without complaint or visible emotion.","c":"堅忍的；不動聲色的","s":"Letters from Civil War soldiers often display a stoical acceptance of hardship, describing frostbite, hunger, and the deaths of close friends in calm, almost matter-of-fact language that rarely betrays the suffering the writers must have felt.","t":"南北戰爭士兵的家書常流露出對苦難的坦然承受，他們以平靜、近乎就事論事的語氣描述凍傷、飢餓與摯友的死亡，字裡行間鮮少透露出寫信人必定感受過的痛苦。","as":"The stoical explorer endured the austere conditions of the Antarctic winter without complaint, rationing supplies in frugal portions and refusing to let the turmoil of the storms disrupt the expedition's careful scientific work.","at":"這位堅忍的探險家毫無怨言地忍受南極冬季的嚴酷環境，以節儉的份量配給物資，並拒絕讓暴風雪帶來的混亂打亂探險隊嚴謹的科學工作。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Lazy and Sluggish","themeZh":"懶散與遲緩","cards":[{"w":"indolent","p":"adj.","d":"Habitually lazy and avoiding effort.","c":"懶惰的；好逸惡勞的","s":"Eighteenth-century reformers often portrayed the aristocracy as indolent, arguing that nobles who lived entirely on inherited rents and spent their days at cards and hunting contributed nothing to the nation's prosperity while the peasants who worked their land went hungry.","t":"十八世紀的改革者常把貴族描繪成好逸惡勞的一群人，認為那些完全靠世襲地租過活、整天打牌狩獵的貴族對國家的繁榮毫無貢獻，而為他們耕種土地的農民卻在挨餓。","as":"The novel satirizes an indolent prince who squanders the royal treasury on lavish banquets, surrounded by obsequious courtiers whose flattery keeps him complacent while his kingdom slides toward ruin.","at":"這部小說諷刺一位懶散的王子，他把國庫揮霍在奢華的宴會上，身邊圍繞著阿諛奉承的朝臣，他們的諂媚讓他自滿安逸，而他的王國卻一步步走向毀滅。"},{"w":"soporific","p":"adj.","d":"Tending to cause sleep or drowsiness.","c":"催眠的；令人昏昏欲睡的","s":"Neuroscientists studying the effects of chamomile tea found that its reputation as a soporific remedy may be partly justified, since one of its compounds binds to the same brain receptors targeted by mild sedatives, although the effect is far weaker than that of prescription medication.","t":"研究洋甘菊茶效果的神經科學家發現，洋甘菊茶被認為有助眠功效的名聲或許有一定道理，因為其中一種化合物會與溫和鎮靜劑所作用的大腦受體結合，不過效果遠比處方藥物微弱。","as":"The keynote speaker's soporific lecture, a verbose catalog of platitudes delivered in a monotone, left even the most avid members of the audience struggling to stay awake.","at":"主講人那場令人昏昏欲睡的演講，以單調的語調冗長地羅列一連串陳腔濫調，連台下最熱衷的聽眾都得努力保持清醒。"},{"w":"sedentary","p":"adj.","d":"Involving much sitting and little physical activity.","c":"久坐的；不活動的；定居的","s":"A long-term study of office workers found that those whose jobs were almost entirely sedentary faced a significantly higher risk of heart disease, even if they exercised vigorously on weekends, suggesting that long uninterrupted hours of sitting carry risks of their own.","t":"一項針對上班族的長期研究發現，工作幾乎完全需要久坐的人罹患心臟病的風險明顯較高，即使他們週末劇烈運動也一樣；這顯示長時間不間斷地坐著本身就帶有風險。","as":"Anthropologists contrast the sedentary farming villages of the river valley with the nomadic herders of the surrounding steppe, whose austere, itinerant way of life required them to travel with the seasons.","at":"人類學家將河谷中定居務農的村落，與周圍草原上逐水草而居的游牧民族作對比；後者簡樸刻苦、四處遷徙的生活方式，使他們必須隨著季節移動。"},{"w":"stagnant","p":"adj.","d":"Not flowing or developing; showing no activity or growth.","c":"停滯的；不流動的；不景氣的","s":"Economists attributed the region's stagnant wages to the closing of its steel mills, noting that although unemployment eventually declined, the new service jobs paid far less, so that median household income in 2010 was barely higher than it had been in 1980.","t":"經濟學家將該地區薪資停滯不前歸因於鋼鐵廠的關閉，並指出雖然失業率最終下降，但新的服務業工作薪水低得多，以致2010年的家庭所得中位數僅略高於1980年。","as":"Critics argued that the once innovative studio had grown stagnant, releasing derivative sequels and hackneyed remakes because its complacent executives preferred safe profits to creative risk.","at":"評論家認為，這家曾經銳意創新的電影公司已經停滯不前，只推出模仿抄襲的續集和陳腐老套的翻拍片，因為自滿的高層寧可獲取穩當的利潤，也不願承擔創作上的風險。"},{"w":"lethargic","p":"adj.","d":"Sluggish and drowsy, lacking energy.","c":"昏昏欲睡的；無精打采的","s":"Marine biologists observed that the sea turtles became increasingly lethargic as water temperatures dropped below ten degrees Celsius, floating motionless near the surface until rescuers could transport them to heated tanks for recovery.","t":"海洋生物學家觀察到，當海水溫度降到攝氏十度以下時，海龜變得愈來愈遲緩無力，一動也不動地漂浮在海面附近，直到救援人員將牠們送往溫水池中休養。","as":"The once ebullient student became lethargic and withdrawn during the semester, and her conscientious teacher, wary of dismissing the change as trivial, contacted the school counselor.","at":"這位一向活潑開朗的學生在這學期變得無精打采、孤僻退縮，她那位認真負責的老師不敢把這種轉變當成小事，便聯絡了學校的輔導老師。"},{"w":"lassitude","p":"n.","d":"Physical or mental weariness; a lack of energy.","c":"倦怠；疲乏；無精打采","s":"Medical historians note that sailors on long eighteenth-century voyages often complained of deep lassitude weeks before the more visible symptoms of scurvy appeared, a weariness that physicians initially blamed on idleness rather than on the absence of fresh fruit.","t":"醫學史學家指出，十八世紀長途航行的水手在壞血病較明顯的症狀出現前數週，常會抱怨極度倦怠；醫生起初把這種疲乏歸咎於懶散，而非缺乏新鮮水果。","as":"A pervasive lassitude settled over the city after the debacle of the failed revolution, and even its most zealous activists grew apathetic, convinced that further protest would only invite more turmoil.","at":"革命失敗的慘敗之後，一股瀰漫的倦怠籠罩全城，連最狂熱的運動人士也變得冷漠，深信再抗議只會招致更多動盪。"},{"w":"languor","p":"n.","d":"A pleasant or dreamy feeling of tiredness or inactivity.","c":"慵懶；倦怠；悶熱的沉寂","s":"Literary critics have observed that Tennessee Williams used the oppressive heat of the American South to create a mood of sensual languor in his plays, with characters lounging on porches and speaking in slow, drawn-out sentences as the afternoon stretches endlessly on.","t":"文學評論家指出，田納西‧威廉斯利用美國南方令人窒息的炎熱，在劇作中營造出一種感官上的慵懶氛圍：劇中人物懶洋洋地倚在門廊上，用緩慢拖長的語句說話，而午後時光彷彿無止盡地延續。","as":"The novel's opening chapters, steeped in the languor of a seaside resort, are deliberately quiescent, and some readers find this prosaic stretch insipid until the sudden turmoil of the third chapter transforms the story.","at":"這部小說的開頭幾章充滿海濱度假勝地的慵懶氣息，刻意寫得平靜沉寂；有些讀者覺得這段平淡的篇幅索然無味，直到第三章突如其來的動盪才讓整個故事改頭換面。"},{"w":"sluggish","p":"adj.","d":"Moving or responding slowly; lacking energy.","c":"遲緩的；緩慢的；萎靡的","s":"Analysts warned that the recovery would remain sluggish as long as interest rates stayed high, since businesses were reluctant to borrow for new factories and consumers continued to postpone major purchases such as cars and houses.","t":"分析師警告，只要利率居高不下，經濟復甦就會持續遲緩，因為企業不願借錢興建新工廠，而消費者也繼續延後購買汽車、房屋等大件商品。","as":"Despite lavish government subsidies intended to ameliorate the crisis, the economy remained sluggish, and frugal households, wary of further turmoil, saved rather than spent their modest incomes.","at":"儘管政府祭出大筆補貼以改善危機，經濟依然疲軟，節儉的家庭因擔心更多動盪，選擇把微薄的收入存起來而不是花掉。"},{"w":"torpid","p":"adj.","d":"Mentally or physically inactive; dormant or numb.","c":"遲鈍的；麻木的；蟄伏的","s":"During the coldest weeks of winter, the hummingbirds enter a torpid state each night, lowering their body temperature and heart rate dramatically to conserve energy, then gradually reviving at dawn before resuming their search for nectar.","t":"在冬季最寒冷的幾週，蜂鳥每晚都會進入蟄伏狀態，大幅降低體溫與心跳以保存能量，然後在黎明時逐漸甦醒，再繼續尋找花蜜。","as":"The once vibrant debate club had become torpid under an apathetic adviser, its meetings reduced to banal discussions until a new teacher revived the students' interest in rhetorical skill.","at":"這個曾經充滿活力的辯論社在一位冷漠的指導老師帶領下變得死氣沉沉，社團聚會淪為平淡乏味的討論，直到一位新老師重新激起學生對修辭技巧的興趣。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Submissive and Servile","themeZh":"順從與卑屈","cards":[{"w":"compliant","p":"adj.","d":"Willing to obey rules or yield to others' wishes.","c":"順從的；遵從的；合規的","s":"Regulators discovered that although the factory appeared compliant with emissions standards during scheduled inspections, its operators routinely disabled the pollution filters at night, releasing several times the legal limit of sulfur dioxide into the surrounding valley.","t":"監管機關發現，雖然這座工廠在定期檢查時看似符合排放標準，但操作人員經常在夜間關閉污染過濾裝置，向周圍的山谷排放數倍於法定上限的二氧化硫。","as":"The dictator preferred compliant ministers to candid ones, and his obsequious cabinet, eager to appease him, offered only grandiloquent praise while the country slid into economic turmoil.","at":"這位獨裁者偏好順從聽話的部長，而非直言不諱的人；他那群阿諛奉承的內閣成員急於討好他，只會獻上浮誇的讚美，而國家卻逐漸陷入經濟動盪。"},{"w":"subservient","p":"adj.","d":"Excessively willing to obey others; treated as less important.","c":"屈從的；卑躬屈膝的；次要的","s":"Feminist literary critics have argued that many Victorian novels cast women in subservient roles, portraying the ideal wife as someone who sacrificed her own ambitions and opinions in order to support the career and comfort of her husband.","t":"女性主義文學評論家認為，許多維多利亞時代的小說都把女性塑造成屈從的角色，將理想的妻子描繪成為了支持丈夫的事業與舒適生活而犧牲自身抱負與意見的人。","as":"Critics charged that the newspaper had become subservient to its wealthy owner, publishing lavish tributes to his allies and refusing to impugn even his most egregious decisions, a complacent stance that alienated its once loyal readers.","at":"批評者指責這家報紙已屈從於其富有的老闆，刊登對其盟友極盡吹捧的報導，連他最惡劣的決策也不敢質疑；這種自滿的立場疏遠了原本忠實的讀者。"},{"w":"submissive","p":"adj.","d":"Ready to yield to the authority or control of others.","c":"順從的；服從的","s":"Ethologists have observed that lower-ranking wolves display submissive behavior toward the pack's dominant pair, lowering their heads, tucking their tails, and rolling onto their backs to avoid conflicts that might otherwise result in serious injury.","t":"研究動物行為的學者觀察到，地位較低的狼會對狼群中的主導配偶表現出順從的行為，牠們低頭、夾起尾巴，並翻身露出腹部，以避免可能導致重傷的衝突。","as":"The once submissive colony grew increasingly bellicose after the empire imposed new taxes, and its contentious assemblies, no longer willing to placate distant officials, began openly to defy royal decrees.","at":"帝國開徵新稅之後，這個原本順從的殖民地變得愈來愈好戰，其爭論不休的議會不再願意安撫遠方的官員，開始公然違抗王室的詔令。"},{"w":"subordinate","p":"adj.","d":"Lower in rank, position, or importance.","c":"下級的；從屬的；次要的","s":"In the Roman army, centurions held authority over the soldiers in their units but remained subordinate to the legion's commanding officers, a carefully structured chain of command that allowed orders to travel rapidly across a force of several thousand men.","t":"在羅馬軍隊中，百夫長對所屬部隊的士兵握有指揮權，但仍隸屬於軍團的指揮官；這種結構嚴謹的指揮體系，使命令能迅速傳達到數千人的部隊。","as":"The general insisted that his subordinate officers remain vigilant, warning that any complacent lapse during the cease-fire could reignite the turmoil and push the region back into precarious conflict.","at":"將軍堅持要求部屬軍官保持警覺，並警告在停火期間任何自滿的疏失，都可能再度引發動盪，使該地區重新陷入岌岌可危的衝突之中。"},{"w":"obsequious","p":"adj.","d":"Too eager to please or obey; fawning.","c":"諂媚的；奉承的","s":"Courtiers at Versailles competed to be obsequious in the presence of Louis XIV, praising his every remark and fighting for the privilege of handing him his shirt each morning, since royal favor determined who would receive lucrative offices and pensions.","t":"凡爾賽宮的朝臣在路易十四面前爭相獻媚，讚美他的每一句話，並爭搶每天早晨為他遞上襯衫的特權，因為國王的恩寵決定了誰能獲得肥缺與年金。","as":"The haughty director surrounded himself with obsequious assistants who praised his most banal ideas as visionary, and this complacent circle left him unable to recognize the trite quality of his recent films.","at":"那位傲慢的導演身邊圍繞著一群諂媚的助理，把他最平庸的點子都吹捧為高瞻遠矚；這個自滿的小圈子使他無法看清自己近期電影的陳腐。"},{"w":"servile","p":"adj.","d":"Excessively eager to serve or please; slavishly obedient.","c":"奴性的；卑屈的","s":"The historian argued that the nineteenth-century regional parliament was largely servile, routinely approving whatever budgets the governor proposed and never once in fifty years rejecting a measure that had the support of the crown.","t":"這位歷史學家認為，十九世紀的地方議會基本上唯命是從，例行公事般批准總督提出的任何預算，五十年來從未否決過任何一項獲王室支持的措施。","as":"Abolitionist writers condemned the iniquitous system that forced enslaved people into servile obedience, and their impassioned eloquence helped convert many complacent Northern readers to the cause of emancipation.","at":"廢奴主義作家譴責那個逼迫奴隸卑屈服從的不公制度，他們慷慨激昂的雄辯，使許多原本安於現狀的北方讀者轉而支持解放黑奴的運動。"},{"w":"fawning","p":"adj.","d":"Displaying exaggerated flattery or affection to win favor.","c":"阿諛奉承的；巴結的","s":"The biography's reviewers complained that its author was too fawning toward her subject, describing the billionaire's every business decision as visionary and omitting the lawsuits, failed ventures, and labor disputes that had marked much of his career.","t":"這本傳記的書評家批評作者對傳主過於阿諛奉承，把這位億萬富翁的每一個商業決策都描述成高瞻遠矚，卻略去了他職業生涯中屢見不鮮的訴訟、失敗的投資與勞資糾紛。","as":"The fawning tributes that greeted the general's return were so grandiloquent and ostentatious that skeptical journalists wondered whether the celebrations were meant to disguise the debacle of his final campaign.","at":"迎接將軍凱旋的那些阿諛奉承的頌詞是如此浮誇又鋪張，以致抱持懷疑的記者不禁懷疑，這些慶祝活動是否是為了掩飾他最後一場戰役的慘敗。"},{"w":"slavish","p":"adj.","d":"Copying or obeying without any originality or independent judgment.","c":"盲從的；毫無創意地模仿的；奴性的","s":"Art historians have noted that many Roman sculptures are slavish copies of earlier Greek bronzes, reproducing every fold of drapery and strand of hair so faithfully that scholars use them to reconstruct originals that were melted down centuries ago.","t":"藝術史學家指出，許多羅馬雕像是早期希臘青銅像亦步亦趨的仿製品，連衣褶與髮絲都如實複製，以致學者能利用它們重建早在幾世紀前就被熔毀的原作。","as":"The critic dismissed the film as a slavish imitation of earlier thrillers, calling it derivative and lackluster and complaining that its hackneyed plot twists could be predicted from the opening scene.","at":"這位影評人把這部電影貶為一味模仿早期驚悚片的作品，稱其抄襲且平淡無奇，並抱怨其陳腐老套的情節轉折從開場就能預料。"},{"w":"sycophant","p":"n.","d":"A person who flatters powerful people to gain advantage.","c":"諂媚者；馬屁精","s":"Historians suggest that the emperor's disastrous military campaigns resulted partly from his reliance on a single sycophant who praised every plan as brilliant, while experienced generals who raised objections were quietly dismissed from court.","t":"歷史學家認為，這位皇帝災難性的軍事行動，部分原因在於他倚賴一名把每項計畫都吹捧為英明的諂媚者，而提出異議的資深將領則被悄悄逐出朝廷。","as":"The memoir portrays the senator's chief aide as a sycophant whose obsequious flattery and fawning loyalty concealed a devious ambition, and readers are left to wonder why so astute a politician, normally contemptuous of flattery, failed to see through him.","at":"這本回憶錄把那位參議員的首席助理描繪成一個諂媚者，他阿諛奉承的言詞與巴結的忠誠背後隱藏著狡詐的野心，讀者不禁納悶，如此精明、平時對奉承不屑一顧的政治人物為何沒能識破他。"},{"w":"toady","p":"n.","d":"A person who flatters or obeys others to win favor.","c":"馬屁精；奉承者","s":"In Dickens's novel, the villainous clerk Uriah Heep plays the role of a humble toady, constantly declaring how lowly he is and flattering his employer, while secretly scheming to seize control of the firm and its finances.","t":"在狄更斯的小說中，邪惡的書記員烏利亞‧希普扮演一個謙卑的馬屁精，不斷聲稱自己有多卑微並奉承雇主，暗地裡卻密謀奪取公司及其財務的控制權。","as":"The satirist mocked the minister as a toady to wealthy donors, a pretentious figure whose grandiloquent speeches about public service could not disguise his mercenary eagerness to reward those who funded his campaigns.","at":"這位諷刺作家嘲諷該部長是富裕捐款人的馬屁精，一個裝腔作勢的人物，他那些關於公共服務的浮誇演說，掩蓋不了他急於回報金主的唯利是圖。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Enthusiasm and Passion","themeZh":"熱情與狂熱","cards":[{"w":"ebullient","p":"adj.","d":"Overflowing with cheerful excitement and enthusiasm.","c":"熱情洋溢的；興高采烈的","s":"Although the mission scientists had braced themselves for a failed landing, they were ebullient when the rover's first panoramic images arrived intact, hugging one another, cheering across the control room, and staying long past midnight to pore over every crater and ridge.","t":"儘管任務科學家們早已做好登陸失敗的心理準備，但當探測車傳回的第一批全景影像完好無損地抵達時，他們仍興高采烈，在控制室裡相互擁抱、歡呼，並一直待到午夜過後，仔細端詳每一座隕石坑與每一道山脊。","as":"The usually taciturn conductor became surprisingly ebullient after the premiere, abandoning his aloof manner to greet the musicians with jocular praise, though critics later found the symphony itself disappointingly derivative of Mahler.","at":"平時沉默寡言的指揮家在首演後出乎意料地興高采烈，一改冷漠疏離的態度，以詼諧的讚美向樂手們致意；不過，評論家後來認為這首交響曲本身過度模仿馬勒，令人失望。"},{"w":"effervescent","p":"adj.","d":"Lively, bubbly, and full of high spirits.","c":"活潑的；興高采烈的；冒泡的","s":"Reviewers agreed that the actress's effervescent performance was the production's saving grace; whenever she bounded onto the stage, her sparkling wit and infectious laughter revived an audience that had been nodding off through the play's long, ponderous philosophical monologues.","t":"評論家一致認為，那位女演員活潑洋溢的演出是整齣戲的救星；每當她輕快地跳上舞台，她妙語如珠的機智與富感染力的笑聲，總能喚醒那些在冗長沉悶的哲學獨白中打瞌睡的觀眾。","as":"Unlike her taciturn predecessor, the new museum director was effervescent and gregarious, and her convivial gala dinners quickly mollified donors who had grown indifferent to the institution's long run of lackluster exhibitions.","at":"與沉默寡言的前任不同，新任博物館館長活潑開朗、喜好交際，她所舉辦的歡樂晚宴很快就安撫了那些因長期乏善可陳的展覽而變得漠不關心的捐款人。"},{"w":"exuberant","p":"adj.","d":"Full of energy, excitement, and cheerful high spirits.","c":"熱情奔放的；精力充沛的","s":"The anthropologist described the harvest festival as the village's most exuberant event of the year: after months of austere rationing, residents danced through the streets until dawn, sang improvised songs, and showered one another with flower petals and rice.","t":"那位人類學家形容，豐收祭是村裡一年中最熱情奔放的盛事：在經歷數月的嚴格配給後，村民們在街上跳舞直到天亮，即興高歌，並彼此拋撒花瓣與米粒。","as":"The coach's exuberant celebration after the upset victory struck some reporters as ostentatious, yet it helped dispel the lethargic mood and pervasive animosity that had plagued the locker room throughout a season of adversity.","at":"教練在爆冷勝利後熱情奔放的慶祝，在部分記者看來過於張揚，但這確實驅散了整個逆境賽季中籠罩更衣室的萎靡氣氛與普遍的敵意。"},{"w":"impassioned","p":"adj.","d":"Filled with or showing intense, strong feeling.","c":"慷慨激昂的；充滿激情的","s":"In her impassioned address to the United Nations, the climate scientist abandoned the cautious language of her published papers, pounding the lectern as she warned delegates that their grandchildren would judge them harshly for every year of delay in cutting carbon emissions.","t":"在對聯合國發表的慷慨激昂演說中，這位氣候科學家拋開了她學術論文中謹慎的措辭，一邊捶打講台，一邊警告各國代表：他們的孫輩將會為減碳行動每拖延一年而嚴厲批判他們。","as":"Frederick Douglass's impassioned oratory did not merely castigate slaveholders; his eloquence also shamed the complacent Northerners who claimed to oppose slavery in principle while remaining indifferent to its daily cruelties.","at":"弗雷德里克・道格拉斯慷慨激昂的演說不僅嚴厲譴責了奴隸主；他的雄辯也讓那些自滿的北方人無地自容——他們聲稱原則上反對奴隸制，卻對奴隸每日所受的殘酷對待漠不關心。"},{"w":"avid","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely eager and enthusiastic about an interest or pursuit.","c":"熱衷的；渴望的","s":"Thomas Jefferson was so avid a collector of books that after the British burned the Library of Congress in 1814, he was able to replace its holdings by selling the nation more than six thousand volumes from his personal library at Monticello.","t":"湯瑪斯・傑佛遜是一位極為熱衷的藏書家，以至於英軍在1814年焚毀國會圖書館後，他能將蒙蒂塞洛私人圖書館中六千多冊藏書賣給國家，以補足館藏。","as":"An avid birdwatcher, the retired judge was usually reticent and somewhat aloof at dinner parties, but any mention of migratory warblers made him so voluble that guests struggled to steer the conversation elsewhere.","at":"這位退休法官是熱衷的賞鳥人，在晚宴上通常沉默寡言、有些疏離，但只要一提到遷徙的林鶯，他就變得滔滔不絕，讓賓客們難以把話題轉到別處。"},{"w":"zealous","p":"adj.","d":"Showing intense, sometimes excessive, devotion to a cause.","c":"熱心的；狂熱的","s":"The prosecutor was so zealous in pursuing the corruption case that she worked through holidays, personally reviewed tens of thousands of bank records, and was eventually reprimanded by the court for pressing witnesses too aggressively in her determination to secure a conviction.","t":"那位檢察官在追查這起貪腐案時極為狂熱，連假日都在工作，親自審閱了數萬筆銀行紀錄，最後甚至因一心想將被告定罪、過度強硬地逼問證人而遭法院申誡。","as":"Zealous reformers of the Progressive Era did not merely deprecate the nefarious practices of urban political machines; they also censured the complacent voters whose apathetic acceptance of bribery allowed corruption to flourish.","at":"進步時代熱忱的改革者不僅抨擊城市政治機器的卑劣行徑，也譴責那些自滿的選民——正是他們對賄賂漠然接受的態度，讓貪腐得以猖獗。"},{"w":"ardent","p":"adj.","d":"Intensely enthusiastic, devoted, or passionate.","c":"熱烈的；熱心的","s":"Although she was an ardent supporter of women's suffrage from her teenage years, the novelist refused to march in public demonstrations, preferring instead to channel her passion into pamphlets and fiction that she believed would change more minds than any parade.","t":"儘管這位小說家從青少年時期就是婦女參政權的熱烈支持者，她卻拒絕參加公開遊行，寧願將熱情投注於小冊子與小說的創作，她相信這些作品比任何遊行都更能改變人心。","as":"Even ardent admirers of the senator conceded that his speeches had grown verbose and his arguments increasingly hackneyed, though few dared to rebuke him openly, given his belligerent reaction to earlier critics.","at":"即使是這位參議員最熱烈的仰慕者也承認，他的演講變得冗長，論點也愈來愈陳腐；不過，鑑於他先前對批評者的好鬥反應，很少有人敢公開指責他。"},{"w":"fanatical","p":"adj.","d":"Filled with extreme, unreasoning enthusiasm or devotion.","c":"狂熱的；盲信的","s":"According to the sociologist's case study, the cult's leader demanded fanatical loyalty from his followers, insisting that they cut off all contact with relatives, surrender their savings to the group, and accept without question his increasingly bizarre predictions about the imminent end of the world.","t":"根據那位社會學家的個案研究，該邪教領袖要求追隨者展現狂熱的忠誠，堅持要他們斷絕與親人的一切聯繫、將積蓄全數交給團體，並毫不質疑地接受他對世界末日即將來臨所做出、愈來愈離奇的預言。","as":"The historian argues that the regime's fanatical propaganda thrived on animosity toward outsiders, transforming ordinary citizens into belligerent zealots and rendering moderate voices so subservient that no one dared to impugn official policy.","at":"這位歷史學家認為，該政權狂熱的宣傳靠煽動對外人的敵意而壯大，把普通百姓變成好戰的狂熱分子，並使溫和派變得唯唯諾諾，沒有人敢質疑官方政策。"},{"w":"fervent","p":"adj.","d":"Showing intense, sincere, and passionate feeling.","c":"熱切的；熱誠的","s":"Despite repeated failures, the Wright brothers maintained a fervent belief that powered flight was achievable, and that conviction sustained them through years of crashed gliders, ridicule from the press, and painstaking wind-tunnel experiments in their modest Dayton bicycle shop.","t":"儘管一再失敗，萊特兄弟始終熱切地相信動力飛行是可以實現的；正是這份信念，支撐他們熬過多年來滑翔機墜毀、媒體嘲諷，以及在代頓那間簡樸自行車店裡進行的艱辛風洞實驗。","as":"Despite her fervent plea for compromise, the mediator could not placate either delegation, and the contentious negotiations soon collapsed into a debacle that left both nations in a precarious position.","at":"儘管調解人熱切呼籲雙方妥協，她仍無法安撫任何一方代表團；這場爭議不斷的談判很快就徹底破局，讓兩國都陷入岌岌可危的處境。"},{"w":"vibrant","p":"adj.","d":"Full of energy, life, and activity.","c":"充滿活力的；生氣勃勃的","s":"Urban planners credit the conversion of abandoned warehouses into studios, cafés, and music venues with transforming the once-deserted riverfront into a vibrant neighborhood where street markets, festivals, and late-night crowds now fill sidewalks that were empty only a decade ago.","t":"都市規劃者認為，將廢棄倉庫改建為工作室、咖啡館和音樂表演場地，使曾經冷清的河濱地區轉變為充滿活力的街區；如今，街頭市集、節慶活動和深夜人潮擠滿了十年前還空無一人的人行道。","as":"Once stagnant and sluggish, the port city's economy has become vibrant again, though critics warn that the lavish spending fueling its revival could prove detrimental if interest rates rise sharply.","at":"這座港口城市的經濟曾經停滯不前、萎靡不振，如今再度充滿活力；不過批評者警告，若利率急遽上升，推動其復甦的大手筆支出可能會帶來不利影響。"}]},{"unit":17,"theme":"Stubbornness and Determination","themeZh":"固執與堅定","cards":[{"w":"intractable","p":"adj.","d":"Hard to control, manage, or solve.","c":"難處理的；難駕馭的；棘手的","s":"For more than three centuries, Fermat's Last Theorem remained one of the most intractable problems in mathematics, defeating generations of brilliant scholars until Andrew Wiles finally produced a proof in 1994 that drew on branches of the field Fermat himself could never have imagined.","t":"三個多世紀以來，費馬最後定理一直是數學界最棘手的難題之一，難倒了一代又一代的傑出學者，直到1994年安德魯・懷爾斯才終於提出證明，而他所運用的數學分支是費馬本人當年無法想像的。","as":"The border dispute proved intractable: each attempt to mediate collapsed amid mutual animosity, and even the most conciliatory proposals were rebuffed by delegates too belligerent to accept any compromise, however modest.","at":"這場邊界爭端證明極為棘手：每一次調停嘗試都在雙方的敵意中破局，即使是最具和解誠意的提案，也被那些過於好戰、不願接受任何妥協（無論多麼微小）的代表斷然拒絕。"},{"w":"recalcitrant","p":"adj.","d":"Stubbornly refusing to obey authority or rules.","c":"桀驁不馴的；頑抗的","s":"When several recalcitrant provinces refused to collect the new imperial tax and openly ignored repeated summonses to the capital, the emperor dispatched troops to enforce compliance, a decision that historians believe accelerated the dynasty's eventual collapse.","t":"當數個頑抗的省份拒絕徵收新的帝國稅，並公然無視朝廷一再召見時，皇帝派遣軍隊強制他們服從；歷史學家認為，這項決定加速了王朝最終的覆滅。","as":"The headmaster tried to placate the recalcitrant students with concessions, but his conciliatory tone only emboldened them, and their insolent defiance soon gave way to open turmoil throughout the school.","at":"校長試圖以讓步來安撫那些桀驁不馴的學生，但他和解的語氣反而助長了他們的氣焰；他們傲慢無禮的反抗很快演變成全校的公開騷亂。"},{"w":"resolve","p":"n.","d":"Firm determination to do something.","c":"決心；堅定","s":"During the Blitz, German planners assumed that months of nightly bombing would break British resolve, yet surveys of Londoners revealed the opposite: civilians who had lost their homes often became more determined than ever to continue the war.","t":"在倫敦大轟炸期間，德國的策劃者認為，連續數月的夜間轟炸將會擊垮英國人的決心，然而對倫敦市民的調查卻顯示了相反的結果：失去家園的平民往往比以往更加堅定地要將戰爭打下去。","as":"Facing adversity that would have left most explorers listless and apathetic, Shackleton's crew drew strength from his quiet resolve, and his stoical leadership helped quell the despair that threatened to overwhelm them on the ice.","at":"面對足以讓大多數探險家萎靡不振、心灰意冷的逆境，沙克爾頓的船員從他沉靜的決心中汲取力量；他堅忍的領導平息了那股幾乎在冰原上將他們吞噬的絕望。"},{"w":"unwavering","p":"adj.","d":"Steady and firm; not changing or weakening.","c":"堅定不移的；不動搖的","s":"Marie Curie's unwavering commitment to her research sustained her through years of grinding labor in a leaky shed, where she processed tons of pitchblende by hand to isolate a fraction of a gram of radium, despite poverty, illness, and the skepticism of colleagues.","t":"瑪麗・居禮對研究堅定不移的投入，支撐她在一間漏水的棚屋裡度過多年辛苦的勞動；她在那裡以人工處理數噸瀝青鈾礦，只為分離出不到一公克的鐳，儘管她當時面臨貧困、疾病與同僚的質疑。","as":"Throughout the contentious three-week trial, the defense attorney showed unwavering composure, refusing to be provoked by the prosecutor's pugnacious questioning and calmly allaying the jury's doubts about her client's character.","at":"在為期三週、爭議激烈的審判中，辯護律師展現出堅定不移的沉著，拒絕被檢察官咄咄逼人的質詢激怒，並冷靜地消除了陪審團對她當事人品格的疑慮。"},{"w":"unyielding","p":"adj.","d":"Firm and inflexible; refusing to give way.","c":"不屈服的；堅硬的","s":"Although the striking miners offered to accept a smaller wage increase, the company's directors remained unyielding, insisting that no concessions of any kind would be made until every worker had returned to the pits and signed the original contract.","t":"儘管罷工的礦工願意接受較小幅度的加薪，公司董事們仍毫不讓步，堅持在每位工人都回到礦坑並簽下原合約之前，絕不做出任何形式的讓步。","as":"The magistrate's unyielding opposition to clemency dismayed reformers, who had hoped that a more benevolent approach would ameliorate overcrowded prisons, but who instead found their appeals rebuffed with disdainful brevity.","at":"這位法官對寬恕毫不讓步的反對態度令改革者們失望；他們原本希望以較仁慈的方式改善監獄擁擠的問題，結果他們的請求卻被以輕蔑的簡短回應斷然拒絕。"},{"w":"obdurate","p":"adj.","d":"Stubbornly refusing to change one's opinion or feelings.","c":"執拗的；冷酷無情的","s":"In Dickens's novel, Ebenezer Scrooge remains obdurate in the face of every appeal to his conscience, rejecting charity collectors, his nephew's warm invitations, and his clerk's modest needs, until a series of ghostly visitors finally softens his hardened heart.","t":"在狄更斯的小說中，艾比尼澤・史古基面對每一次對他良心的呼喚都冷酷不為所動，拒絕了慈善募款人、他外甥熱情的邀請以及他書記員微薄的需求，直到一連串幽靈來訪，才終於軟化了他那顆冷硬的心。","as":"No amount of eloquence from the community's advocates could sway the obdurate committee chair, whose disdainful dismissal of the report's findings struck observers as both arrogant and detrimental to the agency's credibility.","at":"社區倡議者再怎麼雄辯，也無法動搖那位執拗的委員會主席；他對報告結論的輕蔑否定，在旁觀者看來既傲慢，又有損該機構的公信力。"},{"w":"obstinate","p":"adj.","d":"Stubbornly refusing to change one's opinion or course.","c":"固執的；頑固的","s":"Historians often fault the general's obstinate refusal to retreat; even after his scouts reported that the enemy outnumbered his forces three to one, he insisted on holding the exposed ridge, a choice that cost thousands of lives in a single afternoon.","t":"歷史學家常常歸咎於那位將軍固執地拒絕撤退；即使他的斥候回報敵軍兵力是己方的三倍，他仍堅持死守那道毫無掩護的山脊，這個決定在一個下午就斷送了數千條性命。","as":"The obstinate patient refused to modify his sedentary habits, dismissing his cardiologist's repeated warnings as banal platitudes, even though, by every measure, his indolent lifestyle was detrimental to his failing heart.","at":"那位固執的病人拒絕改變久坐不動的習慣，把心臟科醫師一再的警告當作陳腔濫調而不予理會，儘管從各方面看來，他懶散的生活方式顯然對他日漸衰弱的心臟有害。"},{"w":"adamant","p":"adj.","d":"Refusing to be persuaded or to change one's mind.","c":"堅決的；堅定不移的","s":"Although her editor urged her to soften the controversial final chapter, the biographer was adamant that it remain unchanged, arguing that removing evidence of the statesman's private cruelty would betray both the historical record and the readers who trusted her scholarship.","t":"儘管編輯力勸她緩和爭議性的最後一章，這位傳記作家仍堅決不讓它有任何更動，她認為刪除那位政治家私下殘酷行為的證據，既背叛了歷史記錄，也辜負了信任她學術研究的讀者。","as":"The chief engineer was adamant that the bridge was unsafe, and her terse report castigated managers whose complacent neglect of routine inspections had left the structure in a precarious state.","at":"總工程師堅稱這座橋並不安全，她簡短的報告嚴厲指責管理階層，正是他們自滿而疏於例行檢查，才讓這座結構處於岌岌可危的狀態。"},{"w":"dogged","p":"adj.","d":"Showing persistent, tenacious determination despite difficulty.","c":"頑強的；堅持不懈的","s":"The investigative reporters' dogged pursuit of the story lasted nearly two years; they filed hundreds of public-records requests, tracked down former employees in four countries, and persisted even after the company threatened lawsuits, until their articles finally exposed the fraud.","t":"那幾位調查記者頑強地追查這則新聞將近兩年；他們提出數百件公開資料申請，在四個國家追查前員工的下落，即使公司威脅提告也不罷休，直到他們的報導終於揭露了這起詐欺案。","as":"Through dogged archival research, the historian unraveled the enigma of the cryptic letters, revealing that a devious official had used coded messages to conceal his nefarious dealings with foreign agents.","at":"憑藉頑強不懈的檔案研究，這位歷史學家解開了那些神祕信件之謎，揭示一名狡詐的官員曾利用密碼訊息來掩飾他與外國特務之間的不法勾當。"},{"w":"hidebound","p":"adj.","d":"Narrow-minded and stubbornly resistant to new ideas.","c":"守舊的；墨守成規的","s":"The Impressionists were rejected by the Paris Salon, a hidebound institution whose judges insisted that serious art must depict historical or mythological subjects in smooth, polished brushwork and dismissed loose, sunlit scenes of everyday life as unfinished sketches.","t":"印象派畫家遭到巴黎沙龍拒絕；這是一個墨守成規的機構，其評審堅持嚴肅的藝術必須以平滑精緻的筆觸描繪歷史或神話題材，並將描繪日常生活、筆觸鬆散、灑滿陽光的畫面貶斥為未完成的草稿。","as":"Critics castigated the hidebound academy for its supercilious contempt toward young composers, arguing that its rigid insistence on hackneyed forms had made its concerts as insipid as they were predictable.","at":"評論家嚴厲抨擊這所守舊的學院對年輕作曲家抱持傲慢的輕視，認為它死守陳腐的形式，使得其音樂會既乏味又可預料。"},{"w":"willful","p":"adj.","d":"Stubbornly determined to do as one wishes, ignoring others.","c":"任性的；固執己見的","s":"Historians of the Tudor court describe the young Henry VIII as a willful prince who ignored the counsel of his father's experienced ministers, insisted on lavish tournaments the treasury could not afford, and punished anyone who dared to question his personal wishes.","t":"研究都鐸宮廷的歷史學家形容，年輕的亨利八世是一位任性的君主，他無視父王身邊經驗豐富的大臣們的勸告，堅持舉辦國庫負擔不起的奢華比武大會，並懲罰任何膽敢質疑他個人意願的人。","as":"The willful heiress rebuffed every warning from the family's trustees, squandering her inheritance on ostentatious mansions and reacting with insolent contempt whenever advisers urged her to adopt a more frugal lifestyle.","at":"那位任性的女繼承人斷然拒絕家族信託人的每一次警告，把遺產揮霍在浮誇的豪宅上，每當顧問勸她改採較節儉的生活方式時，她都以傲慢無禮的輕蔑回應。"}]},{"unit":18,"theme":"Sound and Noise","themeZh":"聲音與噪音","cards":[{"w":"discordant","p":"adj.","d":"Harsh and inharmonious in sound; lacking agreement.","c":"不和諧的；不一致的","s":"When Stravinsky's The Rite of Spring premiered in Paris in 1913, many listeners found its clashing harmonies and jagged rhythms so discordant that they jeered, whistled, and shouted until the dancers could barely hear the orchestra over the uproar.","t":"1913年史特拉汶斯基的《春之祭》在巴黎首演時，許多聽眾覺得它衝突的和聲與參差的節奏極不和諧，於是噓聲、口哨聲與叫喊聲此起彼落，喧鬧到舞者幾乎聽不見樂團的演奏。","as":"The panel's final report was a discordant document, with each chapter reflecting the contentious views of a different faction, and reviewers complained that its verbose prose and cryptic conclusions only deepened the public's turmoil.","at":"該小組的最終報告是一份內容互相矛盾的文件，每一章都反映了不同派系的爭議性觀點；審閱者抱怨其冗長的文字與晦澀的結論，只加深了大眾的混亂。"},{"w":"euphony","p":"n.","d":"A pleasing, harmonious combination of sounds.","c":"悅耳的聲音；和諧音調","s":"Linguists have long debated why Italian is so often praised for its euphony, with many pointing to its abundance of open vowels, its avoidance of harsh consonant clusters, and the way most words end on a soft, singable syllable.","t":"語言學家長期爭論，為何義大利語常因其悅耳的音韻而備受讚譽；許多人指出，這是因為它擁有大量開口母音、避免刺耳的子音連綴，而且大多數單字都以柔和、易於吟唱的音節結尾。","as":"Tennyson's verse was widely admired for its euphony, yet some Modernist critics deprecated it as vapid and grandiloquent, arguing that the poet's sonorous lines often disguised trite sentiments beneath their polished music.","at":"丁尼生的詩作以音韻和諧而廣受讚賞，但部分現代主義評論家批評其空洞浮誇，認為這位詩人鏗鏘悅耳的詩句常常以精緻的音樂性掩飾老套的情感。"},{"w":"cacophony","p":"n.","d":"A harsh, jarring mixture of loud sounds.","c":"刺耳的噪音；不和諧音","s":"Marine biologists warn that the cacophony produced by cargo ships, sonar systems, and offshore drilling now drowns out the low-frequency songs whales use to locate mates across hundreds of kilometers of open ocean, potentially disrupting entire breeding populations.","t":"海洋生物學家警告，貨輪、聲納系統和離岸鑽探所產生的刺耳噪音，如今已淹沒了鯨魚用來在數百公里開闊海域中尋找配偶的低頻歌聲，可能擾亂整個繁殖族群。","as":"The trading floor's cacophony seemed to mirror the turmoil in global markets, as brokers who were usually nonchalant shouted frantic orders, and even the most phlegmatic analysts struggled to stay detached.","at":"交易大廳的嘈雜喧囂似乎正映照出全球市場的動盪；平時從容自若的經紀人大聲喊出慌亂的指令，即使是最沉著冷靜的分析師也難以保持超然。"},{"w":"vociferous","p":"adj.","d":"Expressing opinions loudly and forcefully.","c":"大聲疾呼的；喧嚷的","s":"The proposal to build a highway through the wetlands met vociferous opposition from local residents, who packed every public hearing, chanted slogans outside city hall, and flooded council members' offices with thousands of angry letters and phone calls.","t":"在濕地上興建高速公路的提案遭到當地居民大聲疾呼的反對；他們擠滿每一場公聽會，在市政廳外高喊口號，並以成千上萬封憤怒的信件和電話淹沒市議員的辦公室。","as":"The vociferous critic, notorious for his pugnacious reviews, berated the playwright for relying on hackneyed plots, though readers increasingly found his own rants as predictable as the dramas he condemned.","at":"這位以好鬥書評聞名、大聲疾呼的評論家，痛斥那位劇作家依賴陳腐的情節；然而讀者愈來愈覺得，他自己的咆哮就和他所譴責的戲劇一樣老套可預測。"},{"w":"strident","p":"adj.","d":"Loud, harsh, and grating; forcefully assertive.","c":"刺耳的；尖銳強硬的","s":"Historians note that the abolitionist newspaper's strident tone, which denounced slaveholders as criminals and refused any gradual compromise, alienated many moderate Northern readers even as it energized activists who believed polite persuasion had already failed.","t":"歷史學家指出，這份廢奴主義報紙尖銳強硬的語氣——將奴隸主斥為罪犯並拒絕任何漸進式的妥協——疏遠了許多溫和的北方讀者，但同時也激勵了那些認為禮貌勸說早已失敗的運動人士。","as":"The candidate's strident attacks on her rivals struck many voters as belligerent, and her advisers urged her to adopt a more cordial tone to mollify the moderates she had alienated.","at":"這位候選人對對手的尖銳攻擊讓許多選民覺得太過好鬥，她的顧問們力勸她採取較為親切友善的語氣，以安撫那些被她疏遠的溫和派選民。"},{"w":"raucous","p":"adj.","d":"Making a harsh, loud, and disorderly noise.","c":"喧鬧的；沙啞刺耳的","s":"Shakespeare's original audiences at the Globe were famously raucous: the groundlings who paid a penny to stand near the stage cracked nuts, heckled the actors, cheered sword fights, and shouted insults at villains throughout the performance.","t":"莎士比亞在環球劇場的原始觀眾以喧鬧著稱：那些付一便士站在舞台旁的平民觀眾，在整場演出中嗑堅果、起鬨嘲弄演員、為劍鬥喝采，並對劇中的反派大聲咒罵。","as":"The once raucous tavern had become quiescent, its gregarious regulars replaced by a few lethargic patrons who sat in silence, a change the owner blamed on the town's economic adversity.","at":"那家曾經喧鬧不已的酒館如今變得一片沉寂，原本愛交際的常客被幾位無精打采、默默坐著的客人所取代；老闆將這樣的改變歸咎於小鎮的經濟困境。"},{"w":"acoustics","p":"n.","d":"The qualities of a room that determine how sound carries.","c":"音響效果；聲學","s":"Architects designing the new concert hall consulted physicists for two years, testing the curved ceiling panels and adjustable wall baffles until the acoustics allowed a single violin to be heard clearly from the farthest seat in the upper balcony.","t":"設計新音樂廳的建築師花了兩年時間諮詢物理學家，測試弧形天花板面板與可調式牆面隔音板，直到音響效果好到讓樓上包廂最遠的座位也能清楚聽見一把小提琴的聲音。","as":"Despite the cathedral's superb acoustics, the visiting choir gave a lackluster, insipid performance, and the organist's ostentatious solos only underscored how little the singers seemed to care about the music they were performing.","at":"儘管大教堂的音響效果絕佳，來訪的合唱團卻演出得平淡乏味，而管風琴手炫技的獨奏更凸顯出歌手們似乎對自己演唱的音樂有多麼不用心。"},{"w":"clamor","p":"n.","d":"A loud, confused noise, especially of shouting voices.","c":"喧鬧聲；強烈要求","s":"As word spread that the Bastille had fallen, the clamor in the streets of Paris grew so loud that residents miles away reported hearing church bells, musket fire, and thousands of voices shouting for liberty throughout the night of July 14, 1789.","t":"隨著巴士底監獄陷落的消息傳開，巴黎街頭的喧鬧聲愈來愈大，數英里外的居民都表示，在1789年7月14日整夜聽見教堂鐘聲、火槍聲，以及成千上萬人高呼自由的聲音。","as":"Amid the clamor of protest, the governor tried to placate demonstrators with vague promises, but his evasive circumlocution only intensified their animosity toward an administration they considered both arrogant and remote.","at":"在一片抗議的喧囂聲中，州長試圖以含糊的承諾來安撫示威者，但他閃爍其詞的拐彎抹角只加深了他們對這個既傲慢又疏離的政府的敵意。"},{"w":"din","p":"n.","d":"A loud, continuous, and unpleasant noise.","c":"持續的喧囂聲；嘈雜聲","s":"Researchers studying classrooms located near major airports found that the constant din of jet engines overhead reduced students' reading comprehension scores significantly, since teachers were repeatedly forced to pause lessons until each passing plane had faded into the distance.","t":"研究位於大型機場附近教室的學者發現，頭頂上噴射引擎持續不斷的轟鳴聲大幅降低了學生的閱讀理解成績，因為老師一再被迫暫停授課，直到每架飛過的飛機聲音逐漸遠去。","as":"Above the din of the crowded night market, a garrulous vendor prattled on about the virtues of his wares, while his taciturn partner simply waited, unperturbed by the turmoil around them.","at":"在擁擠夜市的嘈雜聲中，一位多話的小販喋喋不休地介紹他貨品的優點，而他沉默寡言的夥伴只是靜靜等候，絲毫不受周遭混亂的影響。"},{"w":"mellifluous","p":"adj.","d":"Sweet, smooth, and pleasing to hear.","c":"悅耳流暢的；甜美的","s":"Radio producers in the 1940s prized announcers with mellifluous voices, believing that a warm, smooth, honeyed tone could hold listeners' attention through long news bulletins and persuade them to trust the sponsors whose products were advertised between broadcasts.","t":"1940年代的廣播製作人非常看重嗓音甜美流暢的播音員，他們相信溫暖、圓潤、如蜜般的音色能在冗長的新聞播報中抓住聽眾的注意力，並說服他們信任節目間所廣告產品的贊助商。","as":"The diplomat's mellifluous voice and affable manner charmed his hosts at the summit, though skeptics noted that his eloquence often masked evasive answers and that his speeches were laced with banal platitudes.","at":"這位外交官悅耳的嗓音與和藹的舉止讓高峰會的東道主為之著迷，但懷疑者指出，他的雄辯往往掩飾了閃爍的答覆，而他的演講也充斥著陳腔濫調。"}]},{"unit":19,"theme":"Praise and Honor","themeZh":"讚美與尊崇","cards":[{"w":"acclaim","p":"v.","d":"To praise enthusiastically and publicly.","c":"稱讚；喝采；公開讚揚","s":"Although her early novels sold poorly, critics now acclaim Zora Neale Hurston as one of the most important voices of the Harlem Renaissance, and Their Eyes Were Watching God is taught in thousands of university literature courses around the world.","t":"儘管柔拉・涅爾・賀絲頓早期的小說銷量不佳，評論家如今公認並讚揚她是哈林文藝復興時期最重要的聲音之一，而《他們眼望上蒼》也在全世界數千門大學文學課程中被講授。","as":"Critics acclaimed the debut album for its exuberant energy, contrasting it with the lackluster, derivative records that had dominated the charts, though a few captious reviewers dismissed its lyrics as trite.","at":"評論家盛讚這張首張專輯熱情奔放的活力，並將它與當時稱霸排行榜那些平淡乏味、模仿成風的唱片相比；不過，少數吹毛求疵的評論者認為其歌詞陳腐老套。"},{"w":"extol","p":"v.","d":"To praise someone or something with great enthusiasm.","c":"頌揚；極力讚美","s":"In his travel journals, the eighteenth-century naturalist repeatedly extols the beauty of the Scottish Highlands, devoting page after page to the misty lochs, heather-covered hills, and soaring eagles that he believed rivaled any landscape in the Alps.","t":"在他的旅行日誌中，這位十八世紀的博物學家一再頌揚蘇格蘭高地之美，用了一頁又一頁的篇幅描寫霧氣繚繞的湖泊、長滿石楠的山丘與翱翔的老鷹，他認為這些景致足以媲美阿爾卑斯山的任何風光。","as":"Nutritionists extol the Mediterranean diet, yet they also warn that sedentary habits can be as detrimental to health as poor eating, and that even the most frugal meals cannot offset a lethargic lifestyle.","at":"營養學家大力推崇地中海飲食，但他們也警告，久坐不動的習慣對健康的危害不亞於不良飲食，即使是最簡樸的餐點也無法抵消懶散的生活方式所帶來的影響。"},{"w":"esteem","p":"v.","d":"To respect and admire someone highly.","c":"尊重；敬重；推崇","s":"Medieval Islamic scholars so highly esteemed the works of Aristotle that they translated, copied, and wrote extensive commentaries on them, preserving texts that might otherwise have been lost and later transmitting them to the universities of Europe.","t":"中世紀的伊斯蘭學者極為推崇亞里斯多德的著作，因此翻譯、抄寫並為之撰寫大量評註，保存了那些原本可能失傳的文本，日後更將它們傳入歐洲的大學。","as":"Colleagues esteemed the physician not only for her diagnostic skill but also for her altruistic devotion to indigent patients, and even her most cantankerous rivals conceded that her benevolent work was exemplary.","at":"同事們敬重這位醫師，不只因為她高超的診斷能力，也因為她無私地照顧貧困病患；就連她最難相處的對手也承認，她仁慈的工作堪稱典範。"},{"w":"exalt","p":"v.","d":"To praise highly or raise in rank or dignity.","c":"頌揚；提升地位","s":"Romantic poets such as Wordsworth sought to exalt the lives of ordinary rural people, portraying shepherds, farmers, and wanderers not as crude peasants but as figures of quiet dignity whose closeness to nature gave them a wisdom that city dwellers lacked.","t":"華茲華斯等浪漫主義詩人試圖頌揚鄉間平凡百姓的生活，將牧羊人、農夫與流浪者描繪成不是粗俗的鄉巴佬，而是帶著沉靜尊嚴的人物，他們親近大自然，因而擁有城市居民所欠缺的智慧。","as":"Propaganda posters exalted the dictator as a benevolent father of the nation, but historians argue that such ostentatious imagery merely concealed a regime that was both iniquitous and pernicious to the citizens it claimed to protect.","at":"宣傳海報將那位獨裁者頌揚為國家仁慈的父親，但歷史學家認為，這種浮誇的形象只是掩蓋了一個既邪惡、又對其聲稱要保護的人民有害的政權。"},{"w":"revere","p":"v.","d":"To feel deep respect or admiration for.","c":"尊崇；敬畏","s":"More than a decade after his death, Nelson Mandela is revered by South Africans of every background, and each year on his birthday millions of citizens honor his memory by spending sixty-seven minutes performing community service, one minute for each year of his public life.","t":"即使在曼德拉逝世十多年後，南非各種背景的人民依然尊崇他；每年在他生日那天，數百萬公民會花六十七分鐘從事社區服務來紀念他，每一分鐘代表他投身公共事務的一年。","as":"Villagers revered the elderly healer, whose taciturn manner and austere way of life lent her an air of quiet wisdom, and who remained magnanimous toward even the most cantankerous neighbors.","at":"村民們敬重那位年長的醫者；她沉默寡言的舉止和簡樸的生活方式，讓她散發出一種沉靜的智慧，而且她對最難相處的鄰居也始終寬宏大量。"},{"w":"eulogize","p":"v.","d":"To praise highly, especially in a speech honoring someone who has died.","c":"頌揚；致悼詞讚美","s":"At the state funeral, the former president was eulogized by leaders from both parties, who set aside years of bitter rivalry to recall his courage during the economic crisis and his willingness to compromise when the nation needed unity most.","t":"在國葬典禮上，兩黨領袖都為這位前總統致詞頌揚；他們擱下多年來激烈的競爭，回顧他在經濟危機期間的勇氣，以及在國家最需要團結時願意妥協的胸襟。","as":"Speakers eulogized the late scientist as a magnanimous mentor, recalling how she had alleviated her students' anxieties and remained humble despite acclaim that would have made a lesser person arrogant.","at":"致詞者頌揚這位已故科學家是一位寬宏大量的良師，回憶她如何減輕學生的焦慮，以及她雖獲得足以讓一般人變得傲慢的盛名，卻依然謙遜。"},{"w":"panegyrize","p":"v.","d":"To praise someone formally and elaborately in speech or writing.","c":"公開頌揚；撰文讚頌","s":"Court poets in Renaissance Florence were paid handsomely to panegyrize the Medici family, composing elaborate verses that compared Lorenzo de' Medici to ancient emperors and praised his patronage of artists as proof of his almost divine wisdom.","t":"文藝復興時期佛羅倫斯的宮廷詩人領取優渥的報酬來頌揚麥地奇家族，他們創作華麗的詩篇，將羅倫佐・德・麥地奇比作古代皇帝，並讚揚他對藝術家的贊助是他近乎神聖智慧的明證。","as":"Rather than panegyrizing the general, the honest biographer exposed his arrogant disregard for soldiers' lives and his contemptuous treatment of subordinates, refusing to repeat the grandiloquent myths of earlier accounts.","at":"這位誠實的傳記作者沒有頌揚那位將軍，反而揭露他對士兵性命的傲慢漠視，以及他對部屬的輕蔑對待，拒絕重複早期記述中那些浮誇的神話。"},{"w":"adulate","p":"v.","d":"To praise or admire someone excessively; to flatter.","c":"過度奉承；諂媚吹捧","s":"Psychologists studying celebrity culture have found that fans who adulate pop stars often attribute moral virtues to them that have no basis in evidence, treating the singers' casual remarks as profound wisdom and defending them fiercely against any criticism.","t":"研究名人文化的心理學家發現，過度崇拜流行歌星的粉絲常把一些毫無根據的道德美德套在偶像身上，將歌手隨口說出的話視為深刻的智慧，並激烈地為他們抵擋任何批評。","as":"The courtiers who adulated the king were obsequious and servile, and their fawning flattery left him so complacent that he ignored the ominous signs of rebellion spreading through his realm.","at":"那些對國王百般奉承的朝臣卑躬屈膝、奴顏婢膝，他們諂媚的吹捧讓國王自滿到忽視了在他國土上蔓延的不祥叛亂徵兆。"},{"w":"laud","p":"v.","d":"To praise highly, especially in public.","c":"稱讚；讚美","s":"Environmental groups lauded the city's decision to convert three abandoned rail lines into elevated parks, noting that the project not only provided green space to neighborhoods that had long lacked it but also reduced summer temperatures in nearby streets.","t":"環保團體大力讚揚市府將三條廢棄鐵路改建為高架公園的決定，並指出這項計畫不僅為長期缺乏綠地的社區提供綠色空間，也降低了周邊街道的夏季氣溫。","as":"The committee lauded the mediator for her ability to conciliate the rival factions, praising her affable manner and noting that her patient diplomacy had quelled tensions that once seemed intractable.","at":"委員會讚揚這位調解人能夠化解敵對派系之間的分歧，稱讚她和藹可親的態度，並指出她耐心的斡旋平息了曾經看似棘手難解的緊張局勢。"},{"w":"venerate","p":"v.","d":"To regard with deep, often religious, respect.","c":"崇敬；尊崇","s":"For more than a thousand years, pilgrims have traveled hundreds of kilometers on foot to venerate the relics believed to belong to Saint James at the cathedral in Santiago de Compostela, a journey that continues to draw over three hundred thousand walkers each year.","t":"一千多年來，朝聖者徒步跋涉數百公里，前往聖地牙哥－德孔波斯特拉大教堂，崇敬據信屬於聖雅各的聖髑；這條朝聖之路至今每年仍吸引超過三十萬名步行者。","as":"Generations of European scholars venerated the ancient philosopher, though modern critics argue that such reverence made academics complacent and strangely indifferent to the banal platitudes buried in his later writings.","at":"一代又一代的歐洲學者崇敬這位古代哲學家，但現代評論家認為，這樣的崇敬讓學者們變得自滿，對他晚期著作中那些陳腐的老生常談出奇地漠不關心。"}]},{"unit":20,"theme":"Abundance and Excess","themeZh":"豐富與過量","cards":[{"w":"surfeit","p":"n.","d":"An excessive amount of something; an oversupply.","c":"過量；過剩","s":"Economists explain that the sudden collapse in oil prices in 2020 resulted from a surfeit of crude: as lockdowns slashed demand for fuel, storage tanks around the world filled to capacity, and some producers briefly had to pay buyers to take barrels off their hands.","t":"經濟學家解釋，2020年油價突然崩跌是原油過剩所致：由於封城措施使燃料需求大減，全球的儲油槽都已滿載，部分生產商甚至一度必須付錢請買家把一桶桶原油運走。","as":"A surfeit of lavish banquets left the prodigal prince lethargic and indolent, and his worried advisers warned that such ostentatious extravagance would prove detrimental to the kingdom's already depleted treasury.","at":"過多的奢華宴席讓那位揮霍無度的王子變得昏沉懶散，他憂心的顧問們警告，如此張揚的鋪張浪費將會損害王國早已空虛的國庫。"},{"w":"profuse","p":"adj.","d":"Plentiful, abundant, or pouring out freely.","c":"大量的；豐富的；毫不吝惜的","s":"Doctors treating heat stroke watch carefully for a sudden end to profuse sweating, since a patient who stops perspiring despite a soaring body temperature may be losing the ability to cool down, a sign that organ damage could soon follow.","t":"治療中暑的醫師會密切留意大量出汗是否突然停止，因為若患者在體溫飆升時卻不再流汗，可能代表身體正在失去散熱能力，這是器官即將受損的徵兆。","as":"The executive's profuse apologies failed to placate the angry shareholders, who considered his contrition insincere and censured him for squandering millions on ostentatious offices while the company's profits steadily declined.","at":"那位高階主管連連道歉，卻未能安撫憤怒的股東；股東們認為他的悔意並不真誠，並譴責他在公司獲利持續下滑之際，仍將數百萬元揮霍在浮誇的辦公室上。"},{"w":"plethora","p":"n.","d":"A very large or excessive amount of something.","c":"過多；大量","s":"Behavioral economists have shown that a plethora of options can actually discourage purchases: in one famous study, shoppers offered twenty-four varieties of jam were far less likely to buy any than shoppers offered only six, apparently overwhelmed by the difficulty of choosing.","t":"行為經濟學家發現，過多的選擇反而會降低購買意願：在一項著名研究中，面對二十四種果醬的顧客，購買任何一種的可能性遠低於只面對六種的顧客，他們顯然被選擇的困難壓得喘不過氣。","as":"The government report offered a plethora of statistics, but its verbose analysis and cryptic charts only confounded readers, and critics lamented that the authors seemed indifferent to clarity and accessibility.","at":"這份政府報告提供了大量的統計數據，但其冗長的分析與晦澀的圖表只讓讀者更加困惑，評論者感嘆作者們似乎毫不在意內容是否清楚易懂。"},{"w":"myriad","p":"adj.","d":"Countless or extremely great in number.","c":"無數的；極多的","s":"Using the James Webb Space Telescope, astronomers captured a single image of a patch of sky no larger than a grain of sand held at arm's length, yet it revealed myriad galaxies, some of them so distant that their light had traveled for over thirteen billion years to reach the telescope.","t":"天文學家利用詹姆斯・韋伯太空望遠鏡拍攝了一張影像，畫面中的天空範圍不比伸直手臂時拿著的一粒沙大，卻揭示了無數個星系，其中有些極為遙遠，其光芒傳遞了超過一百三十億年才抵達望遠鏡。","as":"The novelist's sprawling saga, a labyrinth of myriad characters, rival families, and intersecting subplots, may strike readers who prefer a succinct narrative as confounding rather than charming, though admirers praise its ambition.","at":"這位小說家篇幅浩大的長篇作品，宛如一座由無數角色、敵對家族與交錯支線構成的迷宮；偏好簡潔敘事的讀者可能會覺得它令人困惑而非迷人，不過欣賞者則讚揚其雄心。"},{"w":"copious","p":"adj.","d":"Abundant and plentiful in quantity.","c":"大量的；豐富的","s":"Charles Darwin kept copious notes throughout his five-year voyage on the Beagle, filling dozens of notebooks with sketches, measurements, and observations of finches, tortoises, and fossils that he would study for decades before publishing On the Origin of Species.","t":"查爾斯・達爾文在乘坐小獵犬號的五年航程中做了大量筆記，數十本筆記本裡寫滿了對雀鳥、陸龜與化石的素描、測量與觀察紀錄，他在出版《物種起源》之前，花了數十年研究這些資料。","as":"The austere monks politely rejected the copious offerings of wealthy pilgrims, believing that such lavish gifts would make them complacent and gradually undermine the frugal way of life their order demanded.","at":"那些過著嚴格苦修生活的僧侶婉拒了富有朝聖者的大量供品，他們認為如此豐厚的禮物會讓他們變得自滿，並逐漸破壞修會所要求的簡樸生活方式。"},{"w":"ample","p":"adj.","d":"Enough or more than enough; plentiful.","c":"充裕的；足夠的","s":"Although the defense attorneys argued that their client had been wrongly accused, the prosecution presented ample evidence of his guilt, including security footage, fingerprints on the stolen safe, and bank records showing large deposits made the morning after the robbery.","t":"儘管辯護律師主張他們的當事人遭到誣告，檢方仍提出了充分的有罪證據，包括監視器畫面、遭竊保險箱上的指紋，以及顯示搶案隔天早上有大筆存款的銀行紀錄。","as":"Even with ample and reliable funding from private donors, the project faltered under an apathetic manager whose lethargic leadership and indifferent attitude toward deadlines turned a promising initiative into a debacle.","at":"即使有私人捐款者提供的充裕資金，這項計畫仍在一位冷漠的經理手下停滯不前；他萎靡的領導和對期限漠不關心的態度，讓一個前景看好的計畫淪為一場慘敗。"}]},{"unit":21,"theme":"Food and Eating","themeZh":"飲食","cards":[{"w":"abstemious","p":"adj.","d":"Moderate or sparing in eating and drinking.","c":"飲食有節制的；節制的","s":"Longitudinal studies of centenarians in Okinawa suggest that their abstemious habits — rising from the table while still slightly hungry and rarely consuming alcohol — may contribute as much to their longevity as genetics, since chronic overeating accelerates the cellular damage associated with aging.","t":"針對沖繩百歲人瑞的長期研究顯示，他們飲食有節制的習慣——吃到微飽便離開餐桌，且很少飲酒——對長壽的貢獻可能不亞於基因，因為長期暴飲暴食會加速與老化相關的細胞損傷。","as":"The monk's abstemious diet struck visiting merchants as austere, even penurious, yet he insisted that his frugal meals of rice and boiled greens were a spiritual discipline rather than a sign of poverty, and he never presumed to extol such restraint to others.","at":"這位僧侶飲食節制，在來訪商人眼中顯得簡樸，甚至貧寒；然而他堅稱自己以米飯和水煮青菜為主的儉樸餐食是一種修行，而非貧窮的象徵，而且他從不自以為是地向他人頌揚這種克制。"},{"w":"delectable","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely delicious and pleasing to the taste.","c":"美味可口的；令人愉快的","s":"The tomato, now considered one of the most delectableingredients in Mediterranean cooking, was long regarded with suspicion in northern Europe, where botanists classified it alongside poisonous nightshades such as belladonna and many cooks refused to serve it for nearly two centuries.","t":"番茄如今被視為地中海料理中最美味可口的食材之一，卻曾長期在歐洲北部遭人猜疑，因為植物學家將它與顛茄等有毒的茄科植物歸為同類，許多廚師將近兩個世紀都不肯以它入菜。","as":"The food critic, usually so captious that chefs dreaded her visits, could only extol the lavish, delectable tasting menu, conceding in her review that even its humblest course was anything but insipid.","at":"這位美食評論家向來吹毛求疵，令廚師們聞之色變，這次卻只能盛讚那套豐盛又美味可口的品嚐菜單，並在評論中承認，即使是其中最樸素的一道菜也絕不平淡無味。"},{"w":"emaciated","p":"adj.","d":"Abnormally thin and weak, especially from hunger or illness.","c":"憔悴的；瘦弱的；骨瘦如柴的","s":"Photographs of emaciated prisoners released from wartime camps, their ribs visible beneath paper-thin skin, prompted physicians to study refeeding syndrome, a dangerous condition in which a starving patient's body is overwhelmed when nourishment is reintroduced too quickly after prolonged deprivation.","t":"從戰時集中營獲釋、骨瘦如柴的囚犯照片中，他們的肋骨在薄如紙的皮膚下清晰可見，這促使醫師研究「再餵食症候群」——一種長期挨餓的患者在恢復進食過快時，身體因負荷不了而陷入險境的病症。","as":"The emaciated polar bear, stranded on a shrinking ice floe, became an ominous emblem of climate change; even viewers who had found the science confounding conceded that the loss of sea ice was clearly detrimental to Arctic predators.","at":"那隻困在日漸縮小的浮冰上、骨瘦如柴的北極熊，成了氣候變遷的不祥象徵；就連原本覺得相關科學令人困惑的觀眾也承認，海冰流失顯然對北極的掠食動物有害。"},{"w":"alimentary","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to food, nourishment, or digestion.","c":"營養的；飲食的；消化的","s":"Because the alimentary canal stretches roughly nine meters through the human body and hosts trillions of microbes, gastroenterologists increasingly treat it not as a simple tube for processing food but as a complex ecosystem that influences immunity, metabolism, and even mood.","t":"由於消化道在人體內綿延約九公尺，並寄居著數以兆計的微生物，腸胃科醫師越來越不把它視為單純處理食物的管道，而是一個會影響免疫、代謝甚至情緒的複雜生態系統。","as":"Medieval physicians offered myriad remedies for alimentary complaints, but their cures were often deleterious rather than helpful: purging, bloodletting, and copious mercury tonics only compounded the turmoil in a patient's already ailing stomach.","at":"中世紀的醫師針對消化方面的病痛提出了無數療法，但這些療法往往有害無益：催瀉、放血和大量的水銀藥劑，只會讓患者本已不適的腸胃更加翻騰。"},{"w":"culinary","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to cooking or the kitchen.","c":"烹飪的；廚藝的","s":"When UNESCO added Japanese washoku to its list of intangible cultural heritage in 2013, it recognized not a single dish but an entire culinary tradition — seasonal ingredients, precise knife work, and rituals of presentation — that had been passed down through generations of home cooks.","t":"聯合國教科文組織於2013年將日本「和食」列入非物質文化遺產名錄時，所肯定的不是單一菜餚，而是一整套烹飪傳統——當令食材、精準的刀工，以及擺盤的儀式——這些都由一代代家庭廚師傳承下來。","as":"Critics once dismissed fusion cooking as derivative and banal, but the chef's culinary experiments, which paired Taiwanese night-market snacks with French technique, won acclaim from even the most disdainful gourmets in Paris.","at":"評論家曾把融合料理貶為缺乏原創、陳腐乏味，但這位主廚將台灣夜市小吃與法式技法結合的烹飪實驗，卻連巴黎最不屑一顧的美食家都讚不絕口。"},{"w":"epicurean","p":"adj.","d":"Devoted to refined pleasure, especially fine food and drink.","c":"講究美食的；享樂主義的","s":"The Gilded Age financier's epicurean tastes were legendary: his private railway car carried a French chef, a cellar of vintage Bordeaux, and crates of oysters packed in ice, so that he could dine on twelve-course feasts while crossing the most desolate stretches of the American West.","t":"這位鍍金時代金融家講究美食的品味堪稱傳奇：他的私人鐵路車廂載著一位法國主廚、一整窖陳年波爾多葡萄酒，以及一箱箱冰鎮生蠔，讓他即使穿越美國西部最荒涼的地帶，也能享用十二道菜的盛宴。","as":"Ironically, Epicurus himself favored frugal meals of bread and water; the epicurean lifestyle now associated with his name — lavish feasts, rare wines, and ostentatious dining rooms — would have struck the philosopher as a prodigal pursuit of pleasures that ultimately bring more pain than contentment.","at":"諷刺的是，伊比鳩魯本人偏好以麵包和清水為主的簡樸餐食；如今與他名字連在一起的享樂式生活——奢華的盛宴、珍稀的美酒和炫耀的餐廳——在這位哲學家看來，只是揮霍無度地追求那些最終帶來的痛苦多於滿足的享樂。"},{"w":"glutton","p":"n.","d":"A person who habitually eats and drinks too much.","c":"貪吃的人；暴食者","s":"In Dante's Inferno, the gluttons of the third circle lie in freezing, filthy slush beneath an endless rain, a punishment that mirrors their earthly sin: having made food and drink the center of their lives, they are reduced to wallowing in garbage like swine.","t":"在但丁的《地獄篇》中，第三層地獄的暴食者躺在無盡冷雨下冰冷污穢的泥濘裡，這種懲罰呼應了他們生前的罪孽：他們把飲食當成生活的重心，如今便淪落到像豬一樣在穢物中打滾。","as":"The Roman emperor Vitellius was a notorious glutton whose prodigal banquets squandered the treasury, and contemporary historians, never chary of moral judgment, did not hesitate to castigate him for his voracious appetite.","at":"羅馬皇帝維特里烏斯是出了名的暴食者，他揮霍無度的盛宴耗盡了國庫；而同時代的史家向來不吝於道德評判，毫不猶豫地嚴厲抨擊他貪得無厭的胃口。"},{"w":"palatable","p":"adj.","d":"Pleasant to taste; acceptable or agreeable.","c":"可口的；美味的；可接受的","s":"To make bitter quinine more palatable to British soldiers stationed in malaria-ridden India, colonial officers mixed the medicine with soda water, sugar, and gin, inadvertently inventing the gin and tonic, a cocktail that remains popular long after its medicinal purpose has been forgotten.","t":"為了讓駐紮在瘧疾肆虐的印度的英國士兵更容易入口苦澀的奎寧，殖民地軍官將這種藥物與蘇打水、糖和琴酒混合，無意間發明了琴通寧——這款雞尾酒的藥用目的早已被遺忘，卻至今仍廣受歡迎。","as":"To make the austere reform package more palatable to a vociferous opposition, the finance minister offered to mitigate the proposed tax increases, a conciliatory gesture that briefly allayed fears of a general strike.","at":"為了讓這套緊縮改革方案更能被大聲疾呼的反對派接受，財政部長提議減輕擬議中的增稅幅度，這個和解姿態一度平息了外界對大罷工的憂慮。"},{"w":"ravenous","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely hungry; eager for food.","c":"極餓的；飢腸轆轆的；貪婪的","s":"After emerging from months of hibernation having lost up to a third of their body weight, grizzly bears are ravenous and spend nearly every waking hour foraging for roots, carrion, and newborn elk calves to rebuild the fat reserves they will need before winter returns.","t":"灰熊結束數個月的冬眠時，體重可能已減少多達三分之一，因此飢腸轆轆，幾乎每個清醒的時刻都在搜尋植物根莖、腐肉和剛出生的麋鹿幼崽，以重新累積冬天再度來臨前所需的脂肪。","as":"The ravenous troops, exhausted by weeks of retreat through a frozen labyrinth of mountain passes, were too listless to forage, and their commander's precarious supply lines collapsed into a debacle that historians still study today.","at":"飢腸轆轆的部隊在冰封如迷宮般的山間隘口撤退了數週，早已精疲力竭、無精打采，無力再去搜尋糧食；而指揮官岌岌可危的補給線最終崩潰，釀成一場至今仍為史家研究的慘敗。"},{"w":"savory","p":"adj.","d":"Salty or spicy rather than sweet; appetizing.","c":"鹹香的；美味的；可口的","s":"Japanese chemist Kikunae Ikeda identified glutamate as the source of the rich, savory flavor in seaweed broth in 1908, naming this fifth basic taste umami and arguing that it was as fundamental to human perception as sweetness, sourness, saltiness, and bitterness.","t":"日本化學家池田菊苗於1908年確認，麩胺酸是昆布高湯中濃郁鹹香風味的來源，並將這第五種基本味覺命名為「鮮味」，主張它與甜、酸、鹹、苦一樣，都是人類味覺的基本要素。","as":"The aroma of savory dumplings drifted through the night market, and even the most phlegmatic passersby, who had seemed indifferent to the clamor of the vendors, paused to join the line that snaked past the stalls.","at":"鹹香的餃子香氣在夜市中飄散，就連最冷靜淡漠、看似對攤販吆喝聲毫不在意的路人，也停下腳步，加入那條蜿蜒穿過攤位的排隊人龍。"}]},{"unit":22,"theme":"Caution and Care","themeZh":"謹慎與細心","cards":[{"w":"circumspect","p":"adj.","d":"Careful to consider all risks before acting or speaking.","c":"謹慎的；周到的；慎重的","s":"Aware that a single careless remark could rattle global markets, the central bank governor remained circumspect throughout the press conference, weighing every phrase before answering and declining to speculate about future interest-rate decisions until the latest inflation data had been thoroughly analyzed.","t":"這位央行總裁深知一句不經意的發言就可能撼動全球市場，因此在整場記者會中始終保持謹慎，每句話都先斟酌再回答，並且在最新的通膨數據經過徹底分析之前，拒絕臆測未來的利率決策。","as":"Normally voluble in interviews, the novelist became circumspect when asked about her estranged brother, offering only terse, cryptic replies that left the assembled reporters more curious than before and fueled weeks of speculation in the literary press.","at":"這位小說家平常在訪談中滔滔不絕，但被問到與她疏遠的哥哥時卻變得十分謹慎，只給出簡短而費解的回答，讓在場記者比先前更加好奇，也在文學媒體上引發了數週的揣測。"},{"w":"conscientious","p":"adj.","d":"Careful to do one's work or duty thoroughly and well.","c":"認真負責的；盡責的；本著良心的","s":"Years before she developed one of the first compilers, Grace Hopper was known as a conscientious mathematician whose team kept detailed logbooks of every malfunction in the Harvard Mark II; in one of them, the team famously taped the moth that had short-circuited a relay in 1947.","t":"在開發出最早的編譯器之一的數年前，葛麗絲・霍普就以認真負責的數學家著稱，她的團隊將哈佛馬克二號電腦的每一次故障都詳細記錄在日誌中；團隊曾在其中一本日誌裡，貼上一隻在1947年導致繼電器短路的飛蛾，此事廣為人知。","as":"Unlike his indolent predecessor, the conscientious new curator scrutinized every single catalogue entry, and his meticulous research revealed that several of the museum's most prized paintings were spurious copies rather than genuine Renaissance works.","at":"不同於怠惰的前任，這位認真負責的新任策展人仔細審查每一筆目錄資料，而他一絲不苟的研究揭露，博物館好幾幅最受珍視的畫作其實是贗品，而非真正的文藝復興時期作品。"},{"w":"exacting","p":"adj.","d":"Demanding great effort, skill, or precision.","c":"嚴格要求的；費力的；苛求的","s":"The restoration of Notre-Dame's medieval timber roof proved extraordinarily exacting: carpenters had to shape each oak beam with hand axes, using only the tools and techniques available to thirteenth-century builders, so that the reconstructed frame would match the original in every structural detail.","t":"巴黎聖母院中世紀木造屋頂的修復工程極為嚴苛：木匠必須只用十三世紀建築工匠所能使用的工具與技法，以手斧逐一削製每根橡木樑，好讓重建的屋架在每個結構細節上都與原貌相符。","as":"The conductor's exacting standards made him seem cantankerous to many musicians, yet even those who chafed under his rebukes conceded that his rehearsals transformed a discordant student ensemble into a remarkably vibrant orchestra.","at":"這位指揮家的嚴格標準讓許多樂手覺得他脾氣古怪難搞，但即使那些對他的斥責心懷不滿的人也承認，他的排練將一個不和諧的學生樂團，蛻變成一支極富活力的管弦樂團。"},{"w":"gingerly","p":"adj.","d":"Showing great care and caution to avoid harm.","c":"小心翼翼的；謹慎的","s":"Because the two-thousand-year-old Herculaneum scrolls had been carbonized by the eruption of Vesuvius, early researchers' attempts to unroll them by hand had to be painfully gingerly, yet even the most delicate efforts often reduced the brittle papyrus to black flakes.","t":"由於兩千年前的赫庫蘭尼姆古卷在維蘇威火山爆發時已被碳化，早期研究人員徒手展開古卷的嘗試必須極其小心翼翼，然而即使是最輕柔的動作，也常常使脆弱的莎草紙碎成黑色殘片。","as":"After the earthquake, rescue workers made gingerly progress across the precarious rubble, mindful that any rash movement could prove detrimental to survivors trapped below, while an engineer watched for ominous movements of debris on the slope above.","at":"地震過後，救援人員在搖搖欲墜的瓦礫堆上小心翼翼地緩慢前進，深知任何魯莽的舉動都可能危及受困在下方的倖存者，同時一位工程師留意著上方斜坡上碎石是否出現不祥的鬆動。"},{"w":"vigilant","p":"adj.","d":"Keeping careful watch for possible danger or difficulty.","c":"警惕的；警覺的；戒備的","s":"Epidemiologists urged public-health agencies to remain vigilant even after case numbers had fallen, warning that the virus could mutate in animal reservoirs and re-emerge without warning, so wastewater testing and hospital surveillance should continue long after the immediate crisis appeared to have passed.","t":"流行病學家呼籲公共衛生機構即使在病例數下降後仍應保持警覺，並警告病毒可能在動物宿主體內突變並毫無預警地再度出現，因此在眼前的危機看似過去之後，污水檢測與醫院監測仍應長期持續。","as":"A vigilant auditor noticed a small discrepancy in the charity's annual accounts, and her persistent inquiry exposed a nefarious scheme in which devious executives had quietly funneled philanthropic donations into their own private offshore accounts.","at":"一位警覺的稽核員發現這家慈善機構年度帳目中的一處小小差異，她鍥而不捨的調查揭露了一樁邪惡的陰謀：狡詐的高層主管悄悄把慈善捐款轉入了他們自己在海外的私人帳戶。"},{"w":"meticulous","p":"adj.","d":"Showing extreme attention to every small detail.","c":"一絲不苟的；極為細心的","s":"Tycho Brahe's meticulous observations of planetary positions, recorded night after night for over twenty years without a telescope, were accurate enough that his assistant Johannes Kepler could later use them to prove that planets travel in elliptical rather than circular orbits.","t":"第谷・布拉赫在沒有望遠鏡的情況下，二十多年來夜復一夜地記錄行星位置，這些一絲不苟的觀測精確到他的助手克卜勒後來得以藉此證明，行星沿橢圓軌道而非圓形軌道運行。","as":"The forger's meticulous imitation of Vermeer's brushwork fooled even erudite critics, and the scandal that followed was a debacle for the museum, which had lavished praise and money on a spurious masterpiece.","at":"這名偽造者一絲不苟地模仿維梅爾的筆觸，連學識淵博的評論家都被騙過；隨之而來的醜聞對博物館而言是一場慘敗，因為館方曾對這幅偽造的「傑作」大加讚揚、投入鉅資。"},{"w":"wary","p":"adj.","d":"Cautious and alert to possible danger or problems.","c":"機警的；謹慎的；提防的","s":"Having watched several overhyped technologies collapse within a decade, many venture capitalists have grown wary of start-ups that promise revolutionary breakthroughs but cannot produce independent evidence that their products work, preferring to fund companies with modest claims and verifiable results.","t":"眼見好幾項被過度炒作的科技在十年內垮台，許多創投業者已對那些宣稱能帶來革命性突破、卻拿不出獨立證據證明產品有效的新創公司心存戒心，寧可投資那些主張保守但成果可驗證的公司。","as":"Wary of the senator's grandiloquent promises, the skeptical journalist suspected that his lavish praise for the education reform bill was merely a pretext for a pernicious plan to quietly defund the state's public schools.","at":"這位抱持懷疑的記者對參議員浮誇的承諾心存戒心，她懷疑參議員對教育改革法案的大肆讚揚，只是為了掩護一項悄悄削減州立公立學校經費的有害計畫。"},{"w":"chary","p":"adj.","d":"Cautiously reluctant to do or give something.","c":"謹慎的；不輕易的；吝於給予的","s":"Burned by a series of retracted studies, the editors of the medical journal became chary of publishing findings based on small samples, now requiring authors to share their raw data and to replicate key results before any article reporting a dramatic new treatment could appear in print.","t":"在一連串研究遭撤稿後吃了苦頭，這本醫學期刊的編輯對刊登小樣本研究結果變得十分謹慎，如今要求作者公開原始數據，並在任何報導重大新療法的文章付印之前，先重複驗證關鍵結果。","as":"The reclusive composer, always chary of praise and reticent in interviews, deeply distrusted music critics who would extol a new symphony one season and then castigate the very same work the next, depending on fashion.","at":"這位隱居的作曲家向來不輕易稱讚他人，在訪談中也沉默寡言；他深深不信任那些隨潮流而變、這一季大肆頌揚某首新交響曲、下一季又嚴厲抨擊同一部作品的樂評家。"},{"w":"heedful","p":"adj.","d":"Paying close attention to a warning or advice.","c":"留心的；注意的；留意的","s":"Mountaineers who are heedful of subtle changes in the weather, such as a sudden drop in barometric pressure or the appearance of lens-shaped clouds over the summit, often turn back before a storm strikes, while those who ignore such signs risk being trapped on exposed ridges.","t":"對天氣細微變化保持留心的登山者——例如氣壓驟降，或山頂上方出現莢狀雲——往往能在暴風雨來襲前折返，而忽視這些徵兆的人則可能受困於毫無遮蔽的山脊上。","as":"Heedful of the ominous cracks spreading across the dam, the engineer refused to remain complacent and urged officials to evacuate the valley, warning that any further delay could prove deleterious to thousands of residents.","at":"這位工程師留意到大壩上不斷擴大、令人不安的裂縫，拒絕安於現狀，並敦促官員疏散河谷居民，警告任何進一步的延誤都可能對數千名居民造成傷害。"},{"w":"scrupulous","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely careful, thorough, and honest about doing what is right.","c":"一絲不苟的；嚴謹的；正直的","s":"Historians praise the scrupulous record-keeping of Venetian merchants, whose double-entry account books, kept with careful honesty for every transaction from bolts of silk to sacks of pepper, allow modern economists to reconstruct Mediterranean trade networks with remarkable precision.","t":"歷史學家讚揚威尼斯商人一絲不苟的記帳方式：他們以複式記帳法誠實而仔細地記錄每一筆交易，從一匹匹絲綢到一袋袋胡椒，使現代經濟學家得以極為精確地重建地中海的貿易網絡。","as":"A scrupulous judge, she refused even modest gifts from litigants, and her unwavering integrity stood in stark contrast to the mercenary conduct of colleagues who had been censured for accepting bribes.","at":"她是一位正直嚴謹的法官，連訴訟當事人送的小禮物都一概拒絕；她堅定不移的操守，與那些因收受賄賂而遭到譴責、唯利是圖的同僚形成強烈對比。"}]},{"unit":23,"theme":"Fleeting and Wandering","themeZh":"短暫與漂泊","cards":[{"w":"evanescent","p":"adj.","d":"Quickly fading or vanishing from sight or memory.","c":"瞬息即逝的；轉瞬消失的","s":"Physicists at CERN must rely on sophisticated detectors to study the Higgs boson, an evanescent particle that decays into lighter particles less than a trillionth of a billionth of a second after it is created, leaving only indirect traces of its brief existence.","t":"歐洲核子研究組織的物理學家必須仰賴精密的偵測器來研究希格斯玻色子；這種轉瞬即逝的粒子在生成後不到一兆分之一的十億分之一秒內就會衰變成較輕的粒子，只留下其短暫存在的間接痕跡。","as":"The evanescent glow of bioluminescent plankton along the shore enthralled tourists, but marine biologists warned that pernicious runoff and stagnant coastal waters were threatening the delicate ecosystem that produced such a vibrant display.","at":"海岸邊生物發光浮游生物那轉瞬即逝的光芒令遊客著迷，但海洋生物學家警告，有害的逕流與停滯的近岸海水，正威脅著孕育出如此絢麗景象的脆弱生態系統。"},{"w":"transient","p":"adj.","d":"Lasting only a short time; staying briefly in a place.","c":"短暫的；瞬息的；暫住的","s":"Economists cautioned that the sudden spike in gasoline prices was likely transient, a temporary consequence of a refinery fire and a hurricane in the Gulf of Mexico, rather than a sign of the persistent, broad-based inflation that would justify raising interest rates.","t":"經濟學家提醒，汽油價格的突然飆升很可能只是短暫的，是一場煉油廠火災和墨西哥灣颶風所造成的暫時後果，而非足以構成升息理由的持續性、全面性通膨的徵兆。","as":"The reform movement's popularity proved transient; once its zealous leaders fell into acrimonious disputes, their vociferous rallies dwindled, and the public grew apathetic toward causes it had once ardently supported.","at":"這場改革運動的聲勢只是曇花一現；一旦熱忱的領袖們陷入尖刻的爭執，他們大聲疾呼的集會便日漸冷清，民眾也對自己曾熱烈支持的理念變得漠不關心。"},{"w":"transitory","p":"adj.","d":"Not permanent; lasting only a brief time.","c":"短暫的；暫時的","s":"Buddhist teachings emphasize that all worldly pleasures are transitory, arising and passing away like waves on the surface of the sea, and that suffering stems from clinging to wealth, fame, and comfort as though they could provide lasting security or happiness.","t":"佛教教義強調，世間一切享樂都是短暫無常的，如同海面上的波浪般生滅起落；而痛苦正源於執著於財富、名聲與安逸，彷彿它們能帶來長久的安穩或幸福。","as":"The pop star's fame turned out to be transitory: after a brief period of being lauded by critics and adulated by fans, her derivative second album was dismissed as hackneyed, and she quickly faded from public view.","at":"這位流行歌手的名氣原來只是短暫的：在一段短暫受到評論家讚揚、歌迷崇拜的時期之後，她缺乏原創性的第二張專輯被斥為陳腔濫調，她也很快淡出了大眾視野。"},{"w":"ephemeral","p":"adj.","d":"Lasting for a very short time.","c":"短暫的；朝生暮死的","s":"Mayflies are among the most ephemeral creatures on Earth: after spending up to two years as aquatic larvae, the adults emerge without functional mouths, mate within hours, and die before the following sunrise, their entire winged existence compressed into a single day.","t":"蜉蝣是地球上壽命最短暫的生物之一：牠們以水生幼蟲的形態度過長達兩年的時間，羽化成蟲後卻沒有能進食的口器，在數小時內交配，並在隔天日出前死去，整個有翅膀的生命被壓縮在短短一天之內。","as":"Social media trends are notoriously ephemeral, and marketers who chase every viral meme often produce banal, insipid campaigns built on hackneyed slogans that consumers forget almost as soon as they scroll past them.","at":"社群媒體上的潮流出了名的短暫，追逐每一個爆紅迷因的行銷人員，往往做出建立在陳腔濫調標語上、平庸乏味的宣傳活動，消費者幾乎一滑過去就忘了。"},{"w":"peripatetic","p":"adj.","d":"Traveling from place to place, especially for work.","c":"巡迴的；漫遊的；四處奔走的","s":"During the Renaissance, many painters led peripatetic careers, moving from one princely court to another in search of commissions, so that an artist like Leonardo da Vinci worked in Florence, Milan, Venice, and Rome before finally settling in France at the invitation of King Francis I.","t":"文藝復興時期，許多畫家過著四處奔走的職業生涯，在各個王侯宮廷之間輾轉尋求委託案；因此像達文西這樣的藝術家，曾先後在佛羅倫斯、米蘭、威尼斯和羅馬工作，最後才應法王法蘭索瓦一世之邀定居法國。","as":"The peripatetic journalist, never content to remain sedentary, roamed the world's war zones for three decades, and her ardent dispatches about turmoil and adversity in forgotten places earned acclaim from readers around the world.","at":"這位四處奔走的記者從不甘於久坐不動，三十年來穿梭於世界各地的戰區，她對被遺忘之地的動盪與苦難所寫的熱切報導，贏得了世界各地讀者的讚譽。"},{"w":"nomadic","p":"adj.","d":"Moving from place to place without a permanent home.","c":"遊牧的；流浪的","s":"For centuries, the Mongols maintained a nomadic way of life on the Central Asian steppe, moving their felt tents and herds of horses, sheep, and yaks between summer and winter pastures to prevent overgrazing in the harsh, arid grasslands.","t":"數百年來，蒙古人在中亞草原上維持著遊牧的生活方式，在夏季與冬季牧場之間遷移他們的氈帳以及成群的馬、羊和犛牛，以避免在嚴酷乾旱的草原上過度放牧。","as":"Colonial administrators, contemptuous of nomadic herders, tried to force them into sedentary villages, but the policy proved detrimental, as pastures became overgrazed and once-thriving communities sank into penurious dependence on aid.","at":"殖民地官員輕視遊牧民族，試圖迫使他們遷入定居的村落，但這項政策證明是有害的：牧場遭到過度放牧，曾經興盛的社群也陷入仰賴援助的貧困處境。"},{"w":"itinerant","p":"adj.","d":"Traveling from place to place to work.","c":"巡迴的；流動的；四處奔波的","s":"In nineteenth-century America, itinerant portrait painters traveled from town to town along rivers and turnpikes, offering to capture a family's likeness for a modest fee, and many of the anonymous works they left behind are now prized by folk-art collectors.","t":"在十九世紀的美國，巡迴肖像畫家沿著河流與收費公路從一個城鎮走到另一個城鎮，以低廉的費用為人家畫像，他們留下的許多無名作品如今深受民俗藝術收藏家珍視。","as":"The itinerant preacher was a gifted orator whose eloquence and impassioned sermons drew enormous crowds in every frontier town he visited, though some established clergy derided his rhetorical flourishes as mere grandiloquent showmanship.","at":"這位巡迴傳教士是位天賦異稟的演說家，他的雄辯與激昂的布道在他造訪的每個邊疆小鎮都吸引大批群眾，儘管有些體制內的神職人員嘲笑他的修辭技巧只是浮誇的表演。"},{"w":"fleeting","p":"adj.","d":"Passing swiftly; lasting only a moment.","c":"稍縱即逝的；短暫的","s":"Astronomers detected the gravitational waves produced by two colliding black holes as a fleeting signal lasting only a fifth of a second, yet that tiny ripple in spacetime confirmed a prediction Albert Einstein had made a century earlier in his general theory of relativity.","t":"天文學家偵測到兩個碰撞黑洞所產生的重力波，那只是一個持續僅五分之一秒、稍縱即逝的訊號，然而這道時空中的微小漣漪，卻證實了愛因斯坦一個世紀前在廣義相對論中提出的預測。","as":"The candidate's fleeting moment of levity during an otherwise contentious televised debate charmed millions of viewers, briefly softening his long-standing reputation as an aloof and haughty politician who rarely connected with ordinary voters.","at":"在這場原本火藥味十足的電視辯論中，這位候選人短暫流露的幽默打動了數百萬觀眾，一時軟化了他長久以來冷漠高傲、很少與一般選民產生共鳴的政治人物形象。"},{"w":"volatile","p":"adj.","d":"Liable to change rapidly and unpredictably.","c":"易變的；不穩定的；揮發性的","s":"Cryptocurrency prices have proved extraordinarily volatile, sometimes rising or falling by more than twenty percent in a single day in response to a celebrity's social media post or rumors of new government regulation, making them a risky choice for retirement savings.","t":"加密貨幣的價格已證明極度不穩定，有時會因名人在社群媒體上的一則貼文或政府即將出台新規範的傳聞，而在一天之內漲跌超過百分之二十，因此用來作為退休儲蓄是一項風險很高的選擇。","as":"The volatile political climate, inflamed by belligerent rhetoric and rancorous partisanship on both sides, left moderate legislators in a quandary about whether to mediate between the warring factions or simply stay silent until the election.","at":"在雙方好戰的言論與充滿怨恨的黨派對立煽動下，這種動盪多變的政治氣候讓溫和派議員陷入兩難：究竟該在交戰的派系之間居中調停，還是乾脆保持沉默直到選舉結束。"}]},{"unit":24,"theme":"New and Old","themeZh":"新與舊","cards":[{"w":"contemporary","p":"adj.","d":"Belonging to the present time; modern.","c":"當代的；現代的；同時代的","s":"Although Shakespeare's plays were written more than four centuries ago, directors continue to stage them in contemporary settings — corporate boardrooms, refugee camps, and social-media-obsessed high schools — to show audiences that his insights into ambition, jealousy, and power remain strikingly relevant today.","t":"雖然莎士比亞的劇作寫於四百多年前，導演們仍不斷將它們搬上當代的場景——企業董事會議室、難民營，以及沉迷社群媒體的高中——藉此向觀眾展現，他對野心、嫉妒與權力的洞見至今依然切中時弊。","as":"Critics who once derided contemporary architecture as banal and derivative were forced to reconsider their views when the museum's daring glass pavilion, praised by ardent admirers from Tokyo to Berlin, won international acclaim.","at":"曾經嘲笑當代建築平庸又缺乏原創性的評論家，在這座博物館大膽的玻璃展館受到從東京到柏林的熱情擁護者讚賞、並贏得國際好評後，不得不重新思考自己的看法。"},{"w":"inception","p":"n.","d":"The beginning or establishment of something.","c":"開端；開始；創立","s":"From its inception in 1901, the Nobel Prize has generated controversy, as critics have repeatedly questioned why certain groundbreaking scientists and writers were overlooked while others whose achievements now seem modest received the honor and its substantial financial award.","t":"諾貝爾獎自1901年創立以來便爭議不斷，批評者一再質疑，為何某些具開創性的科學家與作家遭到忽視，而另一些如今看來成就平平的人卻獲得這項殊榮及其豐厚的獎金。","as":"Since its inception, the philanthropic foundation has drawn on the munificent gifts of a few donors to alleviate poverty in rural villages, though skeptics have impugned its motives as self-promotion.","at":"這個慈善基金會自創立以來，便仰賴少數捐款人的慷慨捐贈來減輕鄉村的貧困，儘管懷疑者質疑其動機只是為了自我宣傳。"},{"w":"innovation","p":"n.","d":"A new idea, method, or invention.","c":"創新；革新；新發明","s":"Economic historians argue that the shipping container, a simple steel box standardized in the 1950s, was one of the most consequential innovations of the twentieth century, cutting the cost of loading cargo by more than ninety percent and making modern globalized supply chains possible.","t":"經濟史學家認為，1950年代標準化的貨櫃——一個簡單的鋼製箱子——是二十世紀最具影響力的創新之一，它使裝貨成本降低了九成以上，也讓現代全球化的供應鏈成為可能。","as":"Hidebound executives dismissed the engineer's innovation as a frivolous gadget, but its unprecedented success forced the company's obstinate board to abandon its antiquated product line and embrace the new technology.","at":"守舊的高層主管把這位工程師的創新斥為無聊的小玩意，但它空前的成功迫使公司固執的董事會放棄過時的產品線，轉而擁抱這項新技術。"},{"w":"unprecedented","p":"adj.","d":"Never done, seen, or known before.","c":"空前的；史無前例的","s":"When the Apollo 11 astronauts landed on the Moon in July 1969, the event drew an unprecedented television audience of roughly 650 million people, a number far larger than any previous broadcast had attracted and a testament to the global reach of the new medium.","t":"1969年7月阿波羅11號太空人登陸月球時，這起事件吸引了約六億五千萬名電視觀眾，規模空前，遠遠超過以往任何一次轉播，也證明了這個新興媒體在全球的影響力。","as":"The unprecedented flood unleashed turmoil across the river delta, and the government's lackluster response, combined with officials' strangely apathetic public statements, only deepened popular animosity toward the ruling party in the months before the election.","at":"這場空前的洪水在河流三角洲各地造成動盪，而政府乏善可陳的應變，加上官員異常冷漠的公開發言，在選前幾個月只讓民眾對執政黨的敵意更加深重。"},{"w":"relic","p":"n.","d":"An object or custom surviving from an earlier time.","c":"遺物；遺跡；遺風","s":"Linguists regard certain spellings in modern English, such as the silent k in knight and knee, as relics of a period when those letters were actually pronounced, preserving traces of Old English sounds that disappeared from speech many centuries ago.","t":"語言學家認為，現代英語中的某些拼法，例如 knight 和 knee 中不發音的 k，是那些字母仍實際發音時代的遺跡，保存了早在數百年前就已從口語中消失的古英語發音痕跡。","as":"To younger voters, the aging senator's bellicose speeches seemed a relic of the Cold War, and his pompous, grandiloquent style struck many of them as more pretentious than persuasive in an era of short videos.","at":"對年輕選民而言，這位年邁參議員好戰的演說彷彿是冷戰時期的遺風；在短影音當道的時代，他浮誇、華而不實的風格在許多人看來，矯揉造作多於說服力。"},{"w":"obsolete","p":"adj.","d":"No longer used or needed; out of date.","c":"過時的；淘汰的；廢棄的","s":"The rapid spread of smartphones in the 2010s made a range of once-essential devices nearly obsolete within a single decade, as consumers abandoned standalone cameras, GPS units, alarm clocks, and music players in favor of one pocket-sized machine that could perform all of their functions.","t":"2010年代智慧型手機的迅速普及，使得一系列曾經不可或缺的裝置在短短十年內幾乎遭到淘汰，因為消費者紛紛捨棄獨立的相機、衛星導航裝置、鬧鐘和音樂播放器，改用一台能執行所有功能的口袋型機器。","as":"The textile factory's obsolete machinery, sluggish and prone to frequent breakdowns, had become a detrimental burden, yet the parsimonious owner refused to replace it, preferring to squander money on constant repairs that never solved the problem.","at":"這家紡織廠過時的機器運轉遲緩又常常故障，已成為一大負擔，然而吝嗇的老闆卻拒絕更換，寧可把錢浪費在始終解決不了問題的不斷維修上。"},{"w":"novel","p":"adj.","d":"New and original; unlike anything seen before.","c":"新穎的；新奇的","s":"Rather than relying on conventional antibiotics, researchers at the university developed a novel treatment for drug-resistant infections that uses specially engineered viruses to attack harmful bacteria while leaving the patient's own cells and beneficial microbes completely unharmed.","t":"研究人員並未仰賴傳統抗生素，而是開發出一種治療抗藥性感染的新穎療法，利用經過特殊改造的病毒攻擊有害細菌，同時完全不傷害病患自身的細胞與有益的微生物。","as":"Rather than repeating the trite platitudes of her rivals, the candidate offered a novel proposal to mitigate housing costs, and even her most captious critics admitted that the plan was ingenious.","at":"這位候選人沒有重複對手那些陳腐的老生常談，而是提出了一項減輕住房成本的新穎方案，就連最吹毛求疵的批評者都承認這項計畫十分巧妙。"},{"w":"archaic","p":"adj.","d":"Very old or old-fashioned; no longer in common use.","c":"古老的；過時的；古體的","s":"Students reading the King James Bible often stumble over its archaic vocabulary — words such as thee, thou, and wherefore, along with verb endings like -eth — which reflect English as it was spoken in the early seventeenth century rather than the language used today.","t":"閱讀《欽定版聖經》的學生常被其中古老的詞彙絆住——例如 thee、thou、wherefore 等字，以及 -eth 之類的動詞字尾——這些反映的是十七世紀初期所說的英語，而非今日使用的語言。","as":"Reformers castigated the state's archaic voting rules as iniquitous, arguing that the hidebound system allowed a small, complacent elite to retain power for generations while ordinary citizens grew increasingly indignant at being shut out.","at":"改革者嚴厲抨擊該州過時的投票規則極不公平，認為這套守舊的制度讓一小撮自滿的菁英得以世代掌權，而被排除在外的一般公民則越來越憤慨。"},{"w":"antiquated","p":"adj.","d":"Old-fashioned or outdated, no longer suitable.","c":"過時的；陳舊的；老式的","s":"Investigators concluded that the air-traffic control center's antiquated computer system, which still relied on floppy disks and software written in the 1980s, had contributed to the nationwide flight delays, and they urged Congress to fund a long-overdue modernization program.","t":"調查人員認定，這個航管中心老舊的電腦系統——仍仰賴磁碟片和1980年代編寫的軟體——是造成全國航班延誤的原因之一，並敦促國會撥款推動一項早該進行的現代化計畫。","as":"The school's antiquated curriculum, filled with mundane grammar drills and soporific lectures, left even the brightest students listless and disengaged, until a zealous new principal introduced project-based learning and invited local scientists into the classroom.","at":"這所學校陳舊的課程充斥著枯燥的文法練習和令人昏昏欲睡的講課，連最聰明的學生都無精打采、提不起興趣，直到一位熱忱的新校長引進專題式學習，並邀請當地科學家走進教室。"},{"w":"antediluvian","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely old or ridiculously old-fashioned.","c":"遠古的；極其古老的；老掉牙的","s":"The editorial mocked the club's antediluvian membership rules, which still barred women from the main dining room and required gentlemen to wear tailcoats on Sundays, as practices so ancient they seemed to predate not only the twentieth century but recorded history itself.","t":"這篇社論嘲諷該俱樂部那些老掉牙的會員規定——仍禁止女性進入主餐廳，並要求男士週日必須穿燕尾服——說這些做法古老得似乎不僅早於二十世紀，甚至早於有文字記載的歷史本身。","as":"The professor's antediluvian views on women in science struck many of his students as odious, and their vociferous protests outside the lecture hall eventually led the university's board to censure him publicly and suspend his teaching duties.","at":"這位教授對女性從事科學的老掉牙觀點，令許多學生覺得可憎，他們在演講廳外的激烈抗議最終促使大學董事會公開譴責他，並暫停他的授課職務。"},{"w":"antiquity","p":"n.","d":"The distant past, especially before the Middle Ages.","c":"古代；上古時期；古物","s":"The Antikythera mechanism, a bronze device recovered from a Greek shipwreck, has astonished scholars because it used interlocking gears to predict eclipses and planetary motions, proving that engineers in antiquity possessed a mechanical sophistication not seen again in Europe for over a thousand years.","t":"安提基特拉機械是從一艘希臘沉船中打撈出的青銅裝置，它令學者大感驚奇，因為它利用相互嚙合的齒輪預測日月食與行星運行，證明古代的工程師擁有歐洲此後一千多年都未再見過的精密機械技術。","as":"Since antiquity, philosophers from Confucius to Aristotle have extolled the virtue of moderation, warning that avarice and prodigal living are pernicious to both individuals and states, since unchecked desire erodes character and drains public treasuries.","at":"自古以來，從孔子到亞里斯多德的哲學家都頌揚節制的美德，並警告貪婪與揮霍的生活對個人和國家都有害，因為不受約束的慾望會腐蝕品格、耗盡國庫。"}]},{"unit":25,"theme":"Secret and Stealthy","themeZh":"隱密與偷偷摸摸","cards":[{"w":"inconspicuous","p":"adj.","d":"Not easily noticed; not attracting attention.","c":"不顯眼的；不引人注意的","s":"Many of the most dangerous invasive species arrive in a new ecosystem in inconspicuous ways — as tiny seeds lodged in the treads of hikers' boots or as larvae hidden in the ballast water of cargo ships — so that by the time biologists notice them, eradication is nearly impossible.","t":"許多最危險的外來入侵物種都是以不顯眼的方式進入新的生態系——例如卡在登山客鞋底紋路中的微小種子，或藏在貨輪壓艙水中的幼蟲——等到生物學家發現時，往往已幾乎不可能根除。","as":"Though inconspicuous in a crowd, the reticent archivist proved remarkably astute, and her quiet discovery of a forged deed exposed a devious land grab that a more ostentatious investigator, eager for headlines, had completely overlooked.","at":"這位沉默寡言的檔案管理員在人群中毫不起眼，卻展現出非凡的敏銳；她悄悄發現一份偽造的地契，揭穿了一樁狡詐的土地掠奪，而一位愛出風頭、急於搶占頭條的調查員卻完全忽略了這件事。"},{"w":"surreptitious","p":"adj.","d":"Done secretly because it would not be approved of.","c":"暗中的；鬼鬼祟祟的；偷偷的","s":"Historians discovered that the nineteenth-century botanist Robert Fortune made surreptitious journeys into China's tea-growing regions disguised as a Chinese merchant, secretly collecting seeds and plants that the British East India Company later used to break China's monopoly on tea production.","t":"歷史學家發現，十九世紀的植物學家羅伯特・福鈞曾喬裝成中國商人，暗中潛入中國的產茶區，偷偷採集種子與植株，英國東印度公司後來便利用這些植物打破了中國對茶葉生產的壟斷。","as":"The chess grandmaster was accused of surreptitious cheating after officials noticed a tiny device in his sleeve, and the scandal led organizers to censure him and impose a ban that the arrogant player denounced as malicious and unjust.","at":"這位西洋棋特級大師在官員發現他袖子裡藏有一個小裝置後，被指控暗中作弊；這樁醜聞導致主辦單位公開譴責他並對他施以禁賽，而這位傲慢的棋手則痛斥此舉是惡意且不公的。"},{"w":"unobtrusive","p":"adj.","d":"Not conspicuous or attracting attention; quietly modest.","c":"不張揚的；不顯眼的；不引人注目的","s":"The best documentary filmmakers strive to be unobtrusive, using small cameras, natural light, and minimal crews so that their subjects gradually forget they are being filmed and begin to behave as they would in private, revealing emotions they would otherwise conceal.","t":"最優秀的紀錄片導演都力求不引人注目，使用小型攝影機、自然光和精簡的團隊，讓拍攝對象逐漸忘記自己正在被拍攝，開始表現出私下的模樣，流露出他們原本會隱藏的情緒。","as":"The museum's renovation added unobtrusive lighting and quiet climate controls to the antiquated galleries, a subtle approach that won acclaim from critics who had feared an ostentatious redesign and who now extolled the architect's restraint.","at":"博物館的整修工程為老舊的展廳加裝了不顯眼的照明和安靜的空調系統，這種低調的做法贏得了評論家的好評；他們原本擔心會是一場炫耀浮誇的改造，如今則頌揚建築師的克制。"},{"w":"furtive","p":"adj.","d":"Attempting to avoid notice, typically out of guilt.","c":"偷偷摸摸的；鬼鬼祟祟的；心虛的","s":"Security analysts reviewing the footage noticed the suspect's furtive behavior long before the theft occurred: he repeatedly glanced toward the cameras, lingered near the emergency exit, and quickly turned his face away whenever a guard walked through the gallery.","t":"檢視監視畫面的保全分析人員早在竊案發生前，就注意到嫌犯鬼鬼祟祟的舉動：他一再瞄向攝影機，在緊急出口附近徘徊，而且每當警衛走過展廳時，便迅速把臉轉開。","as":"The defendant's furtive glances toward his lawyer did little to help his case; the prosecutor, pugnacious and incisive, seized on his evasive answers and wove them into a damning portrait of a devious man.","at":"被告頻頻偷瞄律師的心虛眼神，對他的案子毫無幫助；好鬥又犀利的檢察官緊抓住他閃爍其詞的回答，將之編織成一幅狡詐之人的致命畫像。"},{"w":"clandestine","p":"adj.","d":"Kept secret or done secretly, often illicitly.","c":"秘密的；暗中進行的；地下的","s":"During the Second World War, members of the French Resistance operated clandestine printing presses in cellars and barns, producing underground newspapers that countered Nazi propaganda, though anyone caught distributing them faced arrest, deportation, or even execution.","t":"第二次世界大戰期間，法國反抗軍成員在地窖和穀倉裡經營秘密印刷廠，印製反制納粹宣傳的地下報紙；然而任何人一旦被抓到散發這些報紙，就會面臨逮捕、驅逐出境，甚至處決。","as":"The investigative journalists uncovered a clandestine network of mercenary customs officials who had colluded with nefarious smugglers for years, and their exposé prompted lawmakers to censure the agency and demand sweeping reforms.","at":"調查記者們揭露了一個秘密網絡：一群唯利是圖的海關官員多年來與邪惡的走私集團勾結；他們的揭弊報導促使立法者譴責該機構，並要求進行全面改革。"},{"w":"covert","p":"adj.","d":"Not openly shown or acknowledged; secret.","c":"隱蔽的；秘密的；暗中的","s":"Declassified documents later revealed that the government had funded a covert program in the 1950s to influence foreign elections, secretly channeling money to friendly newspapers and political parties while publicly insisting that it respected the sovereignty of every nation.","t":"後來解密的文件揭露，政府在1950年代曾資助一項秘密計畫來影響外國選舉，暗中將資金輸送給友好的報社與政黨，同時卻公開堅稱自己尊重每個國家的主權。","as":"The covert surveillance program, once exposed, provoked vociferous outrage, and civil-liberties groups castigated officials whose devious justifications seemed to rest on little more than vague, ominous warnings about unnamed threats.","at":"這項秘密監控計畫一經曝光便引發強烈抗議，公民自由團體嚴厲抨擊官員，因為他們狡詐的辯解似乎只是建立在對不明威脅含糊又不祥的警告之上。"},{"w":"sly","p":"adj.","d":"Cunning and deceitful, or playfully mischievous.","c":"狡猾的；狡黠的；會心的","s":"In West African folklore, Anansi the spider is a sly trickster who outwits far stronger animals, such as the python and the leopard, through clever schemes and deceptive bargains, and his stories taught generations of listeners that intelligence can triumph over brute force.","t":"在西非民間傳說中，蜘蛛阿南西是一個狡猾的騙子，他用巧妙的計謀和騙人的交易智取比他強大得多的動物，例如巨蟒和豹；他的故事教導了一代又一代的聽眾：智慧能戰勝蠻力。","as":"The sly negotiator feigned an affable, almost obsequious manner, flattering his rivals with lavish compliments over dinner while quietly maneuvering to exploit their complacent assumption that the deal was already settled.","at":"這位狡猾的談判者假裝和藹可親、近乎諂媚，在晚宴上以大量的恭維話奉承對手，同時暗中設法利用他們自以為交易已成定局的自滿心態。"},{"w":"stealthy","p":"adj.","d":"Moving or acting quietly and carefully to avoid notice.","c":"偷偷摸摸的；悄悄的；隱密的","s":"Owls are among the most stealthy hunters in the animal kingdom, because the comb-like edges of their flight feathers break up turbulent air and muffle the sound of their wings, allowing them to swoop down on mice and voles without making any audible noise.","t":"貓頭鷹是動物界中最擅長悄然獵食的獵手之一，因為牠們飛羽邊緣的梳狀構造能打散亂流、消除翅膀拍動的聲音，讓牠們能在完全不發出可聞聲響的情況下俯衝捕捉老鼠和田鼠。","as":"The stealthy predator crept through the tall grass toward the gazelles, and its patience contrasted sharply with the raucous, impetuous young lions whose clamor alerted the entire herd and ruined the hunt.","at":"這隻悄無聲息的掠食者穿過高草叢，悄悄逼近瞪羚；牠的耐心與那些吵鬧、魯莽的年輕獅子形成強烈對比，後者的喧鬧聲驚動了整個羚群，壞了這場狩獵。"}]},{"unit":26,"theme":"Types of People","themeZh":"人物類型","cards":[{"w":"adversary","p":"n.","d":"An opponent or enemy in a contest or conflict.","c":"對手；敵手","s":"Although Douglas had been Lincoln's bitter adversary throughout the 1858 Senate campaign, trading accusations in seven heated debates across Illinois, he later stood beside the new president at his inauguration, holding Lincoln's hat as a public gesture of national unity.","t":"雖然道格拉斯在1858年參議員選戰中一直是林肯的激烈對手，兩人在伊利諾州各地的七場激辯中互相指控，但道格拉斯後來在這位新總統的就職典禮上站在他身旁，替林肯拿著帽子，以公開表示國家團結。","as":"Instead of trying to berate or intimidate his longtime adversary, the veteran negotiator adopted a cordial, conciliatory tone, a tactic that helped to mollify the opposing delegation and eventually produced an amicable settlement.","at":"這位資深談判代表沒有試圖斥責或恐嚇他的老對手，而是採取親切、和解的語氣；這個策略有助於安撫對方代表團，最終達成了友好的和解。"},{"w":"raconteur","p":"n.","d":"A person who tells anecdotes and stories with skill and wit.","c":"善於講故事的人；健談者","s":"Mark Twain was celebrated not only as a novelist but as a gifted raconteur whose lecture tours drew packed halls across America and Europe, where audiences laughed for hours at his meandering anecdotes, perfectly timed pauses, and deadpan delivery of absurd frontier tales.","t":"馬克·吐溫不僅以小說家聞名，也是一位才華洋溢、善於說故事的人；他的巡迴演講在美國和歐洲場場爆滿，觀眾聽著他曲折的軼事、拿捏精準的停頓，以及面無表情講述的荒誕邊疆故事，常常笑上好幾個小時。","as":"A born raconteur, the retired diplomat kept his convivial dinner guests enthralled with pithy anecdotes, though he was careful never to digress so far that his stories became verbose or lost their comic brevity.","at":"這位退休外交官天生善於說故事，以精闢的軼事讓歡樂的晚宴賓客聽得入迷；不過他總是小心不扯得太遠，以免故事變得冗長，失去簡潔帶來的喜感。"},{"w":"ascetic","p":"n.","d":"A person who practices severe self-denial, often for religious reasons.","c":"苦行者；禁慾者","s":"The early Christian ascetic Simeon Stylites reportedly spent thirty-seven years living atop a stone pillar in the Syrian desert, renouncing comfort, possessions, and most food in the belief that extreme physical deprivation would bring him closer to spiritual purity.","t":"早期基督教苦行者柱頂聖西門據說在敘利亞沙漠中的一根石柱頂上生活了三十七年，摒棄舒適、財物與大部分食物，相信極端的肉體匱乏能讓他更接近靈性上的純淨。","as":"Unlike the epicurean courtiers around him, the young prince Siddhartha left the palace to become an ascetic, adopting a diet so austere and abstemious that his followers feared he would grow fatally emaciated before attaining enlightenment.","at":"年輕的悉達多王子不同於身邊講究享樂的朝臣，離開王宮成為苦行者，飲食極其簡樸節制，以致追隨者擔心他在悟道之前就會瘦弱致死。"},{"w":"charlatan","p":"n.","d":"A person who falsely claims special knowledge or skill.","c":"江湖郎中；騙子","s":"In the nineteenth century, traveling salesmen peddled 'snake oil' tonics that supposedly cured everything from baldness to tuberculosis; when chemists finally analyzed one popular brand in 1917, they found mostly mineral oil and turpentine, exposing its seller as a charlatan who had profited from the desperation of the sick.","t":"十九世紀，巡迴推銷員兜售「蛇油」補藥，聲稱能治好從禿頭到肺結核的各種病症；1917年化學家終於分析了一個熱門品牌，發現其成分主要是礦物油和松節油，揭穿了其賣家是個利用病人絕望心理牟利的江湖騙子。","as":"The so-called psychic was eventually exposed as a charlatan whose cryptic predictions were nothing more than banal platitudes, delivered with a pretentious air to credulous clients who mistook his vague prattle for profound insight.","at":"這位所謂的靈媒最終被揭穿是個騙子，他那些隱晦的預言不過是陳腐的老生常談，以故作高深的姿態說給輕信的客戶聽，而他們卻把他含糊的胡扯誤認為深刻的洞見。"},{"w":"artisan","p":"n.","d":"A skilled worker who makes things by hand.","c":"工匠；手藝人","s":"In medieval Europe, each artisan belonged to a guild that regulated prices, protected trade secrets, and required apprentices to spend up to seven years learning to forge, weave, or carve by hand before they could submit a 'masterpiece' and open a workshop of their own.","t":"在中世紀歐洲，每位工匠都隸屬於一個行會；行會規範價格、保護行業機密，並要求學徒花上長達七年的時間學習以手工鍛造、編織或雕刻，之後才能提交一件「傑作」，開設自己的作坊。","as":"Though mass production has made many handicrafts obsolete, a meticulous artisan in Kyoto still spends weeks lacquering a single bowl, a scrupulous devotion to antiquated techniques that discerning collectors esteem far above any factory-made novelty.","at":"儘管大量生產已讓許多手工藝過時，京都一位一絲不苟的工匠仍會花上數週為單一個碗上漆；這種對古老技法的嚴謹投入，深受有眼光的收藏家推崇，遠勝任何工廠製造的新奇商品。"},{"w":"diva","p":"n.","d":"A celebrated female opera singer; a prima donna.","c":"歌劇女伶；首席女歌手","s":"Maria Callas, perhaps the most famous operatic diva of the twentieth century, transformed roles such as Norma and Tosca by combining a voice of extraordinary range with intense dramatic acting, and her reputation for temperamental outbursts only added to her legend among devoted opera fans.","t":"瑪麗亞·卡拉絲或許是二十世紀最著名的歌劇女伶，她將音域非凡的嗓音與強烈的戲劇表演結合，徹底改變了《諾瑪》與《托斯卡》等角色；而她喜怒無常、脾氣火爆的名聲，更讓她在忠實歌劇迷心中成為傳奇。","as":"Critics who had expected an ostentatious, haughty diva were surprised when the celebrated soprano proved affable and modest backstage, though onstage her mellifluous voice and ardent performance drew vociferous acclaim from the sold-out audience.","at":"評論家原本預期會見到一位愛炫耀、高傲的女伶，沒想到這位知名女高音在後台親切又謙虛；而在台上，她甜美圓潤的歌聲與熱情洋溢的演出，贏得滿場觀眾熱烈的喝采。"},{"w":"hedonist","p":"n.","d":"A person devoted to the pursuit of pleasure.","c":"享樂主義者","s":"The Roman emperor Elagabalus earned a reputation as a reckless hedonist, staging extravagant banquets where guests were showered with rose petals and served delicacies such as flamingo tongues, while he neglected the empire's finances in his relentless pursuit of sensual delight.","t":"羅馬皇帝埃拉伽巴路斯以肆無忌憚的享樂主義者著稱，他舉辦奢華的宴會，讓賓客沐浴在玫瑰花瓣雨中，並享用紅鶴舌等珍饈，同時在不斷追求感官享受的過程中忽略了帝國的財政。","as":"The prodigal heir, an unrepentant hedonist, continued to squander his vast inheritance on lavish parties and epicurean feasts in Monaco, ignoring the frugal advice of his parsimonious uncle until the family fortune had all but vanished.","at":"這位揮霍無度的繼承人是個毫無悔意的享樂主義者，不斷把龐大的遺產揮霍在摩納哥的奢華派對與美食盛宴上，對吝嗇叔叔的節儉忠告置若罔聞，直到家族財富幾乎消失殆盡。"},{"w":"pariah","p":"n.","d":"A person rejected and despised by society; an outcast.","c":"被排斥者；社會棄兒","s":"After Galileo published his defense of a sun-centered universe in 1632, the Inquisition placed him under house arrest, banned his book, and forbade him to publish any further works, so that one of Europe's most brilliant minds spent his final years as an intellectual pariah.","t":"伽利略於1632年發表為日心說辯護的著作後，宗教裁判所將他軟禁、查禁他的書，並禁止他再出版任何著作；於是，這位歐洲最傑出的頭腦之一，在遭學術界排斥的處境中度過了晚年。","as":"Once the scandal revealed his nefarious accounting schemes, the former tycoon quickly became a pariah; former allies began to censure him publicly, and even his most obsequious employees grew aloof and detached.","at":"醜聞揭露他卑劣的做帳手法後，這位前大亨很快淪為眾人唾棄的對象；昔日盟友開始公開譴責他，就連最阿諛奉承的員工也變得冷淡疏離。"},{"w":"skeptic","p":"n.","d":"A person who questions or doubts accepted beliefs.","c":"懷疑論者；持懷疑態度者","s":"When Alfred Wegener proposed in 1912 that the continents had once formed a single landmass, nearly every leading geologist was a skeptic, dismissing his theory because he could not explain what force might move such enormous masses of rock; only the discovery of seafloor spreading decades later vindicated him.","t":"1912年魏格納提出各大陸曾經是一整塊陸地時，幾乎每位頂尖地質學家都抱持懷疑態度，因為他無法解釋是什麼力量能移動如此龐大的岩塊而否定了他的理論；直到數十年後海底擴張被發現，他才得以平反。","as":"A seasoned skeptic, the science journalist was wary of the startup's grandiloquent claims and demanded rigorous data, refusing to be swayed by the founder's eloquence or the investors' fervent enthusiasm.","at":"這位科學記者是個老練的懷疑論者，對這家新創公司浮誇的說法保持戒心，要求提出嚴謹的數據，不為創辦人的雄辯或投資人狂熱的興奮所動搖。"},{"w":"virtuoso","p":"n.","d":"A person with outstanding technical skill, especially in music.","c":"演奏名家；大師","s":"Niccolò Paganini was such a dazzling virtuoso on the violin that rumors spread across nineteenth-century Europe claiming he had sold his soul to the devil, for audiences could not otherwise explain how one man could play such rapid, intricate passages with apparently effortless precision.","t":"帕格尼尼的小提琴技藝如此令人目眩，以致十九世紀的歐洲謠傳他把靈魂賣給了魔鬼，因為觀眾無法用其他理由解釋，一個人如何能以看似毫不費力的精準度，演奏出如此快速又繁複的樂段。","as":"The young piano virtuoso played with such exuberant brilliance that critics who usually disparage child prodigies were moved to extol her technique, and the audience's clamor for an encore echoed through a hall famous for its superb acoustics.","at":"這位年輕的鋼琴大師演奏得如此活力四射、才華洋溢，連平常愛貶低神童的評論家都忍不住讚揚她的技巧；觀眾要求安可的喧鬧聲，迴盪在這座以絕佳音響效果聞名的音樂廳中。"}]},{"unit":27,"theme":"Unimportant and Irrelevant","themeZh":"無關緊要與不相干","cards":[{"w":"inconsequential","p":"adj.","d":"Not important or significant; having no real effect.","c":"無關緊要的；微不足道的","s":"Early critics dismissed the Wright brothers' twelve-second flight at Kitty Hawk as an inconsequential stunt, a curiosity that covered barely 120 feet and seemed to have no practical value, yet within two decades powered aircraft were carrying mail across continents and reshaping modern warfare.","t":"早期的批評者把萊特兄弟在小鷹鎮那十二秒的飛行斥為無關緊要的特技表演，只是一個飛不到120英尺、看似毫無實用價值的新奇玩意兒；然而不到二十年，動力飛機就已跨越各大洲運送郵件，並重塑了現代戰爭。","as":"The senator tried to dismiss the leaked memo as inconsequential, but his verbose, evasive circumlocution only made reporters more wary, and soon even his complacent allies began to censure him for concealing it.","at":"這位參議員試圖把外洩的備忘錄說成無關緊要，但他冗長、閃爍其詞的拐彎抹角反而讓記者更加警惕；很快地，連他那些自滿的盟友也開始譴責他隱瞞此事。"},{"w":"extraneous","p":"adj.","d":"Not belonging to or directly related to the matter at hand.","c":"無關的；外來的","s":"To ensure that the experiment measured only the effect of the new fertilizer, the researchers controlled every extraneous variable, keeping light, temperature, soil composition, and watering schedules identical for all two hundred seedlings throughout the twelve-week trial.","t":"為了確保實驗只測量新肥料的效果，研究人員控制了所有無關的變因，在為期十二週的試驗中，讓全部兩百株幼苗的光照、溫度、土壤成分和澆水時間都保持一致。","as":"A good editor ruthlessly deletes extraneous material, trimming verbose passages and hackneyed phrases from a manuscript until the prose is concise and every remaining sentence carries the pithy force that discriminating readers expect.","at":"優秀的編輯會毫不留情地刪去稿件中多餘的內容，修剪冗長的段落和陳腐的詞句，直到文字簡潔有力，每個留下來的句子都具備挑剔的讀者所期待的精闢力量。"},{"w":"irrelevant","p":"adj.","d":"Not connected with or applicable to the subject.","c":"不相關的；不切題的","s":"The judge sustained the prosecutor's objection, ruling that the defendant's charitable donations, however generous, were irrelevant to the question before the jury, which concerned only whether he had knowingly falsified the company's financial statements in 2019.","t":"法官裁定檢察官的異議成立，認為被告的慈善捐款無論多麼慷慨，都與陪審團面前的問題無關，因為該問題只涉及他是否在2019年蓄意偽造公司的財務報表。","as":"During the televised debate, the candidate would digress into irrelevant anecdotes about his childhood whenever a question became contentious, a habit that his adversary mocked as rhetorical evasion rather than genuine eloquence.","at":"在電視辯論中，每當問題變得具爭議性，這位候選人就會岔開話題，講些與主題無關的童年軼事；他的對手譏諷這種習慣是修辭上的迴避，而非真正的口才。"},{"w":"incidental","p":"adj.","d":"Occurring as a minor accompaniment to something more important.","c":"附帶的；次要的","s":"The Rosetta Stone was carved to record a routine priestly decree honoring King Ptolemy V; its value as a key to Egyptian hieroglyphs was purely incidental, a by-product of the scribes' decision to repeat the same text in three different scripts.","t":"羅塞塔石碑原本是為了記錄一份向托勒密五世致敬的例行祭司詔令而刻製；它作為破解埃及象形文字之鑰的價值純屬附帶，是書吏決定用三種不同文字重複刻寫同一段內容所帶來的副產品。","as":"For the itinerant scholar, the comfort of hotels was incidental; she was a frugal traveler who tolerated sedentary days in archives only because they yielded the relics and records she coveted.","at":"對這位四處奔走的學者而言，旅館的舒適只是次要的；她是個節儉的旅人，之所以忍受在檔案館裡久坐不動的日子，只因那裡能找到她夢寐以求的文物與紀錄。"},{"w":"trivial","p":"adj.","d":"Of little value or importance.","c":"瑣碎的；微不足道的","s":"Engineers initially regarded the loss of a few foam fragments during shuttle launches as a trivial maintenance issue, but in 2003 a briefcase-sized piece struck Columbia's wing, breaching its heat shield and causing the orbiter to disintegrate during re-entry.","t":"工程師起初認為太空梭發射時掉落幾片泡沫碎片只是微不足道的維修問題，但在2003年，一塊公事包大小的碎片擊中哥倫比亞號的機翼，破壞了它的隔熱罩，導致太空梭在重返大氣層時解體。","as":"The cantankerous critic would berate young novelists over trivial errors of punctuation, yet his own weekly reviews were riddled with banal clichés and so verbose that many readers found them nearly soporific.","at":"這位脾氣暴躁的評論家會因為標點符號上的瑣碎錯誤而痛斥年輕小說家，然而他自己每週的書評卻充斥著平庸的陳腔濫調，而且冗長到許多讀者覺得幾乎催人入睡。"},{"w":"peripheral","p":"adj.","d":"Of minor importance; not central to the main issue.","c":"邊緣的；次要的","s":"In Tom Stoppard's play Rosencrantz and Guildenstern Are Dead, two peripheral characters from Hamlet, who appear in only a few scenes of Shakespeare's tragedy, become the protagonists, while the prince himself is pushed to the margins of the action.","t":"在湯姆·斯托帕德的劇作《君臣人子小命嗚呼》中，兩個在莎士比亞悲劇《哈姆雷特》裡只出現寥寥幾場戲的邊緣人物成了主角，而哈姆雷特王子本人反倒被推到劇情的邊緣。","as":"The committee chair, anxious to quell a contentious dispute over the budget, steered discussion away from peripheral issues and urged members to mediate their differences rather than rant about every disputatious detail.","at":"委員會主席急於平息一場關於預算、爭議激烈的爭端，將討論從次要議題上引開，並敦促委員們調解彼此的分歧，而不是針對每個有爭議的細節大聲咆哮。"},{"w":"negligible","p":"adj.","d":"So small or unimportant as to be not worth considering.","c":"可忽略的；微不足道的","s":"Because air resistance has a negligible effect on a dense steel ball dropped from a few meters, physics students can safely ignore it when calculating the ball's acceleration, though the same assumption would produce wildly inaccurate results for a falling feather.","t":"由於空氣阻力對從幾公尺高處落下的高密度鋼球影響小到可以忽略，物理系學生在計算鋼球加速度時可以放心不予考慮；然而同樣的假設若套用在落下的羽毛上，就會得出極不準確的結果。","as":"The parsimonious company claimed that the cost of replacing its antiquated equipment would be prohibitive, yet auditors found the expense negligible compared with the copious profits it had hoarded with such avarice.","at":"這家吝嗇的公司聲稱汰換老舊設備的成本高得令人卻步，但稽核人員發現，與它貪婪囤積的豐厚利潤相比，這筆支出微不足道。"},{"w":"frivolous","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking seriousness or purpose; silly and unimportant.","c":"輕浮的；無聊的","s":"To discourage frivolous lawsuits, several states allow judges to fine plaintiffs who file claims with no legal merit, such as suits filed solely to harass a business rival or to pressure a defendant into paying a quick settlement rather than facing costly litigation.","t":"為了遏止無聊的訴訟，有幾個州允許法官對提出毫無法律依據之訴訟的原告處以罰款；例如純粹為了騷擾商業對手而提起的訴訟，或是逼迫被告為了避免昂貴的官司而迅速付錢和解的訴訟。","as":"Critics deprecated the minister's frivolous remarks about the flood as callous and insolent, arguing that his jocular levity during the press briefing showed an indifferent attitude toward the thousands of families left homeless.","at":"批評者指責部長對水災所發表的輕率言論冷酷無禮，認為他在記者會上詼諧輕佻的態度，顯示出對數千個無家可歸家庭的漠不關心。"},{"w":"petty","p":"adj.","d":"Of small importance; also, small-minded or spiteful.","c":"瑣碎的；小心眼的","s":"Historians argue that the Renaissance city-states of Italy squandered their wealth and military strength on petty rivalries over border villages and trade privileges, leaving the peninsula divided and vulnerable when the far larger armies of France and Spain invaded in the 1490s.","t":"歷史學家認為，文藝復興時期的義大利城邦把財富與軍力浪費在為邊境村莊和貿易特權而起的瑣碎爭鬥上，導致半島四分五裂，在1490年代法國與西班牙更龐大的軍隊入侵時毫無抵抗之力。","as":"The petty quarrels among the history faculty, fueled by mutual animosity and rancorous gossip, finally escalated into an open feud so contentious that the dean had to intervene and mediate.","at":"歷史系教職員之間的瑣碎爭吵，在彼此的敵意與充滿怨恨的八卦推波助瀾下，最終升級為一場公開的激烈紛爭，使得院長不得不介入調解。"},{"w":"trifling","p":"adj.","d":"Trivial; of little value or importance.","c":"瑣碎的；微不足道的","s":"The Dutch reportedly acquired the island of Manhattan in 1626 for goods worth about sixty guilders, a trifling sum even then, though historians caution that the Lenape probably understood the exchange as a temporary sharing agreement rather than a permanent sale of land.","t":"據說荷蘭人在1626年以價值約六十荷蘭盾的貨物取得曼哈頓島，即使在當時也是微不足道的金額；不過歷史學家提醒，雷納佩人很可能把這場交易理解為暫時的共享協議，而非永久出售土地。","as":"The miserly landlord would berate tenants over trifling damages such as a scuffed doorframe, yet he remained apathetic and indifferent when they reported the deleterious mold spreading through the building.","at":"這位吝嗇的房東會因為門框刮痕這類微不足道的損壞而痛斥房客，但當房客回報大樓裡蔓延的有害黴菌時，他卻始終冷漠、漠不關心。"}]},{"unit":28,"theme":"Wise and Perceptive","themeZh":"睿智與敏銳","cards":[{"w":"discerning","p":"adj.","d":"Showing good judgment and the ability to perceive fine distinctions.","c":"有識別力的；有眼光的","s":"Although Han van Meegeren's fake Vermeer, Supper at Emmaus, fooled leading Dutch experts in 1937, more discerning modern viewers quickly spot what those scholars missed: its heavy-lidded faces resemble 1930s film stars far more than the people Vermeer painted in seventeenth-century Delft.","t":"雖然范·米格倫偽造的維梅爾畫作《以馬忤斯的晚餐》在1937年騙過了荷蘭頂尖的專家，但更有眼光的現代觀者很快就能看出那些學者所忽略的破綻：畫中眼皮厚重的臉孔，比起維梅爾在十七世紀台夫特所畫的人物，更像1930年代的電影明星。","as":"A discerning reader quickly sees past the pretentious, grandiloquent prose of the celebrity memoir and recognizes that beneath its ostentatious vocabulary lie only trite observations, hackneyed sentiments, and a remarkably shallow understanding of history.","at":"有眼光的讀者很快就能看穿這本名人回憶錄矯揉造作、浮誇的文字，發現在那些炫耀的辭藻底下，只有陳腐的觀察、老套的情感，以及對歷史極為膚淺的理解。"},{"w":"erudite","p":"adj.","d":"Having or showing great knowledge gained from study.","c":"博學的；學識淵博的","s":"Jorge Luis Borges filled his short stories with references to medieval theology, Arabic philosophy, and obscure encyclopedias, an erudite style that delighted scholars but sometimes left general readers wondering which of his learned citations were real and which he had invented.","t":"波赫士在短篇小說中充滿了對中世紀神學、阿拉伯哲學和冷僻百科全書的引用；這種博學的風格令學者著迷，卻有時讓一般讀者納悶，他那些學術性引文哪些是真的、哪些是他虛構的。","as":"The erudite historian was neither haughty nor supercilious; her lectures, delivered with affable levity and vivid examples, made even the most labyrinthine debates of antiquity accessible to curious undergraduates with no background in classics.","at":"這位博學的歷史學家既不傲慢也不目中無人；她以親切幽默的方式並搭配生動的例子授課，即使是古代最錯綜複雜的爭論，沒有古典學背景的好奇大學生也能理解。"},{"w":"incisive","p":"adj.","d":"Intelligently analytical, clear, and direct.","c":"一針見血的；犀利的","s":"Rachel Carson's 1962 book Silent Spring offered an incisive critique of pesticide use, cutting through industry claims with precise scientific evidence and clear prose that showed exactly how DDT accumulated in food chains and thinned the eggshells of predatory birds.","t":"瑞秋·卡森1962年的著作《寂靜的春天》對農藥使用提出了一針見血的批判，以精確的科學證據和清晰的文字戳破業界的說法，具體說明了DDT如何在食物鏈中累積，並使猛禽的蛋殼變薄。","as":"Unlike the verbose, diffuse reports submitted by her colleagues, the analyst's incisive memo was succinct and direct, exposing the pernicious flaws in the proposed merger plan in fewer than two pages.","at":"不同於同事們提交的冗長而鬆散的報告，這位分析師一針見血的備忘錄簡明扼要，用不到兩頁的篇幅就揭露了擬議合併計畫中的致命缺陷。"},{"w":"ingenious","p":"adj.","d":"Clever, original, and inventive.","c":"巧妙的；有創意的","s":"To cool their homes without electricity, ancient Persian builders developed an ingenious system of wind-catching towers that funneled breezes over underground water channels, lowering indoor temperatures by as much as fifteen degrees even in the scorching summers of the desert.","t":"為了在沒有電的情況下讓房屋降溫，古代波斯建築工匠發展出一套巧妙的捕風塔系統，將微風引導經過地下水道，即使在沙漠炙熱的夏季，也能使室內溫度降低多達十五度。","as":"Faced with a precarious water supply, the frugal engineers devised an ingenious method of recycling water aboard the station, an innovation that was soon acclaimed as unprecedented by the space agency.","at":"面對不穩定的供水，這些節儉的工程師設計出一套在太空站上回收水的巧妙方法，這項創新很快就被太空總署讚譽為前所未有的成就。"},{"w":"perspicacious","p":"adj.","d":"Having a keen understanding and insight; mentally sharp.","c":"有洞察力的；敏銳的","s":"Alexis de Tocqueville, a perspicacious observer who toured the United States in 1831, predicted with startling accuracy that tensions over slavery would threaten the union and that America and Russia would one day each hold sway over half the world.","t":"托克維爾是一位深具洞察力的觀察家，他於1831年遊歷美國，以驚人的準確度預言奴隸制度的緊張關係將威脅聯邦，而美國與俄國終有一天會各自主宰半個世界。","as":"A perspicacious diplomat, she recognized early on that the rival delegation's cordial manner masked deep animosity toward her country, and she therefore remained vigilant and circumspect throughout the protracted and often tense negotiations.","at":"她是一位洞察力敏銳的外交官，很早就看出對手代表團親切的態度掩飾著對她國家的深刻敵意，因此在冗長且經常緊張的談判過程中始終保持警覺與謹慎。"},{"w":"astute","p":"adj.","d":"Quick to understand situations and turn them to advantage.","c":"機敏的；精明的","s":"Recognizing that the gold rush would enrich suppliers more reliably than miners, the astute merchant Levi Strauss opened a dry-goods business in San Francisco that supplied miners with clothing, fabric, and tools, building a fortune while most of his customers left California with empty pockets.","t":"精明的商人李維·史特勞斯看出淘金熱帶給供應商的財富比給礦工的更可靠，於是在舊金山開設乾貨批發生意，供應礦工衣物、布料與工具；當大多數顧客兩手空空離開加州時，他卻累積了一大筆財富。","as":"An astute investor, she avoided the volatile market's transient fads and refused to squander capital on novel schemes, preferring a prudent strategy that her more impetuous partners derided as overly wary.","at":"她是一位精明的投資人，避開了動盪市場中曇花一現的風潮，拒絕把資金浪費在新奇的計畫上，寧可採取審慎的策略，雖然她那些較衝動的合夥人嘲笑這種做法過於謹慎。"},{"w":"acute","p":"adj.","d":"Sharp and perceptive; keenly sensitive.","c":"敏銳的；靈敏的","s":"Bats compensate for their poor eyesight with remarkably acute hearing; by emitting high-frequency calls and analyzing the returning echoes, they can detect an insect as thin as a human hair and judge its distance and direction in complete darkness.","t":"蝙蝠以極為靈敏的聽覺彌補視力的不足；牠們發出高頻叫聲並分析返回的回聲，能在一片漆黑中偵測到像人類頭髮一樣細的昆蟲，並判斷其距離與方向。","as":"The critic's acute ear could detect the slightest discordant note in a performance, so her rare praise for the young cellist's mellifluous phrasing was esteemed far above the effusive acclaim of less exacting reviewers.","at":"這位評論家敏銳的耳朵能察覺演出中最細微的不和諧音，因此她對這位年輕大提琴家甜美流暢的樂句罕見的讚美，遠比其他標準較寬鬆的評論者熱情洋溢的讚譽更受重視。"},{"w":"prudent","p":"adj.","d":"Acting with care and thought for the future.","c":"謹慎的；審慎的","s":"After the devastating 1755 earthquake destroyed much of Lisbon, the Marquis of Pombal made the prudentedecision to rebuild with flexible wooden frames inside masonry walls, one of the earliest examples of earthquake-resistant construction in European history.","t":"1755年的毀滅性大地震摧毀里斯本大半之後，龐巴爾侯爵作出了審慎的決定，在磚石牆內加入有彈性的木構架來重建城市，這是歐洲史上最早的抗震建築範例之一。","as":"A prudent government stockpiles grain during years of ample harvests, a thrifty policy that can alleviate famine and mitigate the social turmoil that inevitably follows a catastrophic drought or a sudden collapse in food imports.","at":"審慎的政府會在豐收的年份儲備糧食，這種節約的政策能緩解饑荒，並減輕嚴重乾旱或糧食進口驟減後必然隨之而來的社會動盪。"},{"w":"judicious","p":"adj.","d":"Having or showing sound judgment; wise and sensible.","c":"明智的；審慎的","s":"Rather than rewriting the damaged fresco entirely, the conservators made judicious use of reversible pigments, filling only the cracks and missing fragments so that future restorers could distinguish clearly between Giotto's original brushwork and modern repairs.","t":"修復師沒有全面重繪受損的濕壁畫，而是明智地使用可逆的顏料，只填補裂痕和缺失的碎片，好讓日後的修復者能清楚區分喬托的原始筆觸與現代的修補。","as":"The judicious mediator listened impassively to both factions for hours, refused to castigate either side, and finally offered a compromise that managed to placate even the most recalcitrant and obstinate delegates.","at":"這位明智的調解人面無表情地聆聽雙方陣營長達數小時，拒絕嚴厲斥責任何一方，最後提出一個折衷方案，甚至安撫了最頑固、最執拗的代表。"},{"w":"sagacious","p":"adj.","d":"Having deep wisdom and sound judgment.","c":"睿智的；有遠見的","s":"Benjamin Franklin, then over eighty and the oldest delegate, offered the Constitutional Convention a sagacious warning in 1787: no assembly of fallible men could produce a perfect document, so delegates should accept the compromise rather than let their pride destroy the union.","t":"1787年，年過八十、身為最年長代表的班傑明·富蘭克林向制憲會議提出睿智的忠告：任何由會犯錯的凡人組成的會議，都不可能產生完美的文件，因此代表們應該接受這項妥協，而不是讓自尊毀了聯邦。","as":"The sagacious elder was revered by the nomadic tribe, for she could foresee ominous changes in the weather long before others noticed them and offer counsel that helped her people endure adversity without despair.","at":"這位睿智的長者深受這個遊牧部落的敬重，因為她能比別人早得多預見天氣中不祥的變化，並提出建言，幫助族人度過逆境而不陷入絕望。"},{"w":"savvy","p":"adj.","d":"Shrewd and knowledgeable, especially in practical matters.","c":"精明的；懂行的","s":"Long before social media existed, the circus promoter P. T. Barnum proved himself remarkably savvy about publicity, planting anonymous letters in newspapers that questioned his own exhibits so that the resulting controversy would draw even larger crowds to his museum.","t":"早在社群媒體出現之前，馬戲團經紀人巴納姆就展現出他對宣傳極為精明的手腕：他在報紙上匿名投書，質疑自己的展品，讓隨之而來的爭議吸引更多人潮湧入他的博物館。","as":"The savvy campaign manager knew that a candidate's vapid platitudes would not appease skeptical voters, so she urged him to abandon his banal slogans and speak candidly about the debacle.","at":"這位精明的競選經理知道，候選人空洞的陳腔濫調無法平息心存懷疑的選民，於是敦促他拋棄平庸的口號，坦率地談論那場慘敗。"},{"w":"shrewd","p":"adj.","d":"Having sharp practical judgment; clever in a practical way.","c":"精明的；機靈的","s":"In 1803 the United States made a shrewd bargain when it paid France about fifteen million dollars for the Louisiana Territory, doubling the nation's size for roughly three cents an acre at a moment when Napoleon urgently needed money for his wars in Europe.","t":"1803年，美國以約一千五百萬美元向法國購得路易斯安那領地，做了一筆精明的交易：在拿破崙急需資金應付歐洲戰事之際，以每英畝約三美分的代價讓國土面積加倍。","as":"The shrewd negotiator recognized that the mercenary contractors were motivated by avarice alone, so he offered a modest bonus that proved enough to mollify them and avert a costly debacle.","at":"這位精明的談判者看出那些唯利是圖的承包商只受貪婪驅使，於是提供了一筆不多的獎金，結果足以安撫他們，避免了一場代價高昂的慘敗。"}]},{"unit":29,"theme":"Confusable Words I","themeZh":"易混淆字詞（一）","cards":[{"w":"allusion","p":"n.","d":"An indirect or passing reference, often to literature or history.","c":"暗指；典故","s":"The title of Aldous Huxley's novel Brave New World is an ironic allusion to Shakespeare's The Tempest, in which the sheltered Miranda exclaims at the sight of strangers, so readers who recognize the source understand from the first page that the 'new world' will prove far from admirable.","t":"赫胥黎小說《美麗新世界》的書名，諷刺地暗指莎士比亞的《暴風雨》——劇中涉世未深的米蘭達一見到陌生人便驚嘆不已；因此認出出處的讀者從第一頁就明白，這個「新世界」絕非令人嚮往。","as":"The poet's erudite allusion to Homer was lost on most of the audience, yet the discerning critics in attendance were quick to laud its subtlety and to extol the pithy elegance of the closing stanza.","at":"詩人對荷馬的博學引典，大多數聽眾都沒聽出來，但在場有眼光的評論家很快就稱讚其精妙，並讚揚最後一節精煉優雅。"},{"w":"coalesce","p":"v.","d":"To come together to form one mass or whole.","c":"結合；融合","s":"Astronomers believe that about 4.6 billion years ago, countless grains of dust and ice orbiting the young sun gradually coalesced into small rocky bodies called planetesimals, which collided and merged over millions of years to form the planets we observe today.","t":"天文學家認為，大約46億年前，環繞年輕太陽運行的無數塵埃與冰粒逐漸結合成稱為微行星的小型岩質天體，這些天體在數百萬年間不斷碰撞、合併，形成了我們今天所觀察到的行星。","as":"In the turbulence of 1848, contentious factions that had long nursed mutual animosity began to coalesce into a single movement, united by their indignant opposition to the monarchy's harsh taxes.","at":"在1848年的動盪中，長久以來彼此敵視、爭執不休的派系開始結合成單一運動，因共同憤慨地反對君主政體嚴苛的稅收而團結起來。"},{"w":"convalesce","p":"v.","d":"To recover health and strength gradually after illness.","c":"康復；療養","s":"After contracting tuberculosis in 1899, the young physician was sent to a sanatorium in the Swiss Alps to convalesce, where doctors prescribed months of bed rest, mountain air, and nourishing meals, the standard treatment for the disease before the discovery of antibiotics.","t":"這位年輕醫師在1899年感染肺結核後，被送往瑞士阿爾卑斯山的一間療養院休養康復；在那裡，醫生開立了數月的臥床休息、山間空氣和營養餐點，這是抗生素問世前治療此病的標準療法。","as":"While she was convalescing after surgery, the listless patient grew sluggish and lethargic, and her doctors warned that too many weeks of sedentary rest in bed could actually weaken her muscles and slow her recovery.","at":"她在手術後休養康復期間變得無精打采、行動遲緩又昏昏欲睡，醫生警告她，連續數週久坐久臥不動的休息，其實會削弱肌肉，拖慢復原的速度。"},{"w":"delusion","p":"n.","d":"A firmly held false belief despite clear evidence otherwise.","c":"妄想；錯覺","s":"Cervantes's Don Quixote reads so many chivalric romances that he falls under the delusion that he is a knight errant; convinced that ordinary windmills are menacing giants, he charges them with his lance, and the novel uses his madness to satirize the literature that inspired it.","t":"塞萬提斯筆下的唐吉訶德讀了太多騎士傳奇，以致陷入自己是遊俠騎士的妄想；他深信平凡的風車是兇惡的巨人，便持矛衝向它們，而這部小說正是藉他的瘋狂來諷刺啟發他的那類文學。","as":"The arrogant emperor lived under the delusion that his subjects adored him, for his obsequious courtiers were too servile to tell him that his lavish spending had provoked widespread turmoil.","at":"這位傲慢的皇帝活在臣民愛戴他的妄想中，因為他那些阿諛奉承的朝臣太過卑躬屈膝，不敢告訴他，他的奢侈揮霍已引發廣泛的動盪。"},{"w":"illusion","p":"n.","d":"Something that deceives the senses by appearing real.","c":"幻覺；錯覺","s":"In the famous Müller-Lyer figure, two lines of exactly equal length appear dramatically different because of the arrowheads at their ends, an optical illusion that persists even after viewers have measured the lines and know perfectly well that they are identical.","t":"在著名的繆勒-萊爾圖形中，兩條長度完全相同的線段因兩端箭頭的方向不同而看起來差異懸殊；這種視錯覺即使在觀者測量過線段、清楚知道兩者等長之後，依然存在。","as":"The ostentatious marble lobby and lavish quarterly parties created an illusion of prosperity, but auditors soon discovered that the firm's precarious finances were a looming debacle concealed by years of devious accounting.","at":"那座炫耀的大理石大廳和奢華的季度派對營造出繁榮的假象，但稽核人員很快發現，這家公司岌岌可危的財務狀況是一場被多年狡詐會計手法掩蓋、迫在眉睫的災難。"},{"w":"ambiguous","p":"adj.","d":"Open to more than one interpretation; unclear in meaning.","c":"模稜兩可的；含糊的","s":"Because the Second Amendment's opening clause about a 'well regulated Militia' is grammatically ambiguous, legal scholars have argued for more than two centuries over whether it limits the right to bear arms or merely explains one reason for protecting it.","t":"由於美國憲法第二修正案開頭關於「管理良好的民兵」的子句在文法上模稜兩可，兩個多世紀以來，法學學者一直爭論它究竟是限制了持有武器的權利，還是僅說明保障此權利的理由之一。","as":"The diplomat's cryptic, ambiguous reply to the ultimatum only deepened the quandary, and the reticent foreign minister refused to clarify it, leaving reporters and rival governments alike to speculate about what the enigma might mean.","at":"這位外交官對最後通牒隱晦、模稜兩可的回覆只讓困境更加棘手，而沉默寡言的外交部長又拒絕澄清，讓記者和敵對國政府都只能揣測這個謎團究竟代表什麼意思。"},{"w":"acrid","p":"adj.","d":"Unpleasantly sharp or bitter to the smell or taste.","c":"刺鼻的；辛辣的","s":"During the Great Smog of 1952, a thick layer of coal smoke settled over London for five days, filling the streets with an acrid yellow haze that stung residents' eyes and throats and was later linked to at least four thousand deaths.","t":"1952年倫敦大霧霾期間，一層厚厚的煤煙籠罩倫敦長達五天，街道上瀰漫著刺鼻的黃色煙霧，刺痛居民的眼睛和喉嚨，事後被認為與至少四千人的死亡有關。","as":"Long after the conflagration was extinguished, the acrid smoke lingered over the rubble, and residents were indignant that officials had dismissed warnings about the volatile chemicals stored in the warehouse.","at":"大火撲滅許久之後，刺鼻的濃煙仍在瓦礫上方久久不散；居民十分憤慨，因為官員先前對倉庫中存放易揮發化學物質的警告置之不理。"},{"w":"aesthetic","p":"adj.","d":"Concerned with beauty or the appreciation of beauty.","c":"美學的；審美的","s":"When the Eiffel Tower was proposed for the 1889 World's Fair, many prominent Parisian artists objected on aesthetic grounds, condemning the iron lattice as a monstrous eyesore, although the structure has since become one of the most admired works of architecture in the world.","t":"艾菲爾鐵塔被提議作為1889年世界博覽會的建築時，許多巴黎知名藝術家基於美學理由加以反對，斥責這座鐵格結構是醜陋的礙眼之物；然而此後它已成為全世界最受讚賞的建築作品之一。","as":"Critics who had dismissed the architect's aesthetic vision as derivative and banal were forced to revise their opinion when the museum's innovative design, with its curving glass galleries, drew acclaim from visitors around the world.","at":"那些曾把這位建築師的美學理念斥為缺乏原創、平淡無奇的評論家，在博物館擁有弧形玻璃展廳的創新設計贏得全球參觀者讚譽之後，不得不修正自己的看法。"},{"w":"ambivalent","p":"adj.","d":"Having mixed or conflicting feelings about something.","c":"矛盾的；猶豫不決的","s":"Although Thomas Jefferson called slavery a 'moral depravity' and drafted language condemning the slave trade, he remained deeply ambivalent about emancipation, enslaving more than six hundred people over his lifetime and freeing only a handful of them.","t":"雖然湯瑪斯·傑佛遜稱奴隸制度為「道德敗壞」，並起草了譴責奴隸貿易的文字，但他對解放奴隸始終深感矛盾，一生奴役了六百多人，卻只釋放了其中寥寥數人。","as":"The novelist was ambivalent about her sudden fame; she enjoyed the critical acclaim, but she found the effusive praise of sycophants vapid and the endless obligatory interviews both banal and exhausting.","at":"這位小說家對自己突如其來的名氣感到矛盾：她享受評論界的讚譽，卻覺得馬屁精的熱情吹捧空洞無味，而那些沒完沒了、不得不接受的訪談則既平淡又令人疲憊。"},{"w":"arid","p":"adj.","d":"Having little or no rain; too dry to support vegetation.","c":"乾旱的；乾燥的","s":"Chile's Atacama Desert is so arid that some weather stations there have never recorded measurable rainfall, and NASA scientists test Mars rovers in its barren soil because the conditions resemble those on the red planet more closely than any other place on Earth.","t":"智利的阿塔卡馬沙漠乾旱至極，當地有些氣象站從未記錄到可測量的降雨；美國太空總署的科學家在其貧瘠的土壤上測試火星探測車，因為那裡的環境比地球上任何其他地方都更接近火星。","as":"Nomadic herders have endured the adversity of the arid Mongolian steppe for centuries, relying on frugal habits, sturdy horses, and a meticulous knowledge of hidden wells to survive its harsh and precarious seasons.","at":"數百年來，遊牧民族在乾旱的蒙古大草原上忍受艱困，依靠節儉的生活習慣、強健的馬匹，以及對隱密水井一絲不苟的了解，熬過那裡嚴酷又變幻莫測的季節。"},{"w":"atheistic","p":"adj.","d":"Denying or lacking belief in the existence of God.","c":"無神論的","s":"Because Soviet ideology was officially atheistic, the government closed thousands of churches, mosques, and synagogues in the 1920s and 1930s, converting some into museums of scientific materialism and replacing religious holidays with state celebrations of labor and revolution.","t":"由於蘇聯的意識形態官方立場是無神論的，政府在1920至1930年代關閉了數以千計的教堂、清真寺和猶太會堂，將其中一些改建為科學唯物主義博物館，並以國家慶祝勞動與革命的節日取代宗教節日。","as":"The philosopher's atheistic essays provoked a vociferous outcry among the clergy, who sought to censure and castigate him from their pulpits, yet he remained stoical, calmly rebutting each polemical attack in print.","at":"這位哲學家的無神論文章在神職人員之間引發強烈的抗議聲浪，他們試圖在講壇上譴責並嚴厲斥責他，但他始終堅忍沉著，冷靜地以文字反駁每一篇論戰式的攻擊。"}]},{"unit":30,"theme":"Confusable Words II","themeZh":"易混淆字詞（二）","cards":[{"w":"impudent","p":"adj.","d":"Shamelessly rude and disrespectful.","c":"無禮的；厚顏無恥的","s":"When the young journalist interrupted the prime minister's press conference to ask whether he had ever read the bill he was promoting, aides dismissed the question as impudent, though many viewers privately admired her refusal to show the deference that officials usually expected.","t":"這位年輕記者在總理的記者會上插話，質問他是否讀過自己正在推動的法案；幕僚們斥這個問題為無禮，但許多觀眾私下欣賞她拒絕表現出官員通常期待的那種恭敬。","as":"The impudent apprentice was insolent and presumptuous toward the master craftsman who had trained him, and his contemptuous remarks in front of customers soon led the guild to rebuke him and threaten to expel him.","at":"這個無禮的學徒對一手栽培他的師傅傲慢放肆、自以為是，他在顧客面前發表的輕蔑言論，很快就讓行會對他加以斥責，並威脅要將他除名。"},{"w":"intimidate","p":"v.","d":"To frighten or threaten someone into doing what one wants.","c":"恐嚇；威嚇","s":"During the Reconstruction era, armed groups such as the Ku Klux Klan used night raids, arson, and public violence to intimidate newly enfranchised Black citizens, hoping to keep them away from the polls and reverse the political gains guaranteed by the Fifteenth Amendment.","t":"在重建時期，三K黨等武裝團體以夜間突襲、縱火和公開暴力來恐嚇剛獲得投票權的黑人公民，企圖讓他們遠離投票所，並推翻第十五修正案所保障的政治成果。","as":"The belligerent landlord tried to intimidate the indigent tenants with threats of eviction, but their adamant refusal to leave and their vociferous protests eventually drew the attention of city officials.","at":"這位好鬥的房東企圖以驅逐威脅恐嚇貧困的房客，但他們堅決拒絕搬走，加上大聲疾呼的抗議，最終引起了市府官員的注意。"},{"w":"imprudent","p":"adj.","d":"Not showing care for the consequences of an action; rash.","c":"輕率的；不明智的","s":"Economists widely agree that it was imprudent for many banks in the early 2000s to issue mortgages to borrowers with no verified income, a reckless practice that inflated the housing bubble and contributed directly to the financial crisis of 2008.","t":"經濟學家普遍認為，2000年代初期許多銀行向收入未經查核的借款人發放房貸是不明智的；這種魯莽的做法使房市泡沫膨脹，並直接導致了2008年的金融危機。","as":"The prodigal heir's imprudent decision to squander his fortune on lavish yachts left him penurious within a decade, forcing him to rely on the largess of the very relatives he had once scorned.","at":"這位揮霍無度的繼承人輕率地把財富揮霍在豪華遊艇上，不到十年就窮困潦倒，被迫仰賴那些他曾經瞧不起的親戚慷慨接濟。"},{"w":"indignant","p":"adj.","d":"Angry because of something unjust or unfair.","c":"憤慨的；義憤填膺的","s":"Readers were indignant when Upton Sinclair's 1906 novel The Jungle revealed that Chicago meatpackers routinely ground diseased carcasses and even rats into sausage, and their outrage pressured Congress to pass the Pure Food and Drug Act within months.","t":"厄普頓·辛克萊1906年的小說《魔鬼的叢林》揭露芝加哥肉品加工廠經常把病死的屍體甚至老鼠絞碎做成香腸，讀者們義憤填膺，他們的憤怒迫使國會在數月內通過了《純淨食品與藥物法》。","as":"The indignant citizens staged a vociferous protest outside city hall, denouncing the council as callous and apathetic toward the plight of indigent families and demanding that it rebuke the developers who had evicted them.","at":"憤慨的市民在市政廳外發起大聲疾呼的抗議，譴責市議會對貧困家庭的困境冷酷又漠不關心，並要求議會斥責那些驅逐他們的開發商。"},{"w":"obscure","p":"adj.","d":"Not well known; also, unclear or hard to understand.","c":"默默無聞的；晦澀的","s":"Gregor Mendel, an obscure Augustinian friar working in a monastery garden in Brno, published his groundbreaking experiments on pea plants in 1866, but his findings were ignored for over thirty years until scientists rediscovered them and recognized him as the founder of genetics.","t":"孟德爾是一位默默無聞的奧斯定會修士，在布爾諾一座修道院的花園裡工作；他在1866年發表了具開創性的豌豆實驗，但其研究成果被忽視了三十多年，直到科學家重新發現，才尊他為遺傳學之父。","as":"Though the poet died obscure and penurious in a rented room, later critics came to revere her work, and today scholars extol the cryptic, laconic verses that her contemporaries had dismissed as trivial.","at":"雖然這位詩人在租來的房間裡默默無聞、窮困潦倒地離世，後來的評論家卻開始崇敬她的作品；如今學者們讚揚那些曾被同時代人斥為瑣碎的隱晦、簡練詩句。"},{"w":"obtuse","p":"adj.","d":"Slow to understand or perceive; insensitive.","c":"遲鈍的；愚鈍的","s":"In Jane Austen's Pride and Prejudice, Mr. Collins is so obtuse that he fails to notice Elizabeth's obvious distaste for him, interpreting each of her firm refusals of his marriage proposal as the modest hesitation that he believes all elegant young ladies are expected to display.","t":"在珍·奧斯汀的《傲慢與偏見》中，柯林斯先生遲鈍到察覺不出伊莉莎白對他明顯的厭惡，把她每一次堅決拒絕他求婚的回答，都解讀為他認為所有優雅年輕女士都應表現出的矜持猶豫。","as":"The obtuse manager remained oblivious to the animosity growing among his staff for months, and his complacent, nonchalant attitude toward their complaints allowed petty quarrels to escalate into open antagonism that eventually split the department.","at":"這位遲鈍的經理數月來始終沒有察覺員工之間日益滋長的敵意，他對員工抱怨自滿又漫不經心的態度，讓瑣碎的爭吵升級為公開的對立，最終使整個部門分裂。"},{"w":"indigenous","p":"adj.","d":"Originating or occurring naturally in a particular place; native.","c":"本土的；原住民的","s":"Long before European ships arrived, the indigenous peoples of Taiwan, including the Amis, Atayal, and Paiwan, had developed distinct languages belonging to the Austronesian family, and linguists now believe the island may have been the original homeland of that vast language group.","t":"早在歐洲船隻抵達之前，臺灣的原住民族，包括阿美族、泰雅族和排灣族，就已發展出屬於南島語系的各種獨特語言；語言學家如今認為，臺灣可能就是這個龐大語系的發源地。","as":"Conservationists warn that invasive rats and cats pose a pernicious threat to the indigenous birds of New Zealand, whose populations have already been devastated by deleterious pesticides and increasingly precarious habitats.","at":"保育人士警告，外來的老鼠和貓對紐西蘭的本土鳥類構成嚴重的威脅，而這些鳥類的族群數量早已因有害的農藥和日益岌岌可危的棲地而遭受重創。"},{"w":"indigent","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely poor; lacking the basic necessities of life.","c":"貧困的；窮苦的","s":"In the landmark 1963 case Gideon v. Wainwright, the Supreme Court ruled that states must provide free legal counsel to indigentedefendants accused of serious crimes, recognizing that a fair trial is impossible when a person cannot afford a lawyer.","t":"在1963年具里程碑意義的「吉迪恩訴溫賴特案」中，最高法院裁定各州必須為被控重罪的貧困被告提供免費律師，承認一個人若請不起律師，就不可能得到公平的審判。","as":"The philanthropic foundation, known for its munificent grants, funded a clinic for indigent patients, an altruistic gesture that stood in stark contrast to the avarice of the city's miserly landlords.","at":"這個以慷慨捐助聞名的慈善基金會資助了一間為貧困病患服務的診所；這種利他的義舉，與市內吝嗇房東的貪婪形成鮮明對比。"},{"w":"intimate","p":"v.","d":"To suggest or hint at something indirectly.","c":"暗示；透露","s":"In his final letters from the Arctic, the explorer did not openly admit that the expedition was failing, but he intimated as much by describing dwindling food supplies, frostbitten crew members, and his growing hope that a rescue ship might reach them before winter.","t":"這位探險家在北極寫下的最後幾封信中，並未公開承認探險隊正陷入失敗，但他描述日漸減少的糧食、凍傷的隊員，以及他越來越盼望救援船能在冬天之前抵達，已暗示了這一點。","as":"The reticent minister would only intimate his disapproval of the treaty through cryptic, laconic remarks at press conferences, leaving journalists to puzzle for weeks over the enigma of his ambiguous silence.","at":"這位沉默寡言的部長只在記者會上透過隱晦、簡短的評論暗示他對條約的不滿，讓記者們連續數週對他那模稜兩可的沉默之謎百思不解。"},{"w":"ponderable","p":"adj.","d":"Worthy of careful thought; capable of being weighed or assessed.","c":"值得考慮的；可衡量的","s":"Before approving the dam, the commission listed every ponderable consequence it could identify, from the number of villages that would be flooded to the expected gain in electricity, while acknowledging that some cultural losses could never be measured at all.","t":"在核准興建水壩之前，委員會列出了它所能辨識的每一項值得衡量的後果，從將被淹沒的村莊數量到預期增加的發電量，同時也承認有些文化上的損失根本無從衡量。","as":"The review panel dismissed the critic's contentious objections as trivial, yet several scrupulous scientists insisted that the ponderable risks of the mining project were anything but negligible and deserved meticulous study.","at":"審查小組把這位批評者具爭議性的反對意見斥為瑣碎，但幾位嚴謹的科學家堅持，這項採礦計畫中值得考量的風險絕非微不足道，應該加以縝密研究。"},{"w":"ponderous","p":"adj.","d":"Slow and clumsy because of great weight; dull and laborious.","c":"笨重的；沉悶冗長的","s":"The earliest computers, such as the 1945 ENIAC, were ponderous machines that weighed nearly thirty tons, filled an entire room with thousands of vacuum tubes, and required teams of technicians to rewire them by hand whenever a new calculation was needed.","t":"最早期的電腦，例如1945年的ENIAC，是重達近三十噸的笨重機器，數千根真空管塞滿了整個房間，每當需要進行新的計算時，就得由技術人員團隊以手工重新接線。","as":"The professor's ponderous lectures on medieval tax law, filled with verbose digressions and banal platitudes, proved so soporific that even the most avid students grew listless before the hour ended.","at":"這位教授講授中世紀稅法的課程沉悶冗長，充斥著冗長的離題和平庸的陳腔濫調，令人昏昏欲睡，連最熱衷的學生也在下課前變得無精打采。"}]},{"unit":31,"theme":"Aspiration and Outlook","themeZh":"抱負與心態","cards":[{"w":"aspire","p":"v.","d":"To direct one's hopes and efforts toward achieving something.","c":"渴望；立志","s":"Barred from Russian-controlled universities in Warsaw because she was a woman, the young Marie Skłodowska had long aspired to study physics in Paris, working for years as a governess to fund her sister's medical degree before she could finally enroll at the Sorbonne herself.","t":"由於身為女性而被拒於俄國控制下的華沙大學門外，年輕的瑪麗．斯克沃多夫斯卡長久以來一直立志到巴黎攻讀物理；她當了好幾年家庭教師，資助姊姊完成醫學學位，之後才終於得以進入索邦大學就讀。","as":"Many young scientists aspire to make unprecedented discoveries, yet the most astute among them recognize that meticulous, often mundane laboratory work, rather than ostentatious claims, is what ultimately earns the esteem of their peers.","at":"許多年輕科學家渴望做出前所未有的發現，但其中最精明的人明白，最終贏得同儕敬重的，是一絲不苟、往往平凡乏味的實驗室工作，而非浮誇炫耀的宣稱。"},{"w":"accessible","p":"adj.","d":"Easy to reach, enter, use, or understand.","c":"易取得的；易接近的；易懂的","s":"By digitizing thousands of fragile medieval manuscripts and posting high-resolution images online free of charge, the national library made documents that had once been available only to credentialed scholars visiting its reading room accessible to students and amateur historians around the world.","t":"國家圖書館將數千份脆弱的中世紀手稿數位化，並免費在網路上公開高解析度影像，使這些過去只開放給親赴閱覽室、具備資格的學者查閱的文獻，如今全世界的學生和業餘歷史愛好者都能取得。","as":"Although the physicist's research was undeniably erudite, her popular book was remarkably accessible, replacing cryptic equations with lucid analogies and avoiding the pretentious jargon that makes so many scientific texts seem insipid to general readers.","at":"雖然這位物理學家的研究無疑十分博學精深，她的科普著作卻出奇地平易近人：以清晰的比喻取代晦澀難解的方程式，並避開許多科學文本中那種讓一般讀者覺得枯燥乏味的矯飾術語。"},{"w":"antidote","p":"n.","d":"A remedy that counteracts a poison or a harmful influence.","c":"解毒劑；矯正方法","s":"Because the venom of the inland taipan can kill an adult within hours, researchers at the Australian institute spent years immunizing horses with tiny doses so that the animals' blood would produce antibodies, which were then purified into an antidote for distribution to remote hospitals.","t":"由於內陸太攀蛇的毒液可在數小時內致成人於死，這所澳洲研究機構的研究人員花了多年時間，以極少劑量為馬匹進行免疫，讓馬的血液產生抗體，再將抗體純化製成解毒劑，分送至偏遠地區的醫院。","as":"Some educators argue that close reading of primary sources is the best antidote to the pernicious spread of online misinformation, because students who learn to be wary of unsupported claims become less susceptible to the hackneyed slogans and spurious statistics that circulate on social media.","at":"有些教育工作者認為，細讀第一手史料是對抗網路假訊息有害擴散的最佳解藥，因為學會對缺乏根據的說法保持警覺的學生，比較不容易受到社群媒體上流傳的陳腔濫調口號與虛假統計數據所影響。"},{"w":"autonomous","p":"adj.","d":"Self-governing; independent of outside control.","c":"自主的；自治的","s":"Under the 1979 home-rule agreement, Greenland became an autonomous territory within the Danish realm, gaining the authority to run its own schools, health system, and fisheries while the government in Copenhagen retained control over foreign policy and national defense.","t":"根據1979年的地方自治協議，格陵蘭成為丹麥王國內的自治領地，獲得自行管理學校、醫療體系與漁業的權力，而哥本哈根的中央政府則保留外交與國防的主導權。","as":"Engineers designing autonomous delivery robots must be meticulous about safety, since even a negligible software error could make a machine behave in volatile ways on crowded sidewalks, and regulators remain wary of approving them for public use.","at":"設計自動送貨機器人的工程師必須對安全性一絲不苟，因為即使是微不足道的軟體錯誤，也可能讓機器在擁擠的人行道上出現難以預測的行為，而主管機關對於核准這類機器人上路仍抱持戒慎態度。"},{"w":"gratify","p":"v.","d":"To give pleasure or satisfaction; to indulge a desire.","c":"使滿足；使高興","s":"Economists studying consumer behavior have found that people who can gratify their desires instantly through one-click online shopping often report less lasting satisfaction than those who must save for months, suggesting that anticipation itself contributes significantly to the pleasure of a purchase.","t":"研究消費行為的經濟學家發現，能透過一鍵網購立即滿足欲望的人，所感受到的滿足感往往不如必須存錢數月的人來得持久，這顯示期待本身就大大增添了購物的樂趣。","as":"Instead of seeking to gratify the egotistical demands of the temperamental diva, the conductor remained stoical, calmly insisting that every soloist, however acclaimed, follow the same rehearsal schedule as the rest of the orchestra.","at":"指揮並未設法滿足那位喜怒無常的女主角自我中心的要求，而是保持沉著，平靜地堅持每位獨奏者無論多麼備受讚譽，都必須和樂團其他成員遵守相同的排練時程。"},{"w":"candor","p":"n.","d":"Openness and honesty in expression; frankness.","c":"坦率；直率","s":"In her memoir, the former finance minister discussed her own policy mistakes with surprising candor, admitting that she had underestimated the risks of rapid deregulation and acknowledging that her optimistic public forecasts had sometimes contradicted the warnings her own advisers delivered privately.","t":"在回憶錄中，這位前財政部長以令人意外的坦率態度討論自己的政策失誤，承認她低估了快速解除管制的風險，也坦言她公開發表的樂觀預測，有時與她自己的顧問私下提出的警告相互矛盾。","as":"The new CEO's candor was a welcome change from the evasive circumlocution of her predecessor; rather than hiding behind platitudes, she admitted that the company's lackluster products had failed to keep pace with its more savvy competitors.","at":"新任執行長的坦率，與前任閃爍其詞、拐彎抹角的作風形成令人欣喜的對比；她沒有躲在空洞的陳腔濫調背後，而是坦承公司平庸乏味的產品已跟不上更精明的競爭對手。"},{"w":"fastidious","p":"adj.","d":"Very attentive to accuracy and detail; hard to please.","c":"挑剔的；講究的","s":"The novelist Gustave Flaubert was notoriously fastidious about language, sometimes spending an entire week revising a single paragraph of Madame Bovary because he refused to accept any word that was merely adequate rather than exactly right.","t":"小說家福樓拜對語言的講究是出了名的，有時會花上整整一星期修改《包法利夫人》中的一個段落，因為他不肯接受任何只是「堪用」而非「恰到好處」的字詞。","as":"The fastidious editor was meticulous about every comma, yet her scrupulous attention to detail never became captious; authors appreciated that she ignored trivial matters of taste and focused on errors that genuinely obscured meaning.","at":"這位講究的編輯對每個逗號都一絲不苟，但她對細節的嚴謹從未流於吹毛求疵；作者們很欣賞她略過無關緊要的品味問題，專注於真正使文意晦澀的錯誤。"},{"w":"abridge","p":"v.","d":"To shorten a text while keeping its essential content.","c":"刪節；縮短","s":"To fit the radio broadcast into a single evening, the producers abridged the nine-hundred-page novel to a ninety-minute script, cutting several minor subplots entirely while preserving the central courtroom scenes that critics regarded as the heart of the book.","t":"為了讓廣播劇能在一個晚上播完，製作人將這部九百頁的小說刪節成九十分鐘的劇本，完全刪去幾條次要情節，同時保留了評論家視為全書核心的法庭場景。","as":"Although the abridged edition was easier for young readers, scholars complained that its editors had excised the novel's most incisive passages, leaving a prosaic summary that reduced a nuanced satire to a series of trite moral lessons.","at":"雖然這個節本對年輕讀者來說較容易閱讀，學者卻抱怨編輯刪去了小說中最犀利的段落，只留下平淡無奇的摘要，把一部細膩的諷刺作品簡化成一連串陳腐的道德教訓。"},{"w":"bolster","p":"v.","d":"To support or strengthen something.","c":"支持；加強","s":"The discovery of nearly identical fossil plants in South America, Africa, India, and Antarctica bolstered Alfred Wegener's controversial theory of continental drift, since the plants' heavy seeds could not plausibly have crossed vast oceans unless the landmasses had once been joined.","t":"在南美洲、非洲、印度與南極洲發現幾乎相同的植物化石，強化了韋格納頗具爭議的大陸漂移學說，因為這些植物沉重的種子不可能橫渡遼闊的海洋，除非這些陸塊曾經相連。","as":"To bolster her case, the prosecutor presented copious financial records and the testimony of a scrupulous accountant, hoping that such ample evidence would refute the defense's claim that the discrepancies were merely inconsequential clerical errors.","at":"為了強化論點，檢察官提出大量財務紀錄，以及一位嚴謹會計師的證詞，希望藉由如此充分的證據，駁斥辯方所稱這些差異只是無關緊要的文書錯誤的說法。"},{"w":"cynical","p":"adj.","d":"Distrustful of others' motives; believing people act only selfishly.","c":"憤世嫉俗的；懷疑他人動機的","s":"After decades of watching politicians abandon their campaign promises within months of taking office, many voters in the survey had grown deeply cynical, assuming that every new reform proposal was merely a strategy to attract donations rather than a sincere attempt to improve public services.","t":"數十年來眼看政治人物在上任數月內就背棄競選承諾，調查中的許多選民已變得極為憤世嫉俗，認定每一項新的改革提案都只是吸引捐款的手段，而非真心想改善公共服務。","as":"The novelist's cynical narrator views every act of philanthropic generosity as a disguise for avarice, dismissing even the most altruistic characters as shrewd opportunists who merely seek public acclaim in a society he regards as hopelessly corrupt.","at":"這位小說家筆下憤世嫉俗的敘事者，把每一項慈善慷慨之舉都視為貪婪的偽裝，甚至將最無私的角色也貶為只想博取公眾讚揚的精明投機者；在他眼中，這個社會已經無可救藥地腐敗。"}]},{"unit":32,"theme":"Character and Growth","themeZh":"品格與成長","cards":[{"w":"intrepid","p":"adj.","d":"Fearless and adventurous, especially in the face of danger.","c":"無畏的；勇敢的","s":"In 1873, the intrepid travel writer Isabella Bird rode through the Rocky Mountains largely alone on horseback, enduring blizzards, grizzly bears, and nights in remote log cabins at a time when most of her contemporaries considered such journeys far too dangerous for any woman to attempt.","t":"1873年，無畏的旅行作家伊莎貝拉．博德幾乎獨自一人騎馬穿越洛磯山脈，熬過暴風雪、灰熊，以及在偏遠小木屋中度過的夜晚；而在當時，她同時代的大多數人都認為這種旅程對任何女性來說都太危險了。","as":"The intrepid journalist exposed a clandestine network of officials whose nefarious schemes had diverted relief funds, and she remained unwavering even when anonymous critics tried to intimidate her with threats.","at":"這位無畏的記者揭發了一個秘密的官員網絡，他們以邪惡的手法挪用救災款項；即使匿名批評者以威脅試圖恫嚇她，她仍毫不動搖。"},{"w":"opportunist","p":"n.","d":"A person who exploits circumstances for selfish gain, disregarding principles.","c":"投機者；機會主義者","s":"Historians have long debated whether the general was a principled patriot or merely an opportunist who switched sides three times during the civil war, each time aligning himself with whichever faction seemed most likely to reward him with land and political office.","t":"歷史學家長久以來爭論，這位將軍究竟是一位有原則的愛國者，還是只是一個投機者——他在內戰期間三度倒戈，每次都投靠看似最有可能以土地和官職回報他的派系。","as":"During the epidemic, a mercenary opportunist hoarded medical masks and resold them at exorbitant prices, and the public censured his avarice so fiercely that he became a pariah in his own community.","at":"疫情期間，一名唯利是圖的投機者囤積醫療口罩，再以天價轉售；大眾強烈譴責他的貪婪，使他在自己的社區裡成了人人唾棄的人。"},{"w":"homogeneous","p":"adj.","d":"Of the same kind; uniform in composition throughout.","c":"同質的；均勻的","s":"Because the glacier's ice had formed from snow that fell over thousands of years under varying climatic conditions, researchers were surprised to find that the core sample was almost entirely homogeneous, showing virtually no variation in its chemical composition from top to bottom.","t":"由於冰河的冰是由數千年來在不同氣候條件下降下的雪所形成，研究人員驚訝地發現，這段冰芯樣本幾乎完全均質，從頂端到底部的化學成分幾乎沒有任何變化。","as":"Critics argued that the festival's lineup had become dull and homogeneous, filled with derivative bands whose banal lyrics and hackneyed melodies made it hard to distinguish one act from another.","at":"評論家認為，這個音樂節的演出陣容已變得單調而同質化，充斥著模仿他人的樂團，那些平庸的歌詞和陳腐的旋律讓人難以分辨各組表演的差別。"},{"w":"nurture","p":"v.","d":"To care for and encourage the growth or development of.","c":"養育；培育","s":"Rather than demanding immediate profits, the venture fund nurtured its young biotechnology firms for nearly a decade, providing laboratory space, mentoring, and patient capital until their experimental therapies were finally ready for clinical trials.","t":"這家創投基金並未要求立即獲利，而是用了將近十年培育旗下年輕的生技公司，提供實驗室空間、輔導與耐心資本，直到它們的實驗性療法終於準備好進入臨床試驗。","as":"Good mentors nurture students' curiosity with ample encouragement, yet they remain conscientious enough to rebuke careless reasoning, knowing from long experience that unwavering standards, applied patiently and fairly over many years, ultimately produce more discerning and independent thinkers.","at":"優秀的導師以充分的鼓勵培育學生的好奇心，但也盡責地糾正粗率的推理，因為他們從長年經驗中明白，多年來耐心而公正地堅守毫不動搖的標準，最終能培養出更具洞察力、更能獨立思考的人。"},{"w":"proximity","p":"n.","d":"Nearness in space, time, or relationship.","c":"接近；鄰近","s":"Medieval Venice owed much of its commercial power to its proximity to both Byzantine and Islamic ports, which allowed its merchants to transport spices, silk, and glass between East and West far more quickly than rivals located farther inland.","t":"中世紀的威尼斯之所以擁有強大的商業實力，很大程度歸功於它鄰近拜占庭與伊斯蘭的港口，使其商人能夠在東西方之間運送香料、絲綢與玻璃，速度遠勝位於內陸較遠處的對手。","as":"The proximity of the chemical plant to the village alarmed residents, who feared that its acrid fumes might have deleterious effects on their health, and they found the company's indifferent response to their complaints especially odious.","at":"化工廠緊鄰村莊，讓居民憂心忡忡，擔心刺鼻的廢氣可能危害他們的健康；而公司對他們的抱怨漠不關心的回應，更讓他們深感可憎。"},{"w":"hamper","p":"v.","d":"To hinder or obstruct the progress of something.","c":"阻礙；妨礙","s":"Persistent sandstorms and failing solar panels severely hampered the Mars rover's exploration of the crater, forcing mission scientists to cancel several planned drilling operations and to spend weeks waiting for winds strong enough to clear dust from its instruments.","t":"持續的沙塵暴與故障的太陽能板嚴重阻礙了火星探測車對隕石坑的探勘，迫使任務科學家取消數項預定的鑽探作業，並花了好幾週等待強風將儀器上的灰塵吹散。","as":"Rescue efforts after the flood were badly hampered by turbulence in the swollen river, precarious debris from collapsed bridges, and contentious disputes between government agencies that refused to share boats, helicopters, and other essential equipment with one another.","at":"洪災後的救援行動，嚴重受到暴漲河水的湍急亂流、倒塌橋梁所留下岌岌可危的殘骸，以及各政府機關之間爭執不下、彼此拒絕共享船隻、直升機與其他必要設備的糾紛所阻礙。"},{"w":"hardy","p":"adj.","d":"Robust and able to endure difficult conditions.","c":"強健的；耐寒的；能吃苦的","s":"Tardigrades, microscopic animals barely half a millimeter long, are so hardy that they can survive being frozen near absolute zero, heated beyond the boiling point of water, and even exposed to the vacuum and radiation of outer space.","t":"水熊蟲是體長僅約半毫米的微小動物，生命力極為強韌，能在接近絕對零度的冰凍中、超過水沸點的高溫下存活，甚至能承受外太空的真空與輻射。","as":"Only hardy, austere settlers survived the arid frontier, where frugal habits were essential and adversity was so constant that many newcomers became disillusioned and abandoned their claims within a year.","at":"只有強健而刻苦的移居者才能在乾旱的邊疆存活下來；在那裡，節儉的習慣不可或缺，困境接連不斷，許多新來者在一年內就幻滅並放棄了他們的土地。"},{"w":"integrity","p":"n.","d":"Firm adherence to moral principles; honesty.","c":"正直；誠信；完整","s":"The auditor's integrity was widely praised after she refused a substantial bribe from company executives and instead reported the falsified earnings to regulators, even though her decision cost her a lucrative position and years of legal battles.","t":"這位審計員拒絕公司高層的大筆賄賂，轉而向主管機關舉報造假的盈餘，她的正直因而廣受讚揚，儘管這個決定讓她失去了一份待遇優渥的職位，並陷入多年的法律纏訟。","as":"Voters admired the senator's integrity because she refused to placate wealthy donors, censured corrupt colleagues, and remained scrupulous about disclosing every gift, never allowing a devious lobbyist to sway her vote.","at":"選民欽佩這位參議員的正直，因為她拒絕討好富有的捐款人、譴責貪腐的同僚，並且一絲不苟地申報每一份餽贈，從不讓狡詐的說客左右她的投票。"},{"w":"linger","p":"v.","d":"To remain or persist longer than expected.","c":"逗留；徘徊；揮之不去","s":"Long after the factory closed in the 1970s, toxic solvents continued to linger in the groundwater beneath the neighborhood, and environmental engineers estimated that complete cleanup of the contaminated aquifer would require at least another thirty years.","t":"這座工廠在1970年代關閉許久之後，有毒溶劑仍持續殘留在社區地底的地下水中，環境工程師估計，要完全清除受汙染的含水層，至少還需要三十年。","as":"Although the actual fire was fleeting, its consequences lingered for decades: the conflagration had reduced the archive to a single charred relic, and historians still regret the obscure manuscripts lost forever.","at":"雖然這場火災本身轉瞬即逝，影響卻延續了數十年：大火將檔案館燒得只剩下一件焦黑的遺物，歷史學家至今仍惋惜那些永遠失傳、鮮為人知的手稿。"},{"w":"lofty","p":"adj.","d":"Of imposing height; noble or elevated in character.","c":"崇高的；高聳的","s":"The founders of the new university articulated lofty ideals in their charter, promising to admit students regardless of wealth or religion and to pursue knowledge for the benefit of all humanity, though limited funding soon forced them to compromise on several of these goals.","t":"這所新大學的創辦人在章程中闡述了崇高的理想，承諾不論貧富或宗教皆招收學生，並為全人類的福祉追求知識；然而，有限的經費很快迫使他們在其中幾項目標上妥協。","as":"The charity's lofty mission statement was replete with grandiloquent promises to end hunger within a decade, but skeptics noted a glaring discrepancy between this soaring rhetoric and the organization's frugal spending on the actual food programs it claimed to support.","at":"這個慈善機構的崇高使命宣言滿是要在十年內終結飢餓的浮誇承諾，但懷疑論者指出，這番高調言辭與該組織在其宣稱支持的實際糧食計畫上吝嗇的支出之間，存在明顯的落差。"},{"w":"mock","p":"v.","d":"To ridicule someone or something, often by imitation.","c":"嘲笑；模仿取笑","s":"When Ignaz Semmelweis argued in the 1840s that doctors should wash their hands between patients to prevent fatal infections, many prominent physicians openly mocked his theory, dismissing as absurd the suggestion that their own hands could transmit disease.","t":"1840年代，塞麥爾維斯主張醫師在診治不同病患之間應洗手以預防致命感染，許多知名醫師卻公開嘲笑他的理論，認為「自己的雙手可能傳播疾病」這種說法荒謬至極。","as":"The satirist mocked the haughty aristocrats in his plays, exposing their pretentious manners and supercilious attitudes so incisively that his work offended the very audiences who flocked to see it.","at":"這位諷刺作家在劇作中嘲弄傲慢的貴族，如此犀利地揭露他們矯揉造作的舉止與目中無人的態度，以至於他的作品冒犯了那些蜂擁而來觀賞的觀眾。"}]},{"unit":33,"theme":"Judgment and Temperament","themeZh":"評斷與性情","cards":[{"w":"recount","p":"v.","d":"To tell or narrate events in detail.","c":"敘述；詳述","s":"In oral-history interviews conducted decades after the war, former factory workers recounted how they had built aircraft parts during twelve-hour night shifts, providing historians with vivid details about daily wartime labor that official government records had largely ignored.","t":"在戰後數十年進行的口述歷史訪談中，昔日的工廠工人詳述他們如何在十二小時的夜班中製造飛機零件，為歷史學家提供了政府官方紀錄大多忽略的戰時日常勞動生動細節。","as":"The memoir recounts the author's peripatetic childhood with remarkable candor, describing how her nomadic family endured adversity in a series of austere mining towns across the Andes, where her father searched for work and her mother taught the children to read by candlelight.","at":"這本回憶錄以驚人的坦率敘述作者四處漂泊的童年，描寫她那居無定所的家庭如何在安地斯山區一連串簡陋清苦的礦業小鎮中熬過重重困境；父親在那裡四處找工作，母親則在燭光下教孩子們識字。"},{"w":"surpass","p":"v.","d":"To exceed or go beyond in quality or amount.","c":"超越；勝過","s":"By 2010, China's economy had surpassed Japan's to become the second largest in the world, an achievement that economists attributed to three decades of rapid industrialization, massive infrastructure investment, and an export sector that supplied manufactured goods to nearly every global market.","t":"到了2010年，中國經濟已超越日本，成為全球第二大經濟體；經濟學家將這項成就歸功於三十年的快速工業化、大規模的基礎建設投資，以及供應製造品給幾乎所有全球市場的出口產業。","as":"The young virtuoso's audacious interpretation of the concerto surpassed even the most lofty expectations, and critics who had dismissed her as a mere novelty began to extol her ingenious phrasing.","at":"這位年輕演奏名家對協奏曲大膽的詮釋，甚至超越了最崇高的期待；那些曾把她視為一時新奇的評論家，也開始盛讚她巧妙的樂句處理。"},{"w":"saturate","p":"v.","d":"To soak thoroughly or fill completely.","c":"浸透；使飽和","s":"Within a few years of the smartphone's introduction, competing manufacturers had so thoroughly saturated the market with nearly identical models that analysts warned profits would soon decline as companies were forced to cut prices simply to attract customers.","t":"智慧型手機問世後短短幾年內，競爭廠商就以幾乎一模一樣的機型讓市場達到飽和，分析師警告，由於企業被迫降價才能吸引顧客，獲利很快就會下滑。","as":"During the final weeks of the campaign, advertisements saturated the airwaves with vapid slogans and trite platitudes, leaving many voters so apathetic that they ignored even the few incisive debates that addressed real issues such as housing costs and public health.","at":"在選戰最後幾週，廣告以空洞的口號與陳腐的老生常談充斥電波，讓許多選民變得冷漠麻木，甚至忽略了少數真正探討住房成本與公共衛生等實際議題、犀利深入的辯論。"},{"w":"scrutinize","p":"v.","d":"To examine closely and critically.","c":"仔細檢查；詳細審查","s":"Before awarding the prize, the committee scrutinized the physicist's raw data for nearly a year, recalculating each measurement and consulting independent experts, because an earlier claim of a similar discovery had collapsed after other laboratories failed to replicate the results.","t":"在頒獎之前，委員會花了將近一年仔細審查這位物理學家的原始數據，重新計算每一項測量並諮詢獨立專家，因為先前一項類似發現的宣稱，在其他實驗室無法重現結果後便宣告瓦解。","as":"Investors who scrutinized the company's reports found a troubling discrepancy between its ostentatious claims and its actual revenue, and the more astute among them sold their shares before the debacle.","at":"仔細檢視這家公司財報的投資人發現，其浮誇的宣稱與實際營收之間存在令人不安的落差，其中較精明的人在這場慘敗發生前就賣出了持股。"},{"w":"whimsical","p":"adj.","d":"Playfully quaint or fanciful, often in an amusing way.","c":"異想天開的；奇趣的；古怪的","s":"Antoni Gaudí's Park Güell in Barcelona is famous for its whimsical architecture, featuring gingerbread-like gatehouses, a winding bench covered in colorful broken tiles, and a giant mosaic lizard that seems to belong more to a fairy tale than to a public garden.","t":"高第在巴塞隆納設計的奎爾公園，以充滿奇趣的建築聞名：宛如薑餅屋的門房、鋪滿彩色碎瓷磚的蜿蜒長椅，以及一隻巨大的馬賽克蜥蜴，看起來更像屬於童話故事，而不是公共花園。","as":"Unlike the ponderous, hackneyed fantasy novels that dominated the market at the time, her whimsical stories delighted readers of all ages with jocular dialogue and eccentric characters, offering a welcome levity that never became trivial or condescending toward young audiences.","at":"不同於當時充斥市場、冗長沉悶又陳腔濫調的奇幻小說，她那些異想天開的故事以詼諧的對話和古怪的角色取悅各年齡層的讀者，帶來令人歡迎的輕鬆幽默，卻從不流於膚淺，也不對年輕讀者居高臨下。"},{"w":"vilify","p":"v.","d":"To speak or write about someone in an abusively disparaging way.","c":"誹謗；詆毀","s":"During the 1950s, newspapers and congressional committees began to vilify several Hollywood screenwriters as dangerous traitors, even though investigators produced little credible evidence, and many of the accused were unable to work in the film industry for more than a decade.","t":"1950年代，報紙與國會委員會開始把數名好萊塢編劇詆毀為危險的叛國者，儘管調查人員幾乎提不出可信的證據，許多被控者仍有十多年無法在電影業工作。","as":"Rather than engaging her carefully documented arguments, the senator's malicious allies vilified the whistle-blower in a series of rancorous editorials, impugning her motives, questioning her loyalty, and spreading spurious rumors about her personal finances and her past employment.","at":"這位參議員心懷惡意的盟友並未正面回應她那些證據充分的論點，而是在一連串充滿敵意的社論中詆毀這名吹哨者，質疑她的動機與忠誠，並散播關於她個人財務與過去工作經歷的不實謠言。"},{"w":"querulous","p":"adj.","d":"Habitually complaining in a whining or petulant manner.","c":"愛抱怨的；發牢騷的","s":"The letters of the aging composer reveal an increasingly querulous man who grumbled endlessly about drafty apartments, incompetent copyists, and ungrateful publishers, a striking contrast to the serene, joyful music he continued to write during the same years.","t":"這位年邁作曲家的書信顯示，他變得越來越愛發牢騷，無止盡地抱怨漏風的公寓、無能的抄譜員與忘恩負義的出版商，與他同一時期仍持續創作的那些寧靜而歡愉的音樂形成鮮明對比。","as":"The querulous restaurant critic complained about every trivial detail of the meal, from the temperature of the plates to the font on the menu, berating waiters over petty issues and dismissing even the chef's most delectable dishes as insipid.","at":"這位愛抱怨的美食評論家對餐點的每個微不足道的細節都有怨言，從餐盤的溫度到菜單上的字體無一倖免；他為了雞毛蒜皮的小事痛罵服務生，甚至把主廚最美味的菜餚也貶為索然無味。"},{"w":"rigor","p":"n.","d":"Strict precision and thoroughness; also harshness or severity.","c":"嚴謹；嚴格；嚴酷","s":"Reviewers praised the economist's study for its methodological rigor: she tracked more than ten thousand households over twenty years, controlled carefully for income and education, and published her complete data set so that other researchers could test her conclusions independently.","t":"審查者稱讚這位經濟學家的研究在方法上極為嚴謹：她追蹤一萬多個家庭長達二十年，審慎控制收入與教育等變因，並公開完整的資料集，讓其他研究者能獨立檢驗她的結論。","as":"The medical journal is known for its rigor: its exacting reviewers demand meticulous methodology, insist that authors share their raw data, and routinely refuse to accept studies whose conclusions rest on ambiguous measurements or a negligible number of participants.","at":"這份醫學期刊以嚴謹著稱：嚴格的審查者要求一絲不苟的研究方法，堅持作者公開原始數據，並經常拒絕接受結論建立在模稜兩可的測量或微不足道的受試人數上的研究。"},{"w":"tentative","p":"adj.","d":"Not certain or fixed; hesitant or provisional.","c":"試探性的；暫定的；猶豫的","s":"After months of negotiations, the two nations announced a tentative agreement to share water from the river, but officials cautioned that the terms still required approval from both parliaments and could change significantly if new drought forecasts proved accurate.","t":"經過數月談判，兩國宣布了一項分享河水的暫定協議，但官員提醒，協議條款仍須經兩國國會批准，而且若新的乾旱預測屬實，內容可能大幅變動。","as":"Confronted with the enigma of the star's irregular dimming, the astronomer offered only a tentative explanation, acknowledging that the data were ambiguous and that a more prudent conclusion would require several more years of careful observation from multiple telescopes.","at":"面對這顆恆星不規則變暗的謎團，這位天文學家只提出試探性的解釋，並承認數據模稜兩可，要得出較審慎的結論，還需要以多座望遠鏡再仔細觀測好幾年。"},{"w":"thrive","p":"v.","d":"To grow vigorously; to flourish or prosper.","c":"茁壯成長；興旺","s":"Although most coral species are dying as ocean temperatures rise, researchers discovered several reefs in the Red Sea that continue to thrive in unusually warm water, raising hopes that their heat-resistant genes might help scientists restore damaged reefs elsewhere.","t":"雖然大多數珊瑚物種隨著海水溫度上升而逐漸死亡，研究人員卻在紅海發現數個珊瑚礁，在異常溫暖的海水中仍持續茁壯生長，這讓人期待其耐熱基因或許能幫助科學家復育其他地方受損的珊瑚礁。","as":"Some hardy desert species thrive in arid regions by being remarkably frugal with water, storing moisture in thick stems or roots, and their ingenious adaptations allow them to endure a level of adversity that would quickly kill more delicate plants.","at":"有些強健的沙漠物種在乾旱地區蓬勃生長，靠的是極度節約用水，將水分儲存在粗厚的莖或根中；它們巧妙的適應方式，讓它們能熬過足以迅速殺死較嬌弱植物的逆境。"},{"w":"tranquility","p":"n.","d":"A state of peace, quiet, and calm.","c":"平靜；寧靜","s":"Japanese Zen gardens were designed to promote tranquility, using carefully raked gravel, a few moss-covered stones, and the absence of bright flowers to quiet the mind and help visiting monks concentrate during long hours of meditation.","t":"日本的禪意庭園旨在營造寧靜，運用細心耙出紋路的砂石、幾塊覆滿青苔的石頭，以及刻意不用鮮豔花朵的設計，來沉澱心靈，幫助來訪的僧侶在漫長的冥想時間中專注。","as":"Seeking tranquility after the turmoil of the lengthy trial, the exhausted lawyer retreated to a remote mountain cabin without internet access, where the gentle euphony of birdsong and flowing water gradually replaced the cacophony of the city in her memory.","at":"在冗長審判的混亂紛擾之後，筋疲力盡的律師為了尋求平靜，退隱到一間沒有網路的偏遠山間小屋；在那裡，鳥鳴與流水輕柔悅耳的和聲，逐漸取代了她記憶中城市的嘈雜喧囂。"},{"w":"uniformity","p":"n.","d":"The quality of being the same throughout; lack of variation.","c":"一致性；均一","s":"Critics of the national curriculum argued that its emphasis on uniformity — requiring every school to teach the same textbooks in the same sequence on the same schedule — left teachers little freedom to adapt lessons to the interests and needs of their particular students.","t":"國家課綱的批評者認為，課綱過度強調一致性——要求每所學校依相同進度、相同順序教授相同的課本——讓教師幾乎沒有空間依照自己學生的興趣與需求調整課程。","as":"Critics of suburban sprawl lament the dreary uniformity of its identical houses and shopping centers, arguing that such mundane, derivative architecture reflects a complacent culture that prizes conformity and convenience over innovation, history, and a genuine sense of place.","at":"郊區擴張的批評者感嘆那些一模一樣的房屋與購物中心單調一致，認為這種平凡無奇、缺乏原創性的建築，反映出一種自滿的文化——重視從眾與便利，勝過創新、歷史與真正的地方感。"}]},{"unit":34,"theme":"Evidence and Variety","themeZh":"證據與多元","cards":[{"w":"aggregate","p":"n.","d":"A whole formed by combining several separate elements.","c":"總和；總計；集合體","s":"Although no single household's carbon emissions seem significant, climate economists emphasize that the aggregate of millions of small daily choices — commuting by car, heating poorly insulated homes, and discarding food — accounts for a substantial share of a nation's total greenhouse gases.","t":"雖然單一家庭的碳排放看似微不足道，氣候經濟學家強調，數百萬個日常小選擇的總和——開車通勤、為隔熱不良的房屋供暖、丟棄食物——占了一個國家溫室氣體總排放量的相當大比例。","as":"Individually, each donation seemed negligible, but the aggregate of thousands of small gifts amounted to a munificent sum, proving that the town's frugal residents could be remarkably altruistic when a neighbor faced adversity.","at":"單獨來看，每一筆捐款似乎都微不足道，但數千筆小額捐款的總和卻是一筆慷慨可觀的金額，證明這個小鎮節儉的居民在鄰居遭逢困境時，也能展現非凡的無私精神。"},{"w":"complementary","p":"adj.","d":"Combining to complete or enhance each other.","c":"互補的；相輔相成的","s":"The partnership between the two founders succeeded because their talents were complementary: one was a brilliant engineer who could design efficient batteries but disliked public speaking, while the other was a persuasive negotiator who understood investors yet knew little about chemistry.","t":"兩位創辦人的合作之所以成功，是因為他們的才能互補：一位是能設計高效電池、卻不喜歡公開演講的傑出工程師；另一位則是懂得投資人心理、卻對化學所知甚少的說服力十足的談判高手。","as":"The museum's curators believe that ancient artifacts and contemporary art can be complementary, so the eclectic exhibition pairs a weathered relic from antiquity with an innovative sculpture, inviting visitors to discern unexpected connections.","at":"博物館策展人相信古代文物與當代藝術能夠相輔相成，因此這場兼容並蓄的展覽將一件來自古代、飽經風霜的遺物與一件創新的雕塑並置，邀請觀眾察覺意想不到的關聯。"},{"w":"debunk","p":"v.","d":"To expose a claim or belief as false.","c":"揭穿；駁斥","s":"Through a series of careful experiments with swan-necked flasks of broth, Louis Pasteur debunked the ancient theory of spontaneous generation, demonstrating that microorganisms arose from other living microbes carried in the air rather than from nonliving matter itself.","t":"巴斯德透過一系列以鵝頸燒瓶盛裝肉湯的嚴謹實驗，揭穿了古老的自然發生說，證明微生物是由空氣中所攜帶的其他活微生物產生，而非由無生命的物質本身生成。","as":"The skeptic devoted her entire career to debunking charlatans who claimed psychic powers, scrutinizing their spurious claims with meticulous controlled experiments and exposing the cynical tricks they used to deceive gullible audiences and extract money from grieving families.","at":"這位懷疑論者畢生致力於揭穿那些自稱擁有超能力的江湖騙子，以一絲不苟的對照實驗仔細檢驗他們虛假的宣稱，並揭露他們用來欺騙輕信觀眾、向悲傷家屬騙取錢財的那些冷血伎倆。"},{"w":"discrepancy","p":"n.","d":"A lack of agreement between facts that should match.","c":"差異；不一致","s":"Auditors became suspicious when they noticed a discrepancy of nearly two million dollars between the hospital's reported equipment purchases and the actual inventory in its storerooms, prompting a federal investigation that eventually uncovered an elaborate kickback scheme.","t":"審計人員注意到，醫院申報的設備採購金額與倉庫中的實際庫存之間有將近兩百萬美元的差異，因而起了疑心，並促使聯邦展開調查，最終揭發了一套精心策劃的回扣陰謀。","as":"The astute reporter noticed a glaring discrepancy between the senator's frugal public image and his lavish private spending on yachts and vacation homes, and her incisive article ultimately debunked the reputation for integrity that he had so carefully cultivated for decades.","at":"精明的記者注意到，這位參議員節儉的公眾形象與他私下在遊艇和度假別墅上的揮霍開銷之間有明顯的落差，而她犀利的報導最終揭穿了他數十年來精心經營的正直聲譽。"},{"w":"excerpt","p":"n.","d":"A short passage taken from a longer text or work.","c":"摘錄；節錄","s":"On the Digital SAT, each reading question is paired with a brief excerpt of only a few sentences, drawn from novels, scientific journals, or historical speeches, so test takers must interpret the author's argument without the surrounding context a full text would provide.","t":"在數位SAT考試中，每道閱讀題都搭配一段只有幾句話的簡短節錄，選自小說、科學期刊或歷史演說，因此考生必須在缺乏完整文本上下文的情況下解讀作者的論點。","as":"The teacher chose an excerpt from the novel replete with archaic vocabulary and subtle allusions, hoping her erudite students would appreciate its ambiguous imagery rather than dismiss it as obscure.","at":"老師從這部小說中選了一段充滿古雅詞彙與微妙典故的節錄，希望她那些博學的學生能欣賞其意蘊含糊的意象，而不是把它斥為晦澀難懂。"},{"w":"audacious","p":"adj.","d":"Showing a willingness to take bold, daring risks.","c":"大膽的；無畏的","s":"The Apollo program's goal of landing astronauts on the Moon within a decade was remarkably audacious, since at the time of President Kennedy's 1961 announcement, the United States had sent only a single astronaut on a brief suborbital flight lasting fifteen minutes.","t":"阿波羅計畫要在十年內讓太空人登陸月球的目標極為大膽，因為甘迺迪總統在1961年宣布這項計畫時，美國只送過一名太空人進行為時十五分鐘的短暫次軌道飛行。","as":"The audacious young architect proposed an unprecedented design for the waterfront that many critics called imprudent and impractical, yet her innovative tower ultimately surpassed every rival plan in the competition and was later acclaimed as a triumph of modern engineering.","at":"這位大膽的年輕建築師為濱水區提出了前所未有的設計，許多評論家斥之為輕率又不切實際，但她創新的高塔最終在競圖中勝過所有對手的方案，後來更被譽為現代工程學的勝利。"},{"w":"eclectic","p":"adj.","d":"Drawing ideas or styles from a broad range of sources.","c":"兼容並蓄的；多元的","s":"The architect's eclectic style combined Gothic arches, traditional Japanese timber joinery, and sleek modern glass walls in a single building, and although some critics found the mixture confusing, many visitors admired the way it reflected the city's diverse cultural history.","t":"這位建築師兼容並蓄的風格，在同一棟建築中結合了哥德式拱門、傳統日式木作榫接，以及簡潔的現代玻璃牆；雖然有些評論家覺得這種混搭令人困惑，許多參觀者卻欣賞它反映出這座城市多元文化歷史的方式。","as":"The chef's eclectic menu blends culinary traditions from five continents, pairing Peruvian ceviche with Korean kimchi and Ethiopian spices, and even the most discerning epicurean diners find her savory fusion dishes delectable rather than pretentious or merely fashionable.","at":"這位主廚兼容並蓄的菜單融合了五大洲的烹飪傳統，將祕魯檸汁醃魚與韓國泡菜、衣索比亞香料搭配在一起，就連最挑剔的美食家也認為她那些鹹香的融合料理美味可口，而非矯揉造作或只是趕流行。"},{"w":"aviary","p":"n.","d":"A large enclosure or building for keeping birds.","c":"鳥舍；鳥園","s":"To protect the critically endangered Hawaiian crow, which had disappeared from the wild by 2002, conservationists raised the remaining birds in a mountain aviary that imitated their native forest, complete with native fruit trees, misty humidity, and protection from invasive predators.","t":"為了保護在2002年已於野外絕跡、極度瀕危的夏威夷烏鴉，保育人員將剩下的鳥飼養在一座模擬其原生森林的山區鳥舍中，裡面有原生果樹、霧氣般的濕度，並能防範外來掠食者。","as":"The vast glass aviary at the botanical garden offers city workers a welcome respite from the cacophony of traffic and construction, and many visitors linger for hours among exotic birds whose mellifluous songs blend into a soothing euphony.","at":"植物園中寬廣的玻璃鳥園，讓城市上班族得以暫時遠離車流與工地的嘈雜喧囂，許多遊客在珍奇鳥類之間流連數小時，牠們悅耳的歌聲交融成令人放鬆的和諧樂音。"},{"w":"glacial","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely slow, like a glacier; also icy cold.","c":"極緩慢的；冰冷的；冰河的","s":"Reform of the nation's patent system proceeded at a glacial pace, with proposed legislation stalling in committee year after year, so that by the time the law was finally passed, many of the technologies it was meant to regulate had already become obsolete.","t":"這個國家的專利制度改革進展極其緩慢，提出的法案年復一年卡在委員會中，以至於等到法律終於通過時，許多原本要規範的技術早已過時。","as":"Progress on the new bridge was glacial: sluggish bureaucrats, contentious lawsuits filed by neighboring towns, and a myriad of permit delays left the project stagnant for nearly a decade, until frustrated commuters finally organized protests demanding immediate action.","at":"新橋的工程進度極其緩慢：拖拖拉拉的官僚、鄰近城鎮提起的爭議訴訟，以及無數的許可延宕，讓計畫停滯了將近十年，直到不滿的通勤族終於組織抗議，要求立即採取行動。"}]},{"unit":35,"theme":"Obstacles and Deception","themeZh":"阻礙與虛假","cards":[{"w":"insuperable","p":"adj.","d":"Impossible to overcome or surmount.","c":"難以克服的；不可逾越的","s":"For centuries, engineers regarded the Isthmus of Panama as an insuperable barrier to a canal: French attempts in the 1880s collapsed after mudslides, financial scandal, and yellow fever killed more than twenty thousand workers before the excavation was even half complete.","t":"幾個世紀以來，工程師都把巴拿馬地峽視為開鑿運河難以克服的障礙：1880年代法國的嘗試，在土石流、金融醜聞與黃熱病奪走兩萬多名工人性命之後宣告失敗，當時開挖工程甚至還不到一半。","as":"For decades the granite ridge seemed an insuperable obstacle to the railway, but a dogged, unwavering team of engineers eventually devised an ingenious method to tunnel safely beneath the precarious mountain without triggering the landslides that had doomed earlier attempts.","at":"數十年來，這道花崗岩山脊似乎是興建鐵路無法克服的障礙，但一群堅持不懈、毫不動搖的工程師最終設計出一種巧妙的方法，安全地從岌岌可危的山體下方開鑿隧道，而不會引發先前導致嘗試失敗的山崩。"},{"w":"replete","p":"adj.","d":"Filled or well supplied with something.","c":"充滿的；充足的","s":"Charles Darwin's notebooks from the voyage of the Beagle are replete with detailed sketches of finches, barnacles, and fossilized bones, along with tentative questions in the margins that reveal how his ideas about the variation of species gradually developed.","t":"達爾文乘坐小獵犬號航行時的筆記本中，滿是雀鳥、藤壺與骨骼化石的詳細素描，頁邊還有一些試探性的疑問，顯示他對物種變異的想法是如何逐步發展的。","as":"The candidate's victory speech was replete with hackneyed platitudes and grandiloquent promises about a brighter future, but the more discerning listeners noticed that it offered no specific plan for addressing the economic turmoil that had driven so many families from the city.","at":"這位候選人的勝選演說充斥著陳腔濫調和有關光明未來的浮誇承諾，但較有眼光的聽眾注意到，演說中並未提出任何具體方案，來解決那場迫使許多家庭離開這座城市的經濟混亂。"},{"w":"respite","p":"n.","d":"A short period of rest or relief from difficulty.","c":"喘息；暫緩；短暫休息","s":"For the exhausted doctors working through the city's worst influenza season in decades, the brief respite provided by a volunteer medical team from a neighboring province allowed them to sleep for the first time in days before the next wave of patients arrived.","t":"對於在這座城市數十年來最嚴重的流感季中疲於奔命的醫師而言，鄰省志工醫療團隊帶來的短暫喘息，讓他們在下一波病患湧入之前，得以在數天以來首次好好睡上一覺。","as":"The brief truce offered the besieged city only a fleeting respite from the turmoil of war, and residents knew that the volatile peace could collapse into another conflagration at any moment.","at":"短暫的停火只讓被圍困的城市從戰爭的混亂中獲得片刻喘息，居民們都知道，這種動盪不穩的和平隨時可能再度演變成一場大火般的戰禍。"},{"w":"raze","p":"v.","d":"To completely destroy or level a building or town.","c":"夷為平地；徹底摧毀","s":"After defeating Carthage in 146 BCE, Roman forces razed the city so thoroughly that archaeologists today struggle to identify more than a few scattered foundations, although the later legend that the Romans also salted the earth has no basis in ancient sources.","t":"西元前146年擊敗迦太基之後，羅馬軍隊將這座城市徹底夷為平地，以至於今日的考古學家只能辨識出少數零散的地基；不過，後世所謂羅馬人還在土地上撒鹽的傳說，在古代文獻中並無根據。","as":"When developers announced plans to raze the historic market, indignant residents, outraged by the plan's callous disregard for their heritage, launched a vociferous campaign of petitions and public hearings that bolstered support for preserving the century-old building.","at":"當開發商宣布計畫拆除這座歷史悠久的市場時，憤慨的居民對該計畫冷酷無視他們的文化遺產深感憤怒，發起了一場透過請願與公聽會進行、聲勢浩大的運動，強化了民眾對保存這棟百年建築的支持。"},{"w":"lithe","p":"adj.","d":"Flexible, supple, and graceful in movement.","c":"柔軟的；輕盈的；敏捷的","s":"Snow leopards are remarkably lithe predators, able to twist their long, muscular bodies in midair while leaping across rocky ravines and using their thick tails for balance on cliffs so steep that few other mammals can follow them.","t":"雪豹是身手極為矯健柔軟的掠食者，能在躍過岩石峽谷時於半空中扭轉修長而結實的身軀，並在陡峭到少有其他哺乳動物能跟上的懸崖上，利用粗厚的尾巴保持平衡。","as":"Unlike the sluggish, sedentary courtiers who populate the rest of the play, the lithe acrobat cast as the trickster brought a vibrant, effervescent energy to the stage, and audiences acclaimed her tumbling performance as the highlight of the entire production.","at":"不同於劇中其他那些行動遲緩、久坐不動的朝臣，飾演搗蛋鬼的身段輕盈的雜技演員為舞臺帶來充滿活力、熱情洋溢的能量，觀眾盛讚她的翻滾表演是整齣戲的最大亮點。"},{"w":"spurious","p":"adj.","d":"False or fake, though appearing genuine.","c":"虛假的；偽造的；謬誤的","s":"Statisticians warn that analyzing huge data sets without a clear hypothesis can produce spurious correlations, such as the widely shared chart showing that national cheese consumption tracked closely with deaths from tangled bedsheets, even though neither trend could plausibly cause the other.","t":"統計學家警告，在沒有明確假說的情況下分析龐大的資料集，可能產生虛假的相關性，例如那張廣為流傳的圖表顯示全國起司消費量與被床單纏繞致死的人數密切相關，儘管兩者都不可能是對方的成因。","as":"The charlatan's spurious cure for arthritis was promoted with ostentatious advertisements and fabricated testimonials, but skeptical scientists debunked his claims in a controlled trial, revealing that his nefarious scheme preyed chiefly on desperate, indigent patients who could least afford it.","at":"這名江湖郎中號稱能治療關節炎的假藥，以浮誇的廣告和捏造的見證大肆宣傳，但抱持懷疑態度的科學家在對照試驗中揭穿了他的說法，揭露他那邪惡的詐騙手法主要剝削的是最負擔不起的、走投無路的貧困病患。"},{"w":"misanthrope","p":"n.","d":"A person who dislikes and avoids humankind.","c":"厭世者；憎惡人類的人","s":"Literary critics often describe Alceste, the title character of Molière's 1666 comedy, as a misanthrope who despises the flattery and hypocrisy of Parisian society so intensely that he ultimately resolves to abandon civilization altogether and live in solitude.","t":"文學評論家常把莫里哀1666年喜劇的主角阿爾賽斯特形容為一個厭世者，他對巴黎上流社會的阿諛與虛偽深惡痛絕，最終決定完全拋棄文明、離群索居。","as":"The reclusive poet was often dismissed by critics as a cynical misanthrope, yet her recently published letters reveal an affable, magnanimous woman who quietly supported struggling young writers, and whose aloof public manner merely concealed a lifelong and painful shyness.","at":"這位離群索居的詩人常被評論家貶為憤世嫉俗的厭世者，但她最近出版的書信顯示，她是一位和藹可親、寬宏大量的女性，曾默默資助困頓的年輕作家；她在公開場合冷淡疏離的態度，只不過是掩飾她終生為之所苦的害羞。"},{"w":"pitfall","p":"n.","d":"A hidden or unsuspected danger or difficulty.","c":"陷阱；隱患","s":"One common pitfall in historical research is presentism, the tendency to judge people of earlier centuries entirely by modern moral standards, which can prevent scholars from understanding why past societies made the decisions they did.","t":"歷史研究中一個常見的陷阱是「現今主義」，也就是完全以現代道德標準評斷過去幾世紀的人，這可能使學者無法理解過去的社會為何做出那些決定。","as":"The financial adviser warned that the most common pitfall for novice investors is not excessive caution but complacent overconfidence after a few early gains, which often leads them to abandon prudent diversification and make imprudent bets on volatile technology stocks.","at":"這位理財顧問警告，新手投資人最常見的陷阱並非過度謹慎，而是在幾次初期獲利後產生的自滿與過度自信，這往往使他們放棄審慎的分散投資，輕率地押注在波動劇烈的科技股上。"},{"w":"vaporize","p":"v.","d":"To turn into vapor; to disappear suddenly and completely.","c":"使蒸發；使汽化；消失","s":"In mass spectrometry, scientists first vaporize a tiny sample of the substance being studied, converting it into a gas whose charged particles can then be sorted by mass, allowing researchers to identify even trace amounts of a chemical compound.","t":"在質譜分析中，科學家會先將所研究物質的極少量樣本汽化，使其轉變為氣體，其中帶電的粒子接著可依質量加以分類，讓研究人員即使是微量的化合物也能辨識出來。","as":"The company's lofty profits seemed to vaporize overnight once auditors exposed its spurious accounting practices, and the ensuing debacle left once-complacent shareholders indignant at the charismatic executives whom they had foolishly esteemed as visionary leaders.","at":"一旦審計人員揭發這家公司造假的會計手法，其原本高得驚人的利潤彷彿一夜之間蒸發殆盡；隨之而來的慘敗，讓曾經自滿的股東們對那些他們曾愚蠢地敬重為遠見領袖、魅力十足的高層主管憤慨不已。"}]}];
